    ", 4);\n        Vec<i32> b = Vec::clone(&a);\n        assert(Vec::remove(&mut a, 0) == 1);\n        asse"
    "rt(a[0] == 2 && a[1] == 3 && a[2] == 4);\n        assert(Vec::swap_remove(&mut b, 0) == 1);\n        a"
    "ssert(b[0] == 4 && b[1] == 2 && b[2] == 3);\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::collections\u{1f}Vec::clone\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Vec::clone<T:"
    " clone>(ref<Vec<T>, shared> v) : Vec<T>\u{1f}A new `Vec` holding a copy of each element of `v`, in order."
    "\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Vec::clone<T: clone>(ref<Vec<T>, shared> v) : Vec<T>\n    in `std::collections`\n\n    A ne"
    "w `Vec` holding a copy of each element of `v`, in order.\n\n    `T` must be `clone` (owning nothing); "
