    "PriorityQueue\u{1f}struct\u{1f}export struct PriorityQueue<T>\u{1f}A priority queue: it gives its elements back lea"
    "st first, in an order fixed when it is made.\u{1f}\u{1f}export struct PriorityQueue<T>\n    in `std::collection"
    "s`\n\n    A priority queue: it gives its elements back least first, in an order fixed when it is made."
    "\n\n    `PriorityQueue::new` uses the key types' own order, `PriorityQueue::new_by` the caller's `less"
    "`.\n    Elements the order calls equal come out first in, first out. A binary heap: `push` and `pop` "
    "take time\n    in proportion to the logarithm of the length. The queue owns its elements. There is no"
    " `peek_mut`\n    (`pop`, change and `push` instead), no `foreach`, no `clone` and no `reserve`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std"
    "::collections\u{1f}PriorityQueue::new\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn PriorityQueue::new<T>() : PriorityQueue<T>\u{1f}A new, empt"
    "y priority queue in the key types' own order, smallest first (as `Vec::sort` orders).\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Pri"
    "orityQueue::new<T>() : PriorityQueue<T>\n    in `std::collections`\n\n    A new, empty priority queue i"
    "n the key types' own order, smallest first (as `Vec::sort` orders).\n\n    `T` must be a key type; for"
    " any other `T` use `PriorityQueue::new_by`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::collections\u{1f}PriorityQueue::new_by\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Pr"
    "iorityQueue::new_by<T>(fn(ref<T, shared>, ref<T, shared>) : bool less) : PriorityQueue<T>\u{1f}A new, emp"
    "ty priority queue in the order `less` gives: the element no other goes before comes out first.\u{1f}\u{1f}expo"
    "rt fn PriorityQueue::new_by<T>(fn(ref<T, shared>, ref<T, shared>) : bool less) : PriorityQueue<T>\n  "
    "  in `std::collections`\n\n    A new, empty priority queue in the order `less` gives: the element no o"
    "ther goes before comes out\n    first.\n\n    `less` is true when its first argument goes before its se"
    "cond and must be a strict weak order, as for\n    `Vec::sort_by`. A largest-first queue passes a `les"
    "s` that answers \"greater\".\n\n    Example, \"PriorityQueue::new_by: first in, first out among equals\":\n"
    "        auto larger_tens = [](ref<i32, shared> a, ref<i32, shared> b) : bool { *a / 10 > *b / 10 };\n"
    "        PriorityQueue<i32> q = PriorityQueue::new_by(larger_tens);\n        PriorityQueue::push(&mut "
    "q, 15);\n        PriorityQueue::push(&mut q, 31);\n        PriorityQueue::push(&mut q, 12);\n        Pr"
    "iorityQueue::push(&mut q, 38);\n        assert(Option::unwrap(PriorityQueue::pop(&mut q)) == 31);\n   "
    "     assert(Option::unwrap(PriorityQueue::pop(&mut q)) == 38);\n        assert(Option::unwrap(Priorit"
    "yQueue::pop(&mut q)) == 15);\n        assert(Option::unwrap(PriorityQueue::pop(&mut q)) == 12);\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std"
    "::collections\u{1f}PriorityQueue::len\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn PriorityQueue::len<T>(ref<PriorityQueue<T>, shared> q)"
    " : usize\u{1f}The number of elements in `q`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn PriorityQueue::len<T>(ref<PriorityQueue<T>, share"
    "d> q) : usize\n    in `std::collections`\n\n    The number of elements in `q`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::collections\u{1f}Prior"
    "ityQueue::push\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn PriorityQueue::push<T>(ref<PriorityQueue<T>, exclusive> q, T x)\u{1f}Adds `x`"
    " to `q`; logarithmic in the length.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn PriorityQueue::push<T>(ref<PriorityQueue<T>, exclusiv"
    "e> q, T x)\n    in `std::collections`\n\n    Adds `x` to `q`; logarithmic in the length.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::collect"
    "ions\u{1f}PriorityQueue::pop\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn PriorityQueue::pop<T>(ref<PriorityQueue<T>, exclusive> q) : Opt"
    "ion<T>\u{1f}Removes the element that comes out first and returns it; `None` when `q` is empty.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn"
    " PriorityQueue::pop<T>(ref<PriorityQueue<T>, exclusive> q) : Option<T>\n    in `std::collections`\n\n  "
    "  Removes the element that comes out first and returns it; `None` when `q` is empty.\n\n    Among elem"
    "ents the order calls equal, the one pushed first comes out first. Logarithmic in the length.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::"
    "collections\u{1f}PriorityQueue::peek\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn PriorityQueue::peek<T>(ref<PriorityQueue<T>, shared> q)"
    " : Option<ref<T, shared>>\u{1f}The element `pop` would return next, as a shared reference; `None` when `q"
    "` is empty.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn PriorityQueue::peek<T>(ref<PriorityQueue<T>, shared> q) : Option<ref<T, share"
    "d>>\n    in `std::collections`\n\n    The element `pop` would return next, as a shared reference; `None"
    "` when `q` is empty.\n\n    The reference borrows the queue.\n\n    Example, \"PriorityQueue: smallest fi"
