    "ig-endian).\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn read_be<T: integer>(slice<u8, shared> s, usize at) : T\n    in `std::collectio"
    "ns`\n\n    The `T` whose `sizeof<T>()` bytes start at `s[at]`, most significant byte first (big-endian"
    ").\n\n    The type is written at the call: `read_be<u16>(&buf[0..$], 0)`. A signed `T` is read as two'"
    "s\n    complement. Faults (`index_out_of_bounds`) when fewer than `sizeof<T>()` bytes remain from `at"
