    "oint exclusive slices of consecutive elements, in order, as nearly equal in\n    length as they can b"
    "e.\n\n    With `n` elements, each part has `n / parts` elements and the first `n % parts` parts one mo"
    "re; some are\n    empty when `parts > n`. The result is empty when `parts` is 0. The parts are disjoi"
    "nt, so each can be\n    given to a thread of its own (`spawn(work, part)`) and written there without "
