    "out_write\u{1f}extern fn\u{1f}export unsafe extern fn stdout_write(rawptr<u8> buf, usize len) : isize\u{1f}Writes t"
    "he `len` bytes at `buf` to standard output: the primitive under `printf`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export unsafe extern fn s"
    "tdout_write(rawptr<u8> buf, usize len) : isize\n    in `std::io`\n\n    Writes the `len` bytes at `buf`"
    " to standard output: the primitive under `printf`.\n\n    Called inside `unsafe`, with `buf` pointing "
    "at `len` readable bytes; its result is a claim like any\n    extern's. What it writes goes through th"
    "e same buffer as `printf` (`flush_stdout`). Programs write with\n    `printf`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::io\u{1f}stdin_read\u{1f}e"
    "xtern fn\u{1f}export unsafe extern fn stdin_read(rawptr<u8> buf, usize len) : isize\u{1f}Reads up to `len` byt"
    "es of standard input into `buf`: the primitive under `read_all_bytes`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export unsafe extern fn stdi"
    "n_read(rawptr<u8> buf, usize len) : isize\n    in `std::io`\n\n    Reads up to `len` bytes of standard "
    "input into `buf`: the primitive under `read_all_bytes`.\n\n    Called inside `unsafe`, with `buf` poin"
    "ting at `len` writable bytes. Its result, a claim like any\n    extern's, is the number of bytes read"
    ": 0 at the end of the input, negative when the input cannot be read.\n    Programs read with `read_li"
    "ne`, `read_all` or `read_all_bytes`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::io\u{1f}flush_stdout\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn flush_stdout()\u{1f}Writes out w"
    "hat standard output still holds in its buffer.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn flush_stdout()\n    in `std::io`\n\n    Write"
    "s out what standard output still holds in its buffer.\n\n    Standard output is buffered; standard err"
    "or is not. Reading standard input, writing to standard error,\n    `exit` and the program's end write"
    " the buffer out themselves, so this is needed only when standard output\n    is a pipe or a file that"
    " someone watches while the program runs (progress, a log), and before handing over\n    to C code tha"
    "t writes through `stdio`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::io\u{1f}read_line\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn read_line() : Result<Option<String>, File"
    "Error>\u{1f}The next line of standard input, without its line ending, or `Ok(None)` at the end of the inp"
    "ut.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn read_line() : Result<Option<String>, FileError>\n    in `std::io`\n\n    The next line o"
    "f standard input, without its line ending, or `Ok(None)` at the end of the input.\n\n    - A line is e"
    "very byte up to the next `\\n`, which is consumed and not included; a `\\r` just before it is\n      co"
    "nsumed with it, so a Windows line ending reads as a Unix one. A last line with no `\\n` is still a\n  "
    "    line, and keeps a final `\\r`.\n    - `Ok(None)` when the input ended before the line's first byte"
    ", and on every call after that.\n    - `Err(FileError::Utf8(e))` when the line is not UTF-8, `e.offse"
    "t` counted within the line; the line is\n      consumed, so the next call reads the one after it.\n   "
    " - `Err(FileError::Io)` when standard input cannot be read; the bytes of the line read so far are lo"
    "st.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::io\u{1f}read_all_bytes\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn read_all_bytes() : Result<Vec<u8>, FileError>\u{1f}The rest of "
    "standard input, as bytes; empty when the input has already ended.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn read_all_bytes() : Resu"
    "lt<Vec<u8>, FileError>\n    in `std::io`\n\n    The rest of standard input, as bytes; empty when the in"
    "put has already ended.\n\n    `Err(FileError::Io)` when standard input cannot be read. `read_all` take"
    "s it as text.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::io\u{1f}read_all\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn read_all() : Result<String, FileError>\u{1f}The rest of sta"
    "ndard input, as text.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn read_all() : Result<String, FileError>\n    in `std::io`\n\n    The re"
    "st of standard input, as text.\n\n    `Err(FileError::Utf8(e))` when it is not UTF-8, and `Err(FileErr"
    "or::Io)` when it cannot be read;\n    `read_all_bytes` takes it as bytes.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::fs\u{1f}FileError\u{1f}enum\u{1f}ex"
    "port enum FileError\u{1f}The error of every input and output operation of `std`, for files and standard i"
    "nput alike.\u{1f}\u{1f}export enum FileError\n    in `std::fs`\n\n    The error of every input and output operati"
    "on of `std`, for files and standard input alike.\n\n    - `NotFound`: no such file, or a directory on "
    "the path does not exist.\n    - `Denied`: the environment refuses the operation.\n    - `Io`: any othe"
    "r failure (the path names a directory, a device error, …).\n    - `Utf8(e)`: the bytes read are not"
    " UTF-8; `e` gives the offset of the first byte that is not.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::fs\u{1f}FileError::text\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn F"
    "ileError::text(ref<FileError, shared> e) : str\u{1f}The error as a short phrase for a person (`not found`"
    ", `permission denied`).\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn FileError::text(ref<FileError, shared> e) : str\n    in `std::fs`\n"
    "\n    The error as a short phrase for a person (`not found`, `permission denied`).\n\n    Example, \"Fil"
    "eError::text: a phrase to print\":\n        FileError e = FileError::NotFound;\n        assert(FileErro"
    "r::text(&e) == \"not found\");\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::fs\u{1f}read_file\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn read_file(StringView path) : Result<St"
    "ring, FileError>\u{1f}The whole contents of the file at `path`, as text.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn read_file(StringView "
    "path) : Result<String, FileError>\n    in `std::fs`\n\n    The whole contents of the file at `path`, as"
    " text.\n\n    A relative path is resolved against the working directory. `Err(Utf8(e))` when the bytes"
    " are not UTF-8,\n    `e` giving the offset of the first that is not; `Err(NotFound)` when no such fil"
    "e exists; `Err(Denied)`\n    when the environment refuses; `Err(Io)` for any other failure (a directo"
    "ry, a device error). Use\n    `read_bytes` for bytes that need not be text, and `File` for a file too"
    " large to hold.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::fs\u{1f}write_file\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn write_file(StringView path, StringView text) : Res"
    "ult<void, FileError>\u{1f}Makes the file at `path` hold exactly `text`, creating it or replacing its cont"
    "ents.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn write_file(StringView path, StringView text) : Result<void, FileError>\n    in `std:"
    ":fs`\n\n    Makes the file at `path` hold exactly `text`, creating it or replacing its contents.\n\n    "
    "`Err(NotFound)` when a directory on the path does not exist; `Err(Denied)` when the environment refu"
    "ses\n    the write; `Err(Io)` for any other failure.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::fs\u{1f}File\u{1f}struct\u{1f}export resource struct Fil"
    "e\u{1f}An open file, read and written in order from a position that `seek` moves.\u{1f}\u{1f}export resource struct"
    " File\n    in `std::fs`\n\n    An open file, read and written in order from a position that `seek` move"
    "s.\n\n    Every `File` comes from `File::open`, `create`, `append`, `open_rw` or `create_new`. Positio"
    "ns are `u64`,\n    so a file larger than the address space is still addressed. Reading and writing ar"
    "e buffered; the bytes\n    written reach the file no later than the next operation on it, any other f"
    "ile-system operation of the\n    program, the start of a child process, or the program's end.\n\n    De"
    "stroying a `File` closes it without making it durable and without reporting a failure; a program\n   "
    " that must know its bytes were stored calls `File::close`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::fs\u{1f}File::open\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn File::o"
    "pen(StringView path) : Result<File, FileError>\u{1f}Opens the existing file at `path` for reading, at pos"
    "ition 0.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn File::open(StringView path) : Result<File, FileError>\n    in `std::fs`\n\n    Open"
    "s the existing file at `path` for reading, at position 0.\n\n    `Err(NotFound)` when there is no such"
    " file; `Err(Denied)` when the environment refuses; `Err(Io)` for\n    any other failure (the path nam"
    "es a directory).\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::fs\u{1f}File::create\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn File::create(StringView path) : Result<File, Fi"
    "leError>\u{1f}Opens the file at `path` for writing from empty, creating it or discarding its contents.\u{1f}\u{1f}e"
    "xport fn File::create(StringView path) : Result<File, FileError>\n    in `std::fs`\n\n    Opens the fil"
    "e at `path` for writing from empty, creating it or discarding its contents.\n\n    `Err(NotFound)` whe"
    "n a directory on the path does not exist; `Err(Denied)`, `Err(Io)` as `File::open`'s.\n    Use `File:"
    ":create_new` when an existing file must not be overwritten.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::fs\u{1f}File::append\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn File"
    "::append(StringView path) : Result<File, FileError>\u{1f}Opens the file at `path` for writing at its end,"
    " creating it if it does not exist.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn File::append(StringView path) : Result<File, FileError"
    ">\n    in `std::fs`\n\n    Opens the file at `path` for writing at its end, creating it if it does not "
    "exist.\n\n    Every write lands at the end of the file.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::fs\u{1f}File::open_rw\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn File::ope"
    "n_rw(StringView path) : Result<File, FileError>\u{1f}Opens the file at `path` for reading and writing, cr"
    "eating it if it does not exist, its contents kept.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn File::open_rw(StringView path) : Resul"
    "t<File, FileError>\n    in `std::fs`\n\n    Opens the file at `path` for reading and writing, creating "
    "it if it does not exist, its contents kept.\n\n    The position starts at 0; a write lands at the posi"
    "tion reading has reached.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::fs\u{1f}File::read\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn File::read(ref<File, exclusive> f, ref<V"
    "ec<u8>, exclusive> buf, usize max) : Result<usize, FileError>\u{1f}Appends up to `max` bytes from the fil"
    "e's position to the end of `buf` and returns how many.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn File::read(ref<File, exclusive> f,"
    " ref<Vec<u8>, exclusive> buf, usize max) : Result<usize, FileError>\n    in `std::fs`\n\n    Appends up"
    " to `max` bytes from the file's position to the end of `buf` and returns how many.\n\n    At most a Mi"
    "B is read at a time, whatever `max` is; fewer bytes come only at the end of the file, and\n    `Ok(0)"
    "` (for a `max` above 0) means the end. `Err(Io)` on a file opened only for writing.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::fs\u{1f}File::"
    "read_to_end\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn File::read_to_end(ref<File, exclusive> f, ref<Vec<u8>, exclusive> buf) : Re"
    "sult<usize, FileError>\u{1f}Appends the rest of the file, from its position, to the end of `buf` and retu"
    "rns how many bytes.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn File::read_to_end(ref<File, exclusive> f, ref<Vec<u8>, exclusive> buf"
    ") : Result<usize, FileError>\n    in `std::fs`\n\n    Appends the rest of the file, from its position, "
    "to the end of `buf` and returns how many bytes.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::fs\u{1f}File::read_line\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn File::read_li"
    "ne(ref<File, exclusive> f) : Result<Option<String>, FileError>\u{1f}The next line of the file, without it"
    "s final `'\\n'` or one `'\\r'` just before it.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn File::read_line(ref<File, exclusive> f) : Re"
    "sult<Option<String>, FileError>\n    in `std::fs`\n\n    The next line of the file, without its final `"
    "'\\n'` or one `'\\r'` just before it.\n\n    `Ok(None)` at the end of the file. A last line with no `'\\n"
    "'` is still a line. `Err(Utf8(e))` when the\n    line is not UTF-8, `e`'s offset counted from the lin"
    "e's start; `Err(Io)` on a file opened only for\n    writing. Lines end as `read_line` on standard inp"
    "ut ends them.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::fs\u{1f}File::write\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn File::write(ref<File, exclusive> f, slice<u8, share"
    "d> data) : Result<void, FileError>\u{1f}Writes all of `data` at the file's position, or at its end for a "
    "file opened by `File::append`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn File::write(ref<File, exclusive> f, slice<u8, shared> data"
    ") : Result<void, FileError>\n    in `std::fs`\n\n    Writes all of `data` at the file's position, or at"
    " its end for a file opened by `File::append`.\n\n    The file grows as needed and the position moves p"
    "ast the bytes written. Writes are buffered (see `File`);\n    a failure the environment reports late "
    "is reported by the file's next operation. `Err(Io)` on a file\n    opened only for reading.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::fs"
    "\u{1f}File::write_text\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn File::write_text(ref<File, exclusive> f, StringView text) : Result<vo"
    "id, FileError>\u{1f}Writes the bytes of `text` at the file's position, as `File::write` does.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn "
    "File::write_text(ref<File, exclusive> f, StringView text) : Result<void, FileError>\n    in `std::fs`"
    "\n\n    Writes the bytes of `text` at the file's position, as `File::write` does.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::fs\u{1f}File::seek"
    "\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn File::seek(ref<File, exclusive> f, u64 pos) : Result<void, FileError>\u{1f}Moves the file's"
    " position to byte `pos` from the start.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn File::seek(ref<File, exclusive> f, u64 pos) : Res"
    "ult<void, FileError>\n    in `std::fs`\n\n    Moves the file's position to byte `pos` from the start.\n\n"
    "    A position beyond the end is allowed: reading there gives 0 bytes, and writing there extends the"
    " file.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::fs\u{1f}File::len\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn File::len(ref<File, shared> f) : Result<u64, FileError>\u{1f}The "
    "file's length in bytes.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn File::len(ref<File, shared> f) : Result<u64, FileError>\n    in `s"
    "td::fs`\n\n    The file's length in bytes.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::fs\u{1f}File::create_new\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn File::create_new(St"
    "ringView path) : Result<Option<File>, FileError>\u{1f}Opens a new file at `path` for writing, only if not"
    "hing is there yet.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn File::create_new(StringView path) : Result<Option<File>, FileError>\n  "
    "  in `std::fs`\n\n    Opens a new file at `path` for writing, only if nothing is there yet.\n\n    `Ok(N"
    "one)` when a file or a directory of that name already exists, and nothing is changed, so of two\n    "
    "programs that race to make the same file exactly one wins: a lock file, a pid file, a file that must"
    "\n    never be overwritten. `Err(NotFound)` when a directory above `path` does not exist; other error"
    "s as\n    `File::create`'s.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::fs\u{1f}File::flush\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn File::flush(ref<File, exclusive> f) : "
    "Result<void, FileError>\u{1f}Makes everything written to the file so far durable.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn File::flush("
    "ref<File, exclusive> f) : Result<void, FileError>\n    in `std::fs`\n\n    Makes everything written to "
    "the file so far durable.\n\n    The bytes are handed to the operating system and by it to the device, "
    "and from then on survive a crash\n    or a power loss; the write-then-rename pattern flushes before t"
    "he rename. `Err(Io)` on a file open only\n    for reading, or when the device fails.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::fs\u{1f}File::"
    "position\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn File::position(ref<File, shared> f) : Result<u64, FileError>\u{1f}The byte the next"
    " read or write starts at, counted from the start of the file.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn File::position(ref<File, sh"
    "ared> f) : Result<u64, FileError>\n    in `std::fs`\n\n    The byte the next read or write starts at, c"
    "ounted from the start of the file.\n\n    It is 0 when the file is opened (for `File::append`, the len"
    "gth once something is written) and is moved\n    by every read, `read_line`, write and `seek`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std:"
    ":fs\u{1f}File::close\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn File::close(File f) : Result<void, FileError>\u{1f}Closes the file, first ma"
    "king a file open for writing durable, and reports any failure.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn File::close(File f) : Resu"
    "lt<void, FileError>\n    in `std::fs`\n\n    Closes the file, first making a file open for writing dura"
    "ble, and reports any failure.\n\n    `Err(e)` when the environment reports a failure, including one fo"
    "r bytes written earlier; the file is\n    closed all the same. Destroying a `File` closes it too, but"
    " reports nothing.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::fs\u{1f}File::drop\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn File::drop(ref<File, exclusive> self)\u{1f}Closes an "
    "open file when its `File` is destroyed, without making it durable or reporting a failure.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn"
    " File::drop(ref<File, exclusive> self)\n    in `std::fs`\n\n    Closes an open file when its `File` is "
    "destroyed, without making it durable or reporting a failure.\n\n    The destructor; programs do not ca"
    "ll it, and call `File::close` to learn whether the bytes were stored.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::fs\u{1f}read_bytes\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export"
    " fn read_bytes(StringView path) : Result<Vec<u8>, FileError>\u{1f}The whole contents of the file at `path"
    "`, as bytes.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn read_bytes(StringView path) : Result<Vec<u8>, FileError>\n    in `std::fs`\n\n "
    "   The whole contents of the file at `path`, as bytes.\n\n    The errors are `File::open`'s and `File:"
    ":read_to_end`'s. Use `read_file` for text.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::fs\u{1f}write_bytes\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn write_bytes(StringView"
    " path, slice<u8, shared> data) : Result<void, FileError>\u{1f}Makes the file at `path` hold exactly `data"
    "`, creating it or replacing its contents.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn write_bytes(StringView path, slice<u8, shared> "
    "data) : Result<void, FileError>\n    in `std::fs`\n\n    Makes the file at `path` hold exactly `data`, "
    "creating it or replacing its contents.\n\n    The errors are `File::create`'s and `File::write`'s. Use"
    " `write_file` for text.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::fs\u{1f}PathKind\u{1f}enum\u{1f}export enum PathKind\u{1f}What a path names, as `path_kin"
    "d` and `file_info` report it.\u{1f}\u{1f}export enum PathKind\n    in `std::fs`\n\n    What a path names, as `pat"
    "h_kind` and `file_info` report it.\n\n    - `File(n)`: a file of `n` bytes.\n    - `Dir`: a directory.\n"
    "    - `Other`: something else, such as a device or a socket.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::fs\u{1f}make_dir\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn make_di"
    "r(StringView path) : Result<bool, FileError>\u{1f}Makes the directory `path`, whose parent must exist.\u{1f}\u{1f}e"
    "xport fn make_dir(StringView path) : Result<bool, FileError>\n    in `std::fs`\n\n    Makes the directo"
    "ry `path`, whose parent must exist.\n\n    `Ok(true)` when it was made; `Ok(false)` when a directory w"
    "as already there, so it is safe to call\n    again. `Err(NotFound)` when the parent does not exist; `"
    "Err(Io)` when something that is not a directory\n    is at `path`. Use `make_dir_all` to make the mis"
    "sing parents too.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::fs\u{1f}remove_file\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn remove_file(StringView path) : Result<void, Fil"
    "eError>\u{1f}Removes the file at `path`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn remove_file(StringView path) : Result<void, FileError"
    ">\n    in `std::fs`\n\n    Removes the file at `path`.\n\n    `Err(NotFound)` when there is none.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::"
    "fs\u{1f}remove_dir\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn remove_dir(StringView path) : Result<void, FileError>\u{1f}Removes the empty d"
    "irectory at `path`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn remove_dir(StringView path) : Result<void, FileError>\n    in `std::fs"
    "`\n\n    Removes the empty directory at `path`.\n\n    `Err(Io)` when it is not empty; `Err(NotFound)` w"
    "hen there is none. Use `remove_dir_all` to remove a\n    directory and everything in it.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::fs\u{1f}re"
    "name\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn rename(StringView from, StringView to) : Result<void, FileError>\u{1f}Renames (moves) w"
    "hat is at `from` to `to`, replacing a file at `to`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn rename(StringView from, StringView to"
    ") : Result<void, FileError>\n    in `std::fs`\n\n    Renames (moves) what is at `from` to `to`, replaci"
    "ng a file at `to`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::fs\u{1f}list_dir\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn list_dir(StringView path) : Result<Vec<String>, F"
    "ileError>\u{1f}The names of the entries of the directory `path`, sorted by their bytes.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn list_d"
    "ir(StringView path) : Result<Vec<String>, FileError>\n    in `std::fs`\n\n    The names of the entries "
    "of the directory `path`, sorted by their bytes.\n\n    The names are entry names, not paths (join them"
    " to `path` with `path_join`), and never `.` or `..`.\n    `Err(Utf8(e))` for a name that is not UTF-8"
    ".\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::fs\u{1f}path_kind\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn path_kind(StringView path) : Result<PathKind, FileError>\u{1f}What `pa"
    "th` names: a file and its length, a directory, or something else.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn path_kind(StringView pa"
    "th) : Result<PathKind, FileError>\n    in `std::fs`\n\n    What `path` names: a file and its length, a "
    "directory, or something else.\n\n    A symbolic link is followed. `Err(NotFound)` when nothing is at `"
    "path`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::fs\u{1f}path_join\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn path_join(StringView base, StringView tail) : String\u{1f}The pat"
    "h `base` followed by `tail`, with the platform's separator between them.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn path_join(String"
    "View base, StringView tail) : String\n    in `std::fs`\n\n    The path `base` followed by `tail`, with "
    "the platform's separator between them.\n\n    No separator is added after one `base` already ends with"
    ". An absolute `tail` is returned alone. Reads the\n    text only, never the file system.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::fs\u{1f}pa"
    "th_parent\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn path_parent(StringView p) : Option<String>\u{1f}The path `p` without its last part"
    ".\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn path_parent(StringView p) : Option<String>\n    in `std::fs`\n\n    The path `p` without i"
    "ts last part.\n\n    `None` for a root or the empty path; the empty path for a single relative name. R"
    "eads the text only,\n    never the file system; the grammar is the platform's (`\\` also separates par"
    "ts on Windows).\n\n    Example, \"path_parent: a single name\":\n        assert(Option::unwrap(path_paren"
    "t(\"notes.txt\")) == \"\");\n        assert(Option::is_none(&path_parent(\"\")));\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::fs\u{1f}path_file_name\u{1f}"
    "fn\u{1f}export fn path_file_name(StringView p) : Option<String>\u{1f}The last part of the path `p`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn"
    " path_file_name(StringView p) : Option<String>\n    in `std::fs`\n\n    The last part of the path `p`.\n"
    "\n    `None` when the last part is `..`, or when there is none (`/`, the empty path). Reads the text "
    "only.\n\n    Example, \"path_file_name: a final ..\":\n        assert(Option::unwrap(path_file_name(\"src/"
    "main.cb\")) == \"main.cb\");\n        assert(Option::is_none(&path_file_name(\"src/..\")));\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::fs\u{1f}path"
    "_stem\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn path_stem(StringView p) : Option<String>\u{1f}The file name of `p` without its extensi"
    "on (`archive.tar` of `archive.tar.gz`).\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn path_stem(StringView p) : Option<String>\n    in `"
    "std::fs`\n\n    The file name of `p` without its extension (`archive.tar` of `archive.tar.gz`).\n\n    A"
    " name whose only dot is its first byte has no extension, so its stem is the whole name (`.bashrc`).\n"
    "    Reads the text only.\n\n    Example, \"path_stem: the last dot\":\n        assert(Option::unwrap(path"
    "_stem(\"archive.tar.gz\")) == \"archive.tar\");\n        assert(Option::unwrap(path_stem(\".bashrc\")) == \""
    ".bashrc\");\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::fs\u{1f}path_extension\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn path_extension(StringView p) : Option<String>\u{1f}The e"
    "xtension of the file name of `p`, without its dot (`gz` of `archive.tar.gz`).\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn path_extens"
    "ion(StringView p) : Option<String>\n    in `std::fs`\n\n    The extension of the file name of `p`, with"
    "out its dot (`gz` of `archive.tar.gz`).\n\n    `None` when there is none: a name with no dot, or whose"
    " only dot is its first byte. Reads the text only.\n\n    Example, \"path_extension: no extension\":\n    "
    "    assert(Option::unwrap(path_extension(\"archive.tar.gz\")) == \"gz\");\n        assert(Option::is_none"
    "(&path_extension(\".bashrc\")));\n        assert(Option::is_none(&path_extension(\"README\")));\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::fs"
    "\u{1f}path_is_absolute\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn path_is_absolute(StringView p) : bool\u{1f}Whether `p` names a place witho"
    "ut the working directory.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn path_is_absolute(StringView p) : bool\n    in `std::fs`\n\n    Whe"
    "ther `p` names a place without the working directory.\n\n    By the platform's grammar: a leading `/` "
    "on Unix; `C:\\` or `\\\\server\\share\\` on Windows. Reads the text\n    only.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::fs\u{1f}path_normalize\u{1f}fn"
    "\u{1f}export fn path_normalize(StringView p) : String\u{1f}The path `p` with every `.` part removed and every "
    "`x/..` (`x` a name) resolved.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn path_normalize(StringView p) : String\n    in `std::fs`\n\n   "
    " The path `p` with every `.` part removed and every `x/..` (`x` a name) resolved.\n\n    By the text a"
    "lone: a link is not followed, so the result can name another place than `p` when `x` is a\n    link. "
    "A leading `..` stays, `/..` is `/`, and a path with no part left is `.`. Use `path_canonical` to\n   "
    " ask the file system.\n\n    Example, \"path_normalize: . and ..\":\n        assert(path_normalize(\"a/./b"
    "/../c\") == path_join(\"a\", \"c\"));\n        assert(path_normalize(\"../x/..\") == \"..\");\n        assert(p"
    "ath_normalize(\"a/..\") == \".\");\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::fs\u{1f}path_canonical\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn path_canonical(StringView p) : "
    "Result<String, FileError>\u{1f}The absolute path the operating system resolves `p` to, with every link fo"
    "llowed.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn path_canonical(StringView p) : Result<String, FileError>\n    in `std::fs`\n\n    Th"
    "e absolute path the operating system resolves `p` to, with every link followed.\n\n    `p` must exist:"
    " `Err(NotFound)` when nothing is at `p`; `Err(Utf8(e))` when the result is not UTF-8.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::fs\u{1f}File"
    "Info\u{1f}struct\u{1f}export struct FileInfo\u{1f}What `file_info` reports of a path.\u{1f}\u{1f}export struct FileInfo\n    i"
    "n `std::fs`\n\n    What `file_info` reports of a path.\n\n    - `kind`: what the path names, as `path_ki"
    "nd` gives it.\n    - `len`: the length in bytes.\n    - `modified_unix`: the last modification, in who"
    "le seconds since 1970-01-01T00:00:00Z (rounded down).\n    - `readonly`: whether the file is read-onl"
    "y.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::fs\u{1f}file_info\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn file_info(StringView path) : Result<FileInfo, FileError>\u{1f}The kin"
    "d, length, modification time and read-only state of what is at `path`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn file_info(StringVi"
    "ew path) : Result<FileInfo, FileError>\n    in `std::fs`\n\n    The kind, length, modification time and"
