    "`Err(NotFound)` when nothing is at `path`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::fs\u{1f}copy_file\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn copy_file(StringView fro"
    "m, StringView to) : Result<u64, FileError>\u{1f}Copies the file `from` to `to`, replacing a file there, a"
    "nd returns the number of bytes copied.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn copy_file(StringView from, StringView to) : Result"
    "<u64, FileError>\n    in `std::fs`\n\n    Copies the file `from` to `to`, replacing a file there, and r"
    "eturns the number of bytes copied.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::fs\u{1f}copy_permissions\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn copy_permissions(StringVi"
    "ew from, StringView to) : Result<void, FileError>\u{1f}Gives what is at `to` the permissions of what is a"
    "t `from`: on Unix the mode bits, on Windows the read-only flag.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn copy_permissions(StringVi"
    "ew from, StringView to) : Result<void, FileError>\n    in `std::fs`\n\n    Gives what is at `to` the pe"
    "rmissions of what is at `from`: on Unix the mode bits, on Windows the\n    read-only flag.\n\n    For t"
    "he write-then-rename pattern: a file written beside the original and renamed over it keeps the\n    o"
    "riginal's permissions only when they are copied to it before the rename. `Err(NotFound)` when nothin"
    "g\n    is at `from` or at `to`.\n\n    Example, \"copy_permissions: one file's permissions given to anot"
    "her\":\n        String tmp = temp_dir();\n        String dir = path_join(&tmp, &sprintf(\"cb-perm-%v\", p"
    "rocess_id()));\n        _ = make_dir_all(&dir);\n        String a = path_join(&dir, \"a.txt\");\n        "
    "String b = path_join(&dir, \"b.txt\");\n        _ = write_file(&a, \"a\");\n        _ = write_file(&b, \"b\""
    ");\n        assert(Result::is_ok(&copy_permissions(&a, &b)));\n        bool ra = Result::unwrap(file_i"
    "nfo(&a)).readonly;\n        bool rb = Result::unwrap(file_info(&b)).readonly;\n        assert(ra == rb"
    ");\n        String gone = path_join(&dir, \"gone.txt\");\n        assert(Result::is_err(&copy_permission"
    "s(&gone, &b)));\n        _ = remove_dir_all(&dir);\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::fs\u{1f}make_dir_all\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn make_dir_all(S"
    "tringView path) : Result<void, FileError>\u{1f}Makes the directory `path` and every missing directory abo"
