    "\n\n    What a log line or a service's registration names the machine by. `Err(Utf8(e))` when it is no"
    "t UTF-8;\n    `Err(Io)` when the operating system cannot say.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::env\u{1f}Args\u{1f}struct\u{1f}export struct Ar"
    "gs\u{1f}The program's arguments, read as options and positional arguments.\u{1f}\u{1f}export struct Args\n    in `st"
    "d::env`\n\n    The program's arguments, read as options and positional arguments.\n\n    Each `Args::fla"
    "g`, `Args::option` or `Args::options` call names an option, takes its occurrences from\n    the argum"
    "ents and adds a line to `Args::help`; `Args::finish` then gives the arguments left and refuses\n    a"
    "ny option nobody declared. `--name`, `--name=value`, `--name value`, `-s` and `-s value` are read; `"
    "--`\n    ends the options, and a lone `-` is an argument.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::env\u{1f}Args::new\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Args::new"
    "(StringView usage) : Result<Args, Utf8Error>\u{1f}The program's arguments, from `arg(0)` on, with the usa"
    "ge line that `Args::help` shows.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Args::new(StringView usage) : Result<Args, Utf8Error>\n  "
    "  in `std::env`\n\n    The program's arguments, from `arg(0)` on, with the usage line that `Args::help"
