    "g> items, StringView usage) : Args\u{1f}The arguments `items`, read as `Args::new` reads the program's ow"
    "n.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Args::from(Vec<String> items, StringView usage) : Args\n    in `std::env`\n\n    The argu"
    "ments `items`, read as `Args::new` reads the program's own.\n\n    For arguments that come from elsewh"
    "ere, or a test.\n\n    Example, \"Args::from: flags, options, the rest\":\n        Vec<String> items = Ve"
    "c::new();\n        Vec::push(&mut items, \"-v\");\n        Vec::push(&mut items, \"--out=a.txt\");\n       "
    " Vec::push(&mut items, \"in.txt\");\n        Args a = Args::from(items, \"prog [options] FILE\");\n       "
    " assert(Args::flag(&mut a, \"verbose\", \"v\", \"say more\"));\n        assert(Option::unwrap(Args::option("
    "&mut a, \"out\", \"o\", \"FILE\", \"where to write\")) == \"a.txt\");\n        Vec<String> rest = Result::unwra"
    "p(Args::finish(&mut a));\n        assert(Vec::len(&rest) == 1 && rest[0] == \"in.txt\");\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::env\u{1f}Arg"
