    "r `--name` or `-short` is among the arguments before `--`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Args::flag(ref<Args, exclusive"
    "> a, str name, str short, str help) : bool\n    in `std::env`\n\n    Whether `--name` or `-short` is am"
    "ong the arguments before `--`.\n\n    `short` is one letter, or `\"\"` for none; `help` is the option's "
    "line in `Args::help`. Every occurrence\n    is taken, so `Args::finish` does not see it.\n\n    Example"
    ", \"Args::flag: after --\":\n        Vec<String> items = Vec::new();\n        Vec::push(&mut items, \"--\""
    ");\n        Vec::push(&mut items, \"-v\");\n        Args a = Args::from(items, \"prog [options] FILE\");\n "
    "       assert(!Args::flag(&mut a, \"verbose\", \"v\", \"say more\"));\n        Vec<String> rest = Result::u"
    "nwrap(Args::finish(&mut a));\n        assert(Vec::len(&rest) == 1 && rest[0] == \"-v\");\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::env\u{1f}Arg"
    "s::options\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Args::options(ref<Args, exclusive> a, str name, str short, str value_name, s"
    "tr help) : Vec<String>\u{1f}Every value given for the option `--name` or `-short`, in order.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn A"
    "rgs::options(ref<Args, exclusive> a, str name, str short, str value_name, str help) : Vec<String>\n  "
    "  in `std::env`\n\n    Every value given for the option `--name` or `-short`, in order.\n\n    A value i"
    "s given as `--name=value`, `--name value` or `-s value`; each is taken, the value with it.\n    `valu"
    "e_name` names the value in `Args::help` (`FILE`). A `--name` or `-s` that is the last argument,\n    "
    "just before `--`, or followed by an argument an earlier declaration took (a flag's `-v`), has no val"
    "ue\n    and is left for `Args::finish` to refuse.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::env\u{1f}Args::option\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Args::option(r"
    "ef<Args, exclusive> a, str name, str short, str value_name, str help) : Option<String>\u{1f}The value of "
    "the option `--name` or `-short`, the last one when it is given more than once.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Args::opti"
    "on(ref<Args, exclusive> a, str name, str short, str value_name, str help) : Option<String>\n    in `s"
    "td::env`\n\n    The value of the option `--name` or `-short`, the last one when it is given more than "
    "once.\n\n    `None` when it is not given. Takes its arguments as `Args::options` does.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::env\u{1f}Args"
    "::finish\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Args::finish(ref<Args, exclusive> a) : Result<Vec<String>, String>\u{1f}The argumen"
    "ts no declaration took, in order, every argument after `--` among them.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Args::finish(ref<"
    "Args, exclusive> a) : Result<Vec<String>, String>\n    in `std::env`\n\n    The arguments no declaratio"
    "n took, in order, every argument after `--` among them.\n\n    `Err(message)` for the first argument b"
    "efore `--` that starts with `-` and is not a lone `-`:\n    `unknown option --x`, or `missing a value"
    " for --x` for a declared option given without its value. The\n    message is for the program to print"
    ", usually followed by `Args::help`.\n\n    Example, \"Args::finish: an undeclared option\":\n        Vec<"
    "String> items = Vec::new();\n        Vec::push(&mut items, \"--colour\");\n        Args a = Args::from(i"
