    "own option --colour\"),\n            Ok(_)  : assert(false),\n        }\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::env\u{1f}Args::help\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export"
    " fn Args::help(ref<Args, shared> a) : String\u{1f}The usage line and one aligned line per option declared"
    " so far, ready to print.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Args::help(ref<Args, shared> a) : String\n    in `std::env`\n\n    "
    "The usage line and one aligned line per option declared so far, ready to print.\n\n    Example, \"Args:"
    ":help: the layout\":\n        Args a = Args::from(Vec::new(), \"prog FILE\");\n        bool verbose = Arg"
    "s::flag(&mut a, \"verbose\", \"v\", \"say more\");\n        Option<String> out = Args::option(&mut a, \"out\""
    ", \"\", \"FILE\", \"where to write\");\n        String h = Args::help(&a);\n        assert(h == \"Usage: prog"
