    "-out FILE  where to write\\n\");\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::memory\u{1f}Rc\u{1f}struct\u{1f}export resource struct Rc<T>\u{1f}A reference-coun"
    "ted handle to a value on the heap that several owners share.\u{1f}\u{1f}export resource struct Rc<T>\n    in `s"
    "td::memory`\n\n    A reference-counted handle to a value on the heap that several owners share.\n\n    E"
    "ach `Rc` is one strong handle; the value is destroyed when the last strong handle is, and the memory"
    " is\n    freed once no `Weak` handle remains either. The value is reached only as a shared reference "
    "(`Rc::get`),\n    so changing it needs a `mutex` inside. A cycle of `Rc`s is never freed: a parent po"
    "inter, a cache or an\n    observer list holds a `Weak` instead. `Rc` is not thread-safe (the count is"
    " not synchronised); share\n    across threads with `ref<mutex<T>, shared>`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::memory\u{1f}Rc::new\u{1f}fn\u{1f}"
    "export fn Rc::new<T>(T v) : Rc<T>\u{1f}A new `Rc` holding `v`, the only strong handle to it.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn R"
    "c::new<T>(T v) : Rc<T>\n    in `std::memory`\n\n    A new `Rc` holding `v`, the only strong handle to i"
    "t.\n\n    Allocates; faults (`alloc_failure`) when memory cannot be had.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::memory\u{1f}Rc::clone\u{1f}fn\u{1f}ex"
    "port fn Rc::clone<T>(ref<Rc<T>, shared> r) : Rc<T>\u{1f}A second strong handle to the value `r` holds; no"
    "thing is copied.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Rc::clone<T>(ref<Rc<T>, shared> r) : Rc<T>\n    in `std::memory`\n\n    A s"
    "econd strong handle to the value `r` holds; nothing is copied.\n\n    What `clone(&r)` calls for an `R"
    "c`. A reference into the value from `Rc::get` may stay live across it.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::memory\u{1f}Rc::get\u{1f}fn\u{1f}expo"
    "rt fn Rc::get<T>(ref<Rc<T>, shared> r) : ref<T, shared>\u{1f}The value `r` holds, as a shared reference.\u{1f}"
    "\u{1f}export fn Rc::get<T>(ref<Rc<T>, shared> r) : ref<T, shared>\n    in `std::memory`\n\n    The value `r`"
    " holds, as a shared reference.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::memory\u{1f}Rc::drop\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Rc::drop<T>(ref<Rc<T>, exclusive>"
    " self)\u{1f}Ends one strong handle; run when an `Rc` is destroyed, so programs write `drop(r)` or let it "
    "go.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Rc::drop<T>(ref<Rc<T>, exclusive> self)\n    in `std::memory`\n\n    Ends one strong han"
    "dle; run when an `Rc` is destroyed, so programs write `drop(r)` or let it go.\n\n    When this was the"
    " last strong handle the value is destroyed now, and with no `Weak` handle left the\n    memory is fre"
    "ed too.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::memory\u{1f}Weak\u{1f}struct\u{1f}export resource struct Weak<T>\u{1f}A handle to an `Rc`'s value that do"
    "es not keep the value alive.\u{1f}\u{1f}export resource struct Weak<T>\n    in `std::memory`\n\n    A handle to a"
    "n `Rc`'s value that does not keep the value alive.\n\n    It keeps only the memory: once the last `Rc`"
    " ends, the value is gone and `Weak::upgrade` gives `None`.\n    Dropping the last handle of either ki"
    "nd frees the memory.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::memory\u{1f}Rc::downgrade\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Rc::downgrade<T>(ref<Rc<T>, shared> r)"
    " : Weak<T>\u{1f}A `Weak` handle to the value `r` holds.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Rc::downgrade<T>(ref<Rc<T>, shared> r)"
    " : Weak<T>\n    in `std::memory`\n\n    A `Weak` handle to the value `r` holds.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::memory\u{1f}Weak::upg"
    "rade\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Weak::upgrade<T>(ref<Weak<T>, shared> w) : Option<Rc<T>>\u{1f}A new strong handle to th"
    "e value, or `None` when the value has ended.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Weak::upgrade<T>(ref<Weak<T>, shared> w) : O"
