    "mpty.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::sync\u{1f}Channel::try_recv\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Channel::try_recv<T>(ref<Channel<T>, shared> ch) : "
    "Result<Option<T>, void>\u{1f}Takes the value at the front of `ch` if one is waiting, without waiting.\u{1f}\u{1f}ex"
    "port fn Channel::try_recv<T>(ref<Channel<T>, shared> ch) : Result<Option<T>, void>\n    in `std::sync"
    "`\n\n    Takes the value at the front of `ch` if one is waiting, without waiting.\n\n    `Ok(Some(v))` w"
    "ith the value; `Ok(None)` when the channel is empty; `Err(())` once it is closed and empty,\n    so a"
    " loop that also polls something else (a socket, `interrupt_requested`) knows when the senders are\n  "
    "  done.\n\n    Example, \"Channel::try_recv: the three outcomes\":\n        Channel<i32> ch = Channel::ne"
