    "y_recv(&ch))) == 5);\n        assert(Result::is_err(&Channel::try_recv(&ch)));\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::sync\u{1f}Channel::r"
    "ecv_timeout_ms\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Channel::recv_timeout_ms<T>(ref<Channel<T>, shared> ch, u64 ms) : Result"
    "<Option<T>, void>\u{1f}Takes the value at the front of `ch`, waiting at most `ms` milliseconds for one.\u{1f}\u{1f}"
    "export fn Channel::recv_timeout_ms<T>(ref<Channel<T>, shared> ch, u64 ms) : Result<Option<T>, void>\n"
    "    in `std::sync`\n\n    Takes the value at the front of `ch`, waiting at most `ms` milliseconds for "
    "one.\n\n    `Ok(Some(v))` with the value; `Ok(None)` when none arrived in time; `Err(())` when the cha"
    "nnel is closed\n    and empty. The wait is a poll (every millisecond at first, then every five), so i"
    "t ends at most a few\n    milliseconds late.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::sync\u{1f}cpu_count\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn cpu_count() : usize\u{1f}H"
    "ow many threads the machine runs at once, at least 1: the size of a worker pool.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn cpu_coun"
    "t() : usize\n    in `std::sync`\n\n    How many threads the machine runs at once, at least 1: the size "
    "of a worker pool.\n\n    The processors, or what this program may use of them.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::sync\u{1f}Channel::cl"
    "ose\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Channel::close<T>(ref<Channel<T>, shared> ch)\u{1f}Marks `ch` as taking no more values.\u{1f}"
    "\u{1f}export fn Channel::close<T>(ref<Channel<T>, shared> ch)\n    in `std::sync`\n\n    Marks `ch` as takin"
    "g no more values.\n\n    `send` fails from then on, and `recv` gives `None` once the values already in"
    " it are taken. Waiting\n    senders and receivers wake. Closing a closed channel does nothing.\n\n    E"
    "xample, \"Channel::close: draining a closed channel\":\n        Channel<i32> ch = Channel::new(2);\n    "
    "    assert(Result::is_ok(&Channel::send(&ch, 1)));\n        assert(Result::is_ok(&Channel::send(&ch, "
    "2)));\n        Channel::close(&ch);\n        assert(Result::is_err(&Channel::send(&ch, 3)));\n        a"
    "ssert(Option::unwrap(Channel::recv(&ch)) == 1);\n        assert(Option::unwrap(Channel::recv(&ch)) =="
    " 2);\n        assert(Option::is_none(&Channel::recv(&ch)));\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::sync\u{1f}Channel::drop\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Ch"
    "annel::drop<T>(ref<Channel<T>, exclusive> self)\u{1f}Destroys the values still in the channel, oldest fir"
    "st; run when a `Channel` is destroyed.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Channel::drop<T>(ref<Channel<T>, exclusive> self)\n"
    "    in `std::sync`\n\n    Destroys the values still in the channel, oldest first; run when a `Channel`"
