    "in `std::sync`\n\n    A spawned thread's fault, contained and handed over by `try_join` instead of rai"
    "sed again.\n\n    Its text is kept by the runtime until the program ends.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::sync\u{1f}try_join\u{1f}fn\u{1f}expo"
    "rt fn try_join<R>(handle<R> h) : Result<R, ThreadFailure>\u{1f}Waits for the thread `h` and gives its res"
    "ult, or its failure as a value instead of raising it again.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn try_join<R>(handle<R> h) : Re"
    "sult<R, ThreadFailure>\n    in `std::sync`\n\n    Waits for the thread `h` and gives its result, or its"
    " failure as a value instead of raising it again.\n\n    `Ok` of the thread's result; `Err(ThreadFailur"
    "e)` when the thread faulted or was cancelled, and the\n    failure is then taken, so nothing is raise"
    "d. How a supervisor keeps going when a worker has a bug; `join`\n    raises the failure instead.\n\n   "
    " Example, \"try_join: a contained fault\":\n        Option<i32> none = None;\n        auto h = spawn(Opt"
    "ion::unwrap<i32>, none);\n        match (try_join(h))\n        {\n            Ok(_)  : assert(false),\n "
    "           Err(f) :\n            {\n                String d = ThreadFailure::diagnostic(&f);\n        "
    "        assert(d == \"diag.unwrap-failed\");\n                assert(!ThreadFailure::is_cancelled(&f));"
    "\n            },\n        }\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::sync\u{1f}is_finished\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn is_finished<R>(ref<handle<R>, shared>"
    " h) : bool\u{1f}Whether the thread `h` has ended, its result or failure waiting for `join` or `try_join`."
    "\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn is_finished<R>(ref<handle<R>, shared> h) : bool\n    in `std::sync`\n\n    Whether the thre"
    "ad `h` has ended, its result or failure waiting for `join` or `try_join`.\n\n    Never waits and takes"
    " nothing: how a supervisor finds which of its threads to take.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::sync\u{1f}ThreadFailure::text\u{1f}fn\u{1f}ex"
    "port fn ThreadFailure::text(ref<ThreadFailure, shared> f) : String\u{1f}The failure's report, as the prog"
    "ram would have printed it had nothing taken the failure.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn ThreadFailure::text(ref<ThreadFa"
    "ilure, shared> f) : String\n    in `std::sync`\n\n    The failure's report, as the program would have p"
    "rinted it had nothing taken the failure.\n\n    As a fault's report on standard error: its first line "
    "names the diagnostic, its second the location.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::sync\u{1f}ThreadFailure::diagnostic\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Th"
    "readFailure::diagnostic(ref<ThreadFailure, shared> f) : String\u{1f}The name of the failure's diagnostic "
    "alone, such as `diag.index-out-of-bounds` or `diag.thread-cancelled`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn ThreadFailure::diag"
    "nostic(ref<ThreadFailure, shared> f) : String\n    in `std::sync`\n\n    The name of the failure's diag"
    "nostic alone, such as `diag.index-out-of-bounds` or `diag.thread-cancelled`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::sync\u{1f}ThreadFailu"
    "re::is_cancelled\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn ThreadFailure::is_cancelled(ref<ThreadFailure, shared> f) : bool\u{1f}Wheth"
    "er the thread ended because it was cancelled, rather than by a fault of its own.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn ThreadFa"
    "ilure::is_cancelled(ref<ThreadFailure, shared> f) : bool\n    in `std::sync`\n\n    Whether the thread "
    "ended because it was cancelled, rather than by a fault of its own.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::sync\u{1f}Atomic\u{1f}struct\u{1f}export "
    "resource struct Atomic<T>\u{1f}An integer that threads share and change without a lock.\u{1f}\u{1f}export resource "
    "struct Atomic<T>\n    in `std::sync`\n\n    An integer that threads share and change without a lock.\n\n "
    "   Shared by reference, as a `mutex` is: every operation takes `ref<Atomic<T>, shared>`, and each on"
    "e is\n    indivisible and sequentially consistent, so all threads see all operations on all atomics i"
    "n one order.\n    `T` is an integer type of at most 64 bits. For a counter, a flag (an `Atomic<u8>`),"
    " a sequence number or a\n    maximum kept by several threads; state of more than one integer belongs "
    "in a `mutex`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::sync\u{1f}Atomic::new\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Atomic::new<T: integer>(T v) : Atomic<T>\u{1f}A new at"
