    "spinning, waiting for another thread to change something.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn spin_hint()\n    in `std::sync`\n"
    "\n    Tells the processor that this thread is spinning, waiting for another thread to change somethin"
    "g.\n\n    The CPU's pause instruction: it saves power and lets the other hardware thread of the core r"
    "un. Call it in\n    the body of a loop that polls an atomic; `Atomic::wait` blocks instead, for waits"
    " that may be long.\n\n    Example, \"Atomic::fetch_max: extremes and updates\":\n        Atomic<i32> a = "
    "Atomic::new(10: i32);\n        assert(Atomic::fetch_max(&a, 4) == 10);\n        assert(Atomic::fetch_m"
    "ax(&a, 25) == 10);\n        assert(Atomic::fetch_min(&a, 30) == 25);\n        assert(Atomic::fetch_min"
    "(&a, -3) == 25);\n        assert(Atomic::load(&a) == -3);\n        assert(Result::unwrap(Atomic::fetch"
    "_update(&a, [](i32 x) : Option<i32> { Some(x * 2) })) == -3);\n        match (Atomic::fetch_update(&a"
    ", [](i32 x) : Option<i32> { None }))\n        {\n            Ok(_)  : assert(false),\n            Err(v"
    ") : assert(v == -6),\n        }\n\n    Example, \"Atomic::wait: woken by notify_all\":\n        AtomicBool"
    " done = AtomicBool::new(false);\n        {\n            handle<void> h = spawn(move [](ref<AtomicBool,"
    " shared> d)\n            {\n                AtomicBool::store(d, true);\n                AtomicBool::no"
    "tify_all(d);\n            }, &done);\n            AtomicBool::wait(&done, false);\n            join(h);"
    "\n        }\n        assert(AtomicBool::load(&done));\n        assert(AtomicBool::swap(&done, false));\n"
    "\u{1f}\u{1e}std::sync\u{1f}Barrier\u{1f}struct\u{1f}export struct Barrier\u{1f}A meeting point for a fixed number of threads.\u{1f}\u{1f}exp"
    "ort struct Barrier\n    in `std::sync`\n\n    A meeting point for a fixed number of threads.\n\n    Share"
    "d by reference, as a `mutex` is. `Barrier::wait` blocks until `parties` threads have called it, then"
    "\n    releases them all together and is ready for the next round: the phases of a parallel algorithm,"
    " where\n    every thread must finish one before any starts the next.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::sync\u{1f}Barrier::new\u{1f}fn\u{1f}expo"
    "rt fn Barrier::new(usize parties) : Barrier\u{1f}A barrier for `parties` threads.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Barrier::new"
    "(usize parties) : Barrier\n    in `std::sync`\n    requires\n        parties != 0, barrier_zero_parties"
    "\n\n    A barrier for `parties` threads.\n\n    Faults (`barrier_zero_parties`) when `parties` is 0.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}s"
    "td::sync\u{1f}Barrier::wait\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Barrier::wait(ref<Barrier, shared> b) : bool\u{1f}Waits until `partie"
    "s` threads have called it, then lets them all go on.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Barrier::wait(ref<Barrier, shared> b"
    ") : bool\n    in `std::sync`\n\n    Waits until `parties` threads have called it, then lets them all go"
    " on.\n\n    `true` for the last thread to arrive, the one that released the others, and `false` for th"
    "e rest, so one\n    thread of each round can do something once. A wait that fewer threads than `parti"
    "es` can ever reach\n    faults (`deadlock`).\n\n    Example, \"Barrier::wait: rounds, one leader each\":\n"
    "        Barrier b = Barrier::new(4);\n        Atomic<u32> leaders = Atomic::new(0: u32);\n        Atom"
    "ic<u32> seen = Atomic::new(0: u32);\n        Vec<handle<void>> hs = Vec::new();\n        for (u32 i = "
    "0; i < 4; i += 1)\n        {\n            Vec::push(&mut hs, spawn(move [](\n                ref<Barrie"
    "r, shared> b,\n                ref<Atomic<u32>, shared> leaders,\n                ref<Atomic<u32>, sha"
    "red> seen,\n                u32 id,\n            )\n            {\n                for (u32 round = 0; r"
    "ound < 3; round += 1)\n                {\n                    _ = Atomic::fetch_add(seen, 1);\n        "
    "            if (Barrier::wait(b))\n                    {\n                        _ = Atomic::fetch_ad"
    "d(leaders, 1);\n                        assert(Atomic::load(seen) == 4 * (round + 1));   // everyone "
    "wrote before anyone read\n                    }\n                    _ = Barrier::wait(b);            "
    "                     // the read phase ends together too\n                }\n            }, &b, &leade"
    "rs, &seen, i));\n        }\n        foreach (h in hs)\n        {\n            join(h);\n        }\n       "
    " assert(Atomic::load(&leaders) == 3 && Atomic::load(&seen) == 12);\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::sync\u{1f}Semaphore\u{1f}struct\u{1f}expo"
    "rt struct Semaphore\u{1f}A count of permits that threads take and give back.\u{1f}\u{1f}export struct Semaphore\n   "
    " in `std::sync`\n\n    A count of permits that threads take and give back.\n\n    Shared by reference, a"
    "s a `mutex` is. `acquire` takes one permit, waiting while there is none; `release`\n    gives one bac"
    "k, or adds one. It bounds how many threads do something at once (connections open, workers\n    busy)"
    "; made with 0 permits, it hands events from one thread to another, each `release` letting one\n    `a"
    "cquire` through.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::sync\u{1f}Semaphore::new\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Semaphore::new(usize permits) : Semaphore\u{1f}A"
    " semaphore with `permits` permits; 0 is allowed.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Semaphore::new(usize permits) : Semaphor"
    "e\n    in `std::sync`\n\n    A semaphore with `permits` permits; 0 is allowed.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::sync\u{1f}Semaphore::a"
    "cquire\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Semaphore::acquire(ref<Semaphore, shared> s)\u{1f}Takes one permit, waiting while the"
    "re is none.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Semaphore::acquire(ref<Semaphore, shared> s)\n    in `std::sync`\n\n    Takes on"
    "e permit, waiting while there is none.\n\n    Permits are not handed out in arrival order. A wait no t"
    "hread can end faults (`deadlock`).\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::sync\u{1f}Semaphore::try_acquire\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Semaphore::try_ac"
    "quire(ref<Semaphore, shared> s) : bool\u{1f}Takes one permit if one is free, without waiting: `true` when"
    " it did.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Semaphore::try_acquire(ref<Semaphore, shared> s) : bool\n    in `std::sync`\n\n    "
    "Takes one permit if one is free, without waiting: `true` when it did.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::sync\u{1f}Semaphore::release"
    "\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Semaphore::release(ref<Semaphore, shared> s)\u{1f}Gives one permit back, or adds one; a thr"
    "ead waiting in `acquire` wakes.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Semaphore::release(ref<Semaphore, shared> s)\n    in `std:"
    ":sync`\n\n    Gives one permit back, or adds one; a thread waiting in `acquire` wakes.\n\n    Faults (`a"
    "rith_overflow`) when the permits would exceed what `usize` counts.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::sync\u{1f}Semaphore::available\u{1f}"
    "fn\u{1f}export fn Semaphore::available(ref<Semaphore, shared> s) : usize\u{1f}How many permits are free now: a"
    " snapshot another thread may change at once.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Semaphore::available(ref<Semaphore, shared> "
    "s) : usize\n    in `std::sync`\n\n    How many permits are free now: a snapshot another thread may chan"
    "ge at once.\n\n    Example, \"Semaphore: a bound and a hand-over\":\n        Semaphore limit = Semaphore:"
    ":new(2);\n        Atomic<u32> active = Atomic::new(0: u32);\n        Atomic<u32> peak = Atomic::new(0:"
    " u32);\n        Vec<handle<void>> hs = Vec::new();\n        for (u32 i = 0; i < 6; i += 1)\n        {\n "
    "           Vec::push(&mut hs, spawn(move [](\n                ref<Semaphore, shared> limit,\n         "
    "       ref<Atomic<u32>, shared> active,\n                ref<Atomic<u32>, shared> peak,\n            )"
    "\n            {\n                Semaphore::acquire(limit);\n                _ = Atomic::fetch_max(peak"
    ", Atomic::fetch_add(active, 1) + 1);\n                _ = Atomic::fetch_sub(active, 1);\n             "
    "   Semaphore::release(limit);\n            }, &limit, &active, &peak));\n        }\n        foreach (h "
    "in hs)\n        {\n            join(h);\n        }\n        assert(Atomic::load(&peak) <= 2 && Semaphore"
    "::available(&limit) == 2);\n        assert(Semaphore::try_acquire(&limit) && Semaphore::try_acquire(&"
    "limit) && !Semaphore::try_acquire(&limit));\n\n        Semaphore events = Semaphore::new(0);\n        h"
    "andle<u32> h = spawn(move [](ref<Semaphore, shared> e) : u32\n        {\n            Semaphore::acquir"
    "e(e);\n            Semaphore::acquire(e);\n            Semaphore::acquire(e);\n            3\n        },"
    " &events);\n        Semaphore::release(&events);\n        Semaphore::release(&events);\n        Semapho"
    "re::release(&events);\n        assert(join(h) == 3 && Semaphore::available(&events) == 0);\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::syn"
    "c\u{1f}Once\u{1f}struct\u{1f}export struct Once\u{1f}Something done once, by whichever thread gets there first.\u{1f}\u{1f}export "
    "struct Once\n    in `std::sync`\n\n    Something done once, by whichever thread gets there first.\n\n    "
    "Shared by reference, as a `mutex` is. `Once::call(&o, f)` runs `f` the first time any thread calls i"
    "t;\n    every other call, on any thread, returns once that run has finished, without running `f`: ini"
    "tialising\n    what several threads share, lazily and exactly once. Should `f` fault, the `Once` is a"
    "s before, and the\n    next caller runs `f` afresh.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::sync\u{1f}Once::new\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Once::new() : "
    "Once\u{1f}A `Once` whose `f` has not run.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Once::new() : Once\n    in `std::sync`\n\n    A `Once` "
    "whose `f` has not run.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::sync\u{1f}Once::call\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Once::call(ref<Once, shared> o, fn() f)\u{1f}R"
    "uns `f` if no call has run it yet; otherwise waits until the call that is running it has finished.\u{1f}\u{1f}"
    "export fn Once::call(ref<Once, shared> o, fn() f)\n    in `std::sync`\n\n    Runs `f` if no call has ru"
    "n it yet; otherwise waits until the call that is running it has finished.\n\n    `f` runs on the calli"
    "ng thread. After `call` returns, on any thread, `f` has run to its end exactly once\n    (unless it f"
    "aulted, and then the next caller runs it again).\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::sync\u{1f}Once::is_done\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Once::is_don"
    "e(ref<Once, shared> o) : bool\u{1f}Whether `f` has run to its end.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Once::is_done(ref<Once, sha"
    "red> o) : bool\n    in `std::sync`\n\n    Whether `f` has run to its end.\n\n    Example, \"Once::call: on"
    "ce among four threads\":\n        Once o = Once::new();\n        Atomic<u32> runs = Atomic::new(0: u32)"
    ";\n        Vec<handle<bool>> hs = Vec::new();\n        for (u32 i = 0; i < 4; i += 1)\n        {\n      "
    "      Vec::push(&mut hs, spawn(move [](ref<Once, shared> o, ref<Atomic<u32>, shared> runs) : bool\n  "
    "          {\n                Once::call(o, [runs]() { _ = Atomic::fetch_add(runs, 1); });\n           "
    "     Once::is_done(o)\n            }, &o, &runs));\n        }\n        foreach (h in hs)\n        {\n    "
    "        assert(join(h));\n        }\n        assert(Atomic::load(&runs) == 1 && Once::is_done(&o));\n\u{1f}\u{1e}"
    "std::random\u{1f}Rng\u{1f}struct\u{1f}export struct Rng\u{1f}A general-purpose pseudo-random generator: xoshiro256** see"
    "ded through splitmix64.\u{1f}\u{1f}export struct Rng\n    in `std::random`\n\n    A general-purpose pseudo-random"
    " generator: xoshiro256** seeded through splitmix64.\n\n    The same seed gives the same sequence in ev"
    "ery implementation, so a run can be reproduced. Not suitable\n    for cryptographic purposes: its sta"
    "te is recoverable from its output, so it must not produce keys, tokens\n    or nonces; use `os_random"
    "_bytes` for those.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::random\u{1f}Rng::new\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Rng::new(u64 seed) : Rng\u{1f}A generator seeded f"
    "rom `seed`; equal seeds give equal sequences.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Rng::new(u64 seed) : Rng\n    in `std::rando"
    "m`\n\n    A generator seeded from `seed`; equal seeds give equal sequences.\n\n    `Rng::from_os` seeds "
    "one unpredictably instead.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::random\u{1f}Rng::next_u64\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Rng::next_u64(ref<Rng, exclusive"
    "> r) : u64\u{1f}The next 64 pseudo-random bits from `r`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Rng::next_u64(ref<Rng, exclusive> r) "
    ": u64\n    in `std::random`\n\n    The next 64 pseudo-random bits from `r`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::random\u{1f}Rng::below\u{1f}fn"
    "\u{1f}export fn Rng::below(ref<Rng, exclusive> r, u64 n) : u64\u{1f}A pseudo-random number from 0 up to, not i"
    "ncluding, `n`, each value equally likely.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Rng::below(ref<Rng, exclusive> r, u64 n) : u64\n"
    "    in `std::random`\n\n    A pseudo-random number from 0 up to, not including, `n`, each value equall"
    "y likely.\n\n    Unbiased: a draw that would favour some values is rejected and drawn again. Faults (`"
    "div_by_zero`) when\n    `n` is 0.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::random\u{1f}Rng::unit_f64\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Rng::unit_f64(ref<Rng, exc"
    "lusive> r) : f64\u{1f}A pseudo-random `f64` with `0.0 <= x < 1.0`, from the top 53 bits of one draw.\u{1f}\u{1f}exp"
    "ort fn Rng::unit_f64(ref<Rng, exclusive> r) : f64\n    in `std::random`\n\n    A pseudo-random `f64` wi"
    "th `0.0 <= x < 1.0`, from the top 53 bits of one draw.\n\n    Example, \"Rng: reproducible draws in ran"
    "ge\":\n        Rng a = Rng::new(42);\n        Rng b = Rng::new(42);\n        assert(Rng::next_u64(&mut a"
    ") == Rng::next_u64(&mut b));\n        for (usize i = 0; i < 100; i += 1)\n        {\n            assert"
    "(Rng::below(&mut a, 6) < 6);\n            f64 x = Rng::unit_f64(&mut a);\n            assert(x >= 0.0 "
    "&& x < 1.0);\n        }\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::random\u{1f}os_random_bytes\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn os_random_bytes(slice<u8, exclusiv"
    "e> out)\u{1f}Fills `out` with bytes from the operating system's cryptographically secure source.\u{1f}\u{1f}export "
    "fn os_random_bytes(slice<u8, exclusive> out)\n    in `std::random`\n\n    Fills `out` with bytes from t"
    "he operating system's cryptographically secure source.\n\n    Suitable for keys, tokens and nonces, an"
    "d for seeding `Rng`. Faults (`entropy_unavailable`) when the\n    system has no such source.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::r"
    "andom\u{1f}os_random_u64\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn os_random_u64() : u64\u{1f}A `u64` from the operating system's cryptogra"
    "phically secure source.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn os_random_u64() : u64\n    in `std::random`\n\n    A `u64` from the "
    "operating system's cryptographically secure source.\n\n    Faults (`entropy_unavailable`) when the sys"
    "tem has no such source.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::random\u{1f}Rng::from_os\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Rng::from_os() : Rng\u{1f}A generator see"
    "ded from the operating system's secure source, so each run draws a different sequence.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Rn"
    "g::from_os() : Rng\n    in `std::random`\n\n    A generator seeded from the operating system's secure s"
    "ource, so each run draws a different sequence.\n\n    The sequence itself is still `Rng`'s, so it is s"
    "till not for cryptographic purposes.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::random\u{1f}Rng::shuffle\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Rng::shuffle<T>(ref<Rng"
    ", exclusive> r, slice<T, exclusive> s)\u{1f}Puts the elements of `s` in a uniformly random order drawn fr"
    "om `r`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Rng::shuffle<T>(ref<Rng, exclusive> r, slice<T, exclusive> s)\n    in `std::random"
    "`\n\n    Puts the elements of `s` in a uniformly random order drawn from `r`.\n\n    Fisher-Yates over `"
    "Rng::below`; elements are exchanged, never copied. The same seed gives the same order\n    in every i"
    "mplementation.\n\n    Example, \"Rng::shuffle: a Vec through its slice\":\n        Rng r = Rng::new(7);\n "
    "       Vec<i32> v = Vec::new();\n        for (i32 i = 1; i <= 5; i += 1)\n        {\n            Vec::p"
    "ush(&mut v, i);\n        }\n        Rng::shuffle(&mut r, &mut v);\n        assert(Vec::len(&v) == 5 && "
    "Vec::contains(&v, 3));\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::random\u{1f}uuid_v4\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn uuid_v4() : String\u{1f}A version 4 UUID (RFC 9"
    "562) from the operating system's secure source, as 36 lowercase characters.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn uuid_v4() : S"
