    "\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::math\u{1f}is_finite\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn is_finite<T: number>(T x) : bool\u{1f}Whether `x` is neither a NaN no"
    "r an infinity; `true` for every integer.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn is_finite<T: number>(T x) : bool\n    in `std::ma"
    "th`\n\n    Whether `x` is neither a NaN nor an infinity; `true` for every integer.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::math\u{1f}gcd\u{1f}fn\u{1f}"
    "export fn gcd<T: integer>(T a, T b) : T\u{1f}The greatest common divisor of `a` and `b`, never negative; "
    "`gcd(0, 0)` is 0.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn gcd<T: integer>(T a, T b) : T\n    in `std::math`\n\n    The greatest comm"
    "on divisor of `a` and `b`, never negative; `gcd(0, 0)` is 0.\n\n    Euclid's algorithm over the magnit"
    "udes, so a signed type's minimum faults (`arith_overflow`) as in `abs`.\n\n    Example, \"gcd: with cla"
    "mp, pow, abs and the float tests\":\n        assert(gcd(-12, 18) == 6);\n        assert(gcd(0, 0) == 0)"
    ";\n        assert(clamp(15, 0, 10) == 10 && clamp(-3, 0, 10) == 0);\n        assert(pow(3, 4) == 81 &&"
    " pow(7, 0) == 1);\n        assert(abs(-0.0) == 0.0 && is_nan(0.0 / 0.0) && !is_finite(1.0 / 0.0));\n\u{1f}\u{1e}"
    "std::math\u{1f}BigUint\u{1f}struct\u{1f}export struct BigUint\u{1f}An unsigned integer of any size, for public-key arith"
    "metic and numbers too large for `u128`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export struct BigUint\n    in `std::math`\n\n    An unsigned i"
    "nteger of any size, for public-key arithmetic and numbers too large for `u128`.\n\n    Each operation "
    "gives the exact integer result. The time an operation takes depends on its operands'\n    values, so "
    "a `BigUint` is for public values only, never a private key or anything secret. It owns its\n    digit"
    "s, so a program reassigns one with `overwrite`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::math\u{1f}BigUint::zero\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn BigUint::zero"
    "() : BigUint\u{1f}The number 0.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn BigUint::zero() : BigUint\n    in `std::math`\n\n    The number 0"
    ".\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::math\u{1f}BigUint::from_u64\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn BigUint::from_u64(u64 x) : BigUint\u{1f}The number `x`.\u{1f}\u{1f}exp"
    "ort fn BigUint::from_u64(u64 x) : BigUint\n    in `std::math`\n\n    The number `x`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::math\u{1f}BigUin"
    "t::from_bytes_be\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn BigUint::from_bytes_be(slice<u8, shared> bytes) : BigUint\u{1f}The number w"
    "hose big-endian bytes are `bytes`; leading zero bytes are allowed, and no bytes give 0.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn B"
    "igUint::from_bytes_be(slice<u8, shared> bytes) : BigUint\n    in `std::math`\n\n    The number whose bi"
    "g-endian bytes are `bytes`; leading zero bytes are allowed, and no bytes give 0.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::math\u{1f}BigUint"
    "::to_bytes_be\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn BigUint::to_bytes_be(ref<BigUint, shared> a) : Vec<u8>\u{1f}The big-endian byt"
    "es of `a`, with no leading zero byte; none for zero.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn BigUint::to_bytes_be(ref<BigUint, sh"
    "ared> a) : Vec<u8>\n    in `std::math`\n\n    The big-endian bytes of `a`, with no leading zero byte; n"
    "one for zero.\n\n    `BigUint::to_bytes_be_padded` gives a fixed width instead.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::math\u{1f}BigUint::t"
    "o_bytes_be_padded\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn BigUint::to_bytes_be_padded(ref<BigUint, shared> a, usize width) : Ve"
    "c<u8>\u{1f}The big-endian bytes of `a` in exactly `width` bytes, zeros in front.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn BigUint::to_b"
