    "\u{1e}std::stats\u{1f}sum\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn sum<T: number>(slice<T, shared> data) : T\u{1f}The sum of `data`'s values in"
    " their own type; 0 for an empty slice.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn sum<T: number>(slice<T, shared> data) : T\n    in `"
    "std::stats`\n\n    The sum of `data`'s values in their own type; 0 for an empty slice.\n\n    Added left"
    " to right with `+`, so an integer sum that does not fit in `T` faults (`arith_overflow`),\n    as `+`"
    " does. For the sum as an `f64` whatever `T` is, multiply `mean` by the count.\n\n    Example, \"sum: in"
    " the slice's own type\":\n        array<i32, 4> a = [3, -1, 4, 1];\n        assert(sum(&a) == 7);\n     "
    "   assert(sum(&a[0..0]) == 0);\n        array<f64, 3> f = [0.5, 0.25, 2.0];\n        assert(sum(&f) =="
    " 2.75);\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::stats\u{1f}mean\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn mean<T: number>(slice<T, shared> data) : Option<f64>\u{1f}The arit"
    "hmetic mean of `data`'s values; `None` for an empty slice.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn mean<T: number>(slice<T, share"
    "d> data) : Option<f64>\n    in `std::stats`\n\n    The arithmetic mean of `data`'s values; `None` for a"
    "n empty slice.\n\n    Each value is converted to `f64` with `to_float` and the values added left to ri"
    "ght, then divided by\n    the count. A NaN among the values makes the mean a NaN.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::stats\u{1f}varian"
    "ce\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn variance<T: number>(slice<T, shared> data) : Option<f64>\u{1f}The population variance of "
    "`data`'s values, the mean of the squared deviations from their mean; `None` for an empty slice.\u{1f}\u{1f}exp"
    "ort fn variance<T: number>(slice<T, shared> data) : Option<f64>\n    in `std::stats`\n\n    The populat"
    "ion variance of `data`'s values, the mean of the squared deviations from their mean;\n    `None` for "
    "an empty slice.\n\n    Two passes: the mean first, then the sum of `(x - mean)²` left to right, divid"
    "ed by the count. For\n    the variance of a sample drawn from a larger population, use `sample_varian"
    "ce`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::stats\u{1f}stddev\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn stddev<T: number>(slice<T, shared> data) : Option<f64>\u{1f}The pop"
    "ulation standard deviation of `data`'s values, the square root of `variance`; `None` for an empty sl"
    "ice.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn stddev<T: number>(slice<T, shared> data) : Option<f64>\n    in `std::stats`\n\n    The "
