    "mpty slice.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::stats\u{1f}sample_variance\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn sample_variance<T: number>(slice<T, shared> da"
    "ta) : Option<f64>\u{1f}The sample variance of `data`'s values, the squared deviations from their mean div"
    "ided by one less than the count (Bessel's correction); `None` for fewer than two values.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn "
    "sample_variance<T: number>(slice<T, shared> data) : Option<f64>\n    in `std::stats`\n\n    The sample "
    "variance of `data`'s values, the squared deviations from their mean divided by one less\n    than the"
    " count (Bessel's correction); `None` for fewer than two values.\n\n    For values that are the whole p"
    "opulation, use `variance`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::stats\u{1f}sample_stddev\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn sample_stddev<T: number>(slice<T,"
    " shared> data) : Option<f64>\u{1f}The sample standard deviation of `data`'s values, the square root of `s"
    "ample_variance`; `None` for fewer than two values.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn sample_stddev<T: number>(slice<T, shar"
    "ed> data) : Option<f64>\n    in `std::stats`\n\n    The sample standard deviation of `data`'s values, t"
    "he square root of `sample_variance`; `None` for\n    fewer than two values.\n\n    Example, \"variance: "
    "population and sample\":\n        array<u32, 8> a = [2, 4, 4, 4, 5, 5, 7, 9];\n        assert(Option::u"
    "nwrap(variance(&a)) == 4.0);\n        assert(Option::unwrap(stddev(&a)) == 2.0);\n        assert(Optio"
