    "m sorted, or the mean of the two middle ones\n    when the count is even; `None` for an empty slice.\n"
    "\n    The values are copied, converted to `f64` and sorted as `Vec::sort` sorts floats (every NaN aft"
    "er\n    every number); `data` is not changed.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::stats\u{1f}percentile\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn percentile<T: numb"
    "er>(slice<T, shared> data, f64 p) : Option<f64>\u{1f}The `p`th percentile of `data`'s values, `p` from 0 "
    "to 100, with linear interpolation between the two sorted values it falls between; `None` for an empt"
    "y slice.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn percentile<T: number>(slice<T, shared> data, f64 p) : Option<f64>\n    in `std::s"
    "tats`\n    requires\n        p >= 0.0 && p <= 100.0, assert_failed, \"percentile: `p` is outside 0 to 1"
    "00\"\n\n    The `p`th percentile of `data`'s values, `p` from 0 to 100, with linear interpolation betwe"
    "en the\n    two sorted values it falls between; `None` for an empty slice.\n\n    The position is `(cou"
    "nt - 1) · p / 100` in the sorted values (R's type 7, the default of spreadsheets\n    and NumPy): `p"
    "ercentile(data, 0.0)` is the minimum, `percentile(data, 100.0)` the maximum, and\n    `percentile(dat"
    "a, 50.0)` the median. Faults (`assert_failed`) when `p` is below 0, above 100 or a NaN.\n\n    Example"
    ", \"percentile: interpolated between neighbours\":\n        array<i64, 5> a = [15, 20, 35, 40, 50];\n   "
    "     assert(Option::unwrap(percentile(&a, 25.0)) == 20.0);\n        assert(Option::unwrap(percentile("
    "&a, 40.0)) == 29.0);\n        assert(Option::unwrap(percentile(&a, 50.0)) == 35.0);\n        assert(Op"
    "tion::unwrap(median(&a)) == 35.0);\n        assert(Option::unwrap(median(&a[0..4])) == 27.5);\n       "
    " assert(Option::unwrap(percentile(&a, 0.0)) == 15.0);\n        assert(Option::unwrap(percentile(&a, 1"
    "00.0)) == 50.0);\n        assert(Option::is_none(&median(&a[0..0])));\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::stats\u{1f}minimum\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export "
