    "rror, as `Child::read_output_line` reads standard output.\n\n    Each stream is read ahead on its own."
    "\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::process\u{1f}Child::wait\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Child::wait(ref<Child, exclusive> ch) : Result<i32, FileErr"
    "or>\u{1f}Closes the child's standard input, waits for the child to end and gives its status.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn C"
    "hild::wait(ref<Child, exclusive> ch) : Result<i32, FileError>\n    in `std::process`\n\n    Closes the "
    "child's standard input, waits for the child to end and gives its status.\n\n    The status is `Output:"
    ":status`'s. Asked again, it gives the same status.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::process\u{1f}Child::try_wait\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Child"
    "::try_wait(ref<Child, exclusive> ch) : Result<Option<i32>, FileError>\u{1f}The child's status if it has e"
    "nded, without waiting.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Child::try_wait(ref<Child, exclusive> ch) : Result<Option<i32>, Fi"
    "leError>\n    in `std::process`\n\n    The child's status if it has ended, without waiting.\n\n    `Ok(No"
    "ne)` while it runs.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::process\u{1f}Child::kill\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Child::kill(ref<Child, exclusive> ch) : "
    "Result<void, FileError>\u{1f}Ends the child at once (SIGKILL on Unix, TerminateProcess on Windows).\u{1f}\u{1f}expo"
    "rt fn Child::kill(ref<Child, exclusive> ch) : Result<void, FileError>\n    in `std::process`\n\n    End"
    "s the child at once (SIGKILL on Unix, TerminateProcess on Windows).\n\n    `Child::wait` then gives it"
    "s status. Nothing happens to a child that has already ended. Use\n    `Child::terminate` to let the c"
    "hild stop cleanly, and `Child::kill_tree` to end the processes it started\n    too.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::process\u{1f}Ch"
    "ild::kill_tree\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Child::kill_tree(ref<Child, exclusive> ch) : Result<void, FileError>\u{1f}End"
    "s the child and every process it started, and theirs in turn.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Child::kill_tree(ref<Child,"
    " exclusive> ch) : Result<void, FileError>\n    in `std::process`\n\n    Ends the child and every proces"
    "s it started, and theirs in turn.\n\n    On Linux the processes are found from `/proc`; on Windows by "
    "`taskkill /T`; elsewhere only the child is\n    ended, as `Child::kill` ends it. `Child::wait` then g"
    "ives its status.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::process\u{1f}Child::terminate\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Child::terminate(ref<Child, exclusive>"
    " ch) : Result<void, FileError>\u{1f}Asks the child to end: SIGTERM on Unix, which a program may catch to "
    "stop cleanly.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Child::terminate(ref<Child, exclusive> ch) : Result<void, FileError>\n    in"
    " `std::process`\n\n    Asks the child to end: SIGTERM on Unix, which a program may catch to stop clean"
    "ly.\n\n    On Windows it ends the child as `Child::kill` does. On Unix the status `Child::wait` then g"
    "ives is -15,\n    unless the child handles the signal. Nothing happens, and `Ok(())` is returned, for"
    " a child that has\n    already ended.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::process\u{1f}Child::drop\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Child::drop(ref<Child, "
    "exclusive> self)\u{1f}Closes the child's pipes when its `Child` is destroyed, leaving the child running.\u{1f}"
    "\u{1f}export fn Child::drop(ref<Child, exclusive> self)\n    in `std::process`\n\n    Closes the child's pip"
    "es when its `Child` is destroyed, leaving the child running.\n\n    The destructor; programs do not ca"
    "ll it.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::process\u{1f}ChildInput\u{1f}struct\u{1f}export resource struct ChildInput\u{1f}A child's standard input a"
    "s a value of its own, taken out of its `Child` by `Child::take_input`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export resource struct Child"
    "Input\n    in `std::process`\n\n    A child's standard input as a value of its own, taken out of its `C"
    "hild` by `Child::take_input`.\n\n    It is independent of the `Child` and of the child's output, and o"
    "utlives the `Child`, so one thread can\n    write a child's input while another reads its output (or "
    "one child's output can feed another's input).\n    Destroying it closes the pipe, and the child readi"
    "ng its input then finds its end.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::process\u{1f}ChildOutput\u{1f}struct\u{1f}export resource struct ChildOutpu"
    "t\u{1f}A child's standard output as a value of its own, taken out of its `Child` by `Child::take_output`."
    "\u{1f}\u{1f}export resource struct ChildOutput\n    in `std::process`\n\n    A child's standard output as a value"
    " of its own, taken out of its `Child` by `Child::take_output`.\n\n    It is independent of the `Child`"
    " and of the child's input, and outlives the `Child`. Destroying it closes\n    the pipe.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::proce"
    "ss\u{1f}Child::take_input\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Child::take_input(ref<Child, exclusive> ch) : Option<ChildInput>\u{1f}T"
    "he child's standard input, moved out of the `Child`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Child::take_input(ref<Child, exclusi"
    "ve> ch) : Option<ChildInput>\n    in `std::process`\n\n    The child's standard input, moved out of the"
    " `Child`.\n\n    `Child::write_input` and `Child::close_input` then do nothing. `None` when the input "
