    "ef<Child, exclusive> ch) : Option<ChildOutput>\u{1f}The child's standard output, moved out of the `Child`"
    " with whatever was read ahead.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Child::take_output(ref<Child, exclusive> ch) : Option<Chil"
    "dOutput>\n    in `std::process`\n\n    The child's standard output, moved out of the `Child` with whate"
    "ver was read ahead.\n\n    `Child::read_output` then finds the end. `None` when the output was taken a"
    "lready.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::process\u{1f}ChildInput::write\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn ChildInput::write(ref<ChildInput, exclusive> p"
    ", slice<u8, shared> data) : Result<void, FileError>\u{1f}Writes all of `data` to the child's standard inp"
    "ut, as `Child::write_input` does.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn ChildInput::write(ref<ChildInput, exclusive> p, slice<u"
    "8, shared> data) : Result<void, FileError>\n    in `std::process`\n\n    Writes all of `data` to the ch"
    "ild's standard input, as `Child::write_input` does.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::process\u{1f}ChildInput::drop\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Chi"
    "ldInput::drop(ref<ChildInput, exclusive> self)\u{1f}Closes the pipe when its `ChildInput` is destroyed, s"
    "o the child reads the end of its input.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn ChildInput::drop(ref<ChildInput, exclusive> self)"
    "\n    in `std::process`\n\n    Closes the pipe when its `ChildInput` is destroyed, so the child reads t"
    "he end of its input.\n\n    The destructor; programs do not call it.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::process\u{1f}ChildOutput::read\u{1f}"
    "fn\u{1f}export fn ChildOutput::read(ref<ChildOutput, exclusive> p, ref<Vec<u8>, exclusive> buf, usize max"
    ") : Result<usize, FileError>\u{1f}Appends to `buf` what has arrived on the child's standard output, up to"
    " `max` bytes, and returns how many.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn ChildOutput::read(ref<ChildOutput, exclusive> p, ref<"
    "Vec<u8>, exclusive> buf, usize max) : Result<usize, FileError>\n    in `std::process`\n\n    Appends to"
    " `buf` what has arrived on the child's standard output, up to `max` bytes, and returns how many.\n\n  "
    "  As `Child::read_output`: at most a MiB at a time, and `Ok(0)` (for a `max` above 0) only at the en"
    "d.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::process\u{1f}ChildOutput::read_line\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn ChildOutput::read_line(ref<ChildOutput, exclus"
    "ive> p) : Result<Option<String>, FileError>\u{1f}The next line of the child's standard output, as `Child:"
    ":read_output_line` reads it.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn ChildOutput::read_line(ref<ChildOutput, exclusive> p) : Resu"
    "lt<Option<String>, FileError>\n    in `std::process`\n\n    The next line of the child's standard outpu"
    "t, as `Child::read_output_line` reads it.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::process\u{1f}ChildOutput::drop\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn ChildOutput:"
