    " fn ChildOutput::drop(ref<ChildOutput, exclusive> self)\n    in `std::process`\n\n    Closes the pipe w"
    "hen its `ChildOutput` is destroyed.\n\n    The destructor; programs do not call it.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::process\u{1f}pro"
    "cess_id\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn process_id() : u64\u{1f}The operating system's number for this program (its process "
    "id), as a pid file records it.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn process_id() : u64\n    in `std::process`\n\n    The operatin"
    "g system's number for this program (its process id), as a pid file records it.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::process\u{1f}watch_"
    "interrupts\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn watch_interrupts()\u{1f}From now on, makes an interrupt set the flag `interrupt_r"
    "equested` reads instead of ending the program.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn watch_interrupts()\n    in `std::process`\n\n"
    "    From now on, makes an interrupt set the flag `interrupt_requested` reads instead of ending the p"
    "rogram.\n\n    An interrupt is SIGINT or SIGTERM on Unix; Ctrl-C, Ctrl-Break or closing the console on"
    " Windows. A\n    blocking `std` call an interrupt arrives in may return early (`accept` and a socket'"
    "s `read` give\n    `Err(TimedOut)`), so a long-running loop checks the flag and stops cleanly. There "
    "is no callback.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::process\u{1f}interrupt_requested\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn interrupt_requested() : bool\u{1f}Whether"
    " an interrupt has arrived since `watch_interrupts` was called.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn interrupt_requested() : bo"
    "ol\n    in `std::process`\n\n    Whether an interrupt has arrived since `watch_interrupts` was called.\n"
    "\u{1f}\u{1e}std::net\u{1f}IpAddr\u{1f}enum\u{1f}export enum IpAddr\u{1f}An IP address: IPv4 (`V4`, four bytes) or IPv6 (`V6`, sixt"
    "een bytes).\u{1f}\u{1f}export enum IpAddr\n    in `std::net`\n\n    An IP address: IPv4 (`V4`, four bytes) or IPv"
    "6 (`V6`, sixteen bytes).\n\n    The bytes are in the order the text writes them: `127.0.0.1` is `V4([1"
    "27, 0, 0, 1])`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::net\u{1f}SocketAddr\u{1f}struct\u{1f}export struct SocketAddr\u{1f}An IP address and a port: wher"
    "e a socket is bound or connected.\u{1f}\u{1f}export struct SocketAddr\n    in `std::net`\n\n    An IP address and"
    " a port: where a socket is bound or connected.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::net\u{1f}NetError\u{1f}enum\u{1f}export enum NetError\u{1f}Why a s"
    "ocket operation failed.\u{1f}\u{1f}export enum NetError\n    in `std::net`\n\n    Why a socket operation failed.\n"
    "\n    - `Refused`: nothing listens at the address connected to.\n    - `Reset`: the peer reset the con"
    "nection.\n    - `TimedOut`: the socket's timeout passed; the socket is still usable.\n    - `Unreachab"
    "le`: the address cannot be reached.\n    - `AddrInUse`: the address to bind is already in use.\n    - "
    "`AddrNotAvailable`: the address to bind cannot be used on this machine.\n    - `UnknownHost`: the nam"
    "e resolves to nothing or cannot be resolved.\n    - `NotPermitted`: the system denied permission.\n   "
    " - `Closed`: the peer has gone while writing, or a `read_exact` was cut short.\n    - `Failed`: any o"
    "ther failure.\n    - `NotUtf8(e)`: a line `read_line` read is not UTF-8.\n\n    No variant shares a nam"
    "e with `FileError`'s, so either may be written unqualified.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::net\u{1f}NetError::text\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn N"
    "etError::text(ref<NetError, shared> e) : str\u{1f}A short description of the error, in lower case, for me"
    "ssages.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn NetError::text(ref<NetError, shared> e) : str\n    in `std::net`\n\n    A short desc"
    "ription of the error, in lower case, for messages.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::net\u{1f}IpAddr::localhost_v4\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn IpAd"
    "dr::localhost_v4() : IpAddr\u{1f}The IPv4 loopback address, `127.0.0.1`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn IpAddr::localhost_v4("
    ") : IpAddr\n    in `std::net`\n\n    The IPv4 loopback address, `127.0.0.1`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::net\u{1f}IpAddr::unspeci"
