    ") : SocketAddr\n    in `std::net`\n\n    The socket address of `ip` and `port`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::net\u{1f}IpAddr::pars"
    "e\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn IpAddr::parse(StringView text) : Result<IpAddr, ParseError>\u{1f}Reads an IP address from "
    "its text, as the platform's library does.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn IpAddr::parse(StringView text) : Result<IpAddr,"
    " ParseError>\n    in `std::net`\n\n    Reads an IP address from its text, as the platform's library doe"
    "s.\n\n    Accepts dotted decimal (`127.0.0.1`) and RFC 4291 IPv6 with `::` (`::1`, `2001:db8::8a2e:370"
    ":7334`,\n    `::ffff:192.0.2.1`), without brackets or a port. `Err(Empty)` for \"\", `Err(Invalid(0))` "
    "for any other\n    text that is not an address.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::net\u{1f}IpAddr::text\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn IpAddr::text(ref"
    "<IpAddr, shared> ip) : String\u{1f}The address as text: dotted decimal, or IPv6 in RFC 5952's shortest fo"
    "rm (`::1`).\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn IpAddr::text(ref<IpAddr, shared> ip) : String\n    in `std::net`\n\n    The addr"
    "ess as text: dotted decimal, or IPv6 in RFC 5952's shortest form (`::1`).\n\n    Example, \"IpAddr::tex"
    "t: IPv6 in its shortest form\":\n        IpAddr ip = Result::unwrap(IpAddr::parse(\"2001:db8:0:0:0:0:0:"
    "1\"));\n        assert(IpAddr::text(&ip) == \"2001:db8::1\");\n        assert(IpAddr::text(&IpAddr::local"
    "host_v4()) == \"127.0.0.1\");\n        assert(Result::is_err(&IpAddr::parse(\"256.0.0.1\")));\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::net\u{1f}"
    "SocketAddr::parse\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn SocketAddr::parse(StringView text) : Result<SocketAddr, ParseError>\u{1f}R"
    "eads an address and a port written `a.b.c.d:port` or `[v6]:port`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn SocketAddr::parse(Strin"
    "gView text) : Result<SocketAddr, ParseError>\n    in `std::net`\n\n    Reads an address and a port writ"
    "ten `a.b.c.d:port` or `[v6]:port`.\n\n    - `Err(Empty)` for \"\".\n    - `Err(Invalid(i))` at the first "
    "byte that does not fit; `i` is the address's first byte when the\n      address is not one (an IPv6 a"
    "ddress must be in brackets, an IPv4 address must not).\n    - `Err(OutOfRange)` for a port above 6553"
    "5.\n\n    Example, \"SocketAddr::parse: IPv6 needs brackets\":\n        SocketAddr a = Result::unwrap(Soc"
    "ketAddr::parse(\"[::1]:8080\"));\n        assert(a.port == 8080);\n        assert(SocketAddr::text(&a) ="
    "= \"[::1]:8080\");\n        match (SocketAddr::parse(\"::1:8080\"))\n        {\n            Err(Invalid(i))"
    " : assert(i == 0),\n            _               : assert(false),\n        }\n        assert(Result::is_"
    "err(&SocketAddr::parse(\"127.0.0.1:70000\")));\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::net\u{1f}SocketAddr::text\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn SocketAddr::te"
    "xt(ref<SocketAddr, shared> a) : String\u{1f}The address and port as text, in the forms `SocketAddr::parse"
    "` reads: `127.0.0.1:8080`, `[::1]:8080`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn SocketAddr::text(ref<SocketAddr, shared> a) : St"
    "ring\n    in `std::net`\n\n    The address and port as text, in the forms `SocketAddr::parse` reads: `1"
    "27.0.0.1:8080`, `[::1]:8080`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::net\u{1f}resolve\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn resolve(StringView host, u16 port) : R"
    "esult<Vec<SocketAddr>, NetError>\u{1f}The socket addresses `host` names, each with `port`, through the sy"
    "stem's resolver.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn resolve(StringView host, u16 port) : Result<Vec<SocketAddr>, NetError>\n "
    "   in `std::net`\n\n    The socket addresses `host` names, each with `port`, through the system's reso"
    "lver.\n\n    The resolver reads its hosts file, then DNS, and the addresses come in its order; \"localh"
    "ost\" resolves\n    without a network. `Err(UnknownHost)` when the name resolves to nothing or cannot "
    "be resolved. The call\n    blocks until the resolver answers.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::net\u{1f}TcpListener\u{1f}struct\u{1f}export re"
    "source struct TcpListener\u{1f}A socket that listens for TCP connections; `accept` gives each one as a `T"
    "cpStream`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export resource struct TcpListener\n    in `std::net`\n\n    A socket that listens for TCP "
    "connections; `accept` gives each one as a `TcpStream`.\n\n    Dropping it closes the socket.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::ne"
    "t\u{1f}TcpStream\u{1f}struct\u{1f}export resource struct TcpStream\u{1f}A TCP connection: a stream of bytes each way.\u{1f}\u{1f}e"
    "xport resource struct TcpStream\n    in `std::net`\n\n    A TCP connection: a stream of bytes each way."
    "\n\n    The bytes on the wire are exactly those written, in order, with no framing or encoding added, "
    "and a\n    `read` gives whatever part of them has arrived. Calls block until they complete or the str"
    "eam's timeout\n    passes (`set_read_timeout_ms`, `set_write_timeout_ms`). Dropping the stream closes"
    " it; the connection\n    closes when the last stream on it (`try_clone`) is dropped. Formatted text i"
    "s sent with\n    `TcpStream::printf(s, format, …)`, as `File::printf` writes to a file.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::net\u{1f}"
    "TcpListener::bind\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn TcpListener::bind(SocketAddr a) : Result<TcpListener, NetError>\u{1f}Liste"
    "ns for TCP connections at `a`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn TcpListener::bind(SocketAddr a) : Result<TcpListener, NetE"
    "rror>\n    in `std::net`\n\n    Listens for TCP connections at `a`.\n\n    Port 0 asks the system for a f"
    "ree port, which `local_addr` names. `Err(AddrInUse)`,\n    `Err(AddrNotAvailable)` or `Err(NotPermitt"
    "ed)` when the address cannot be bound.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::net\u{1f}TcpListener::local_addr\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn TcpListener::"
    "local_addr(ref<TcpListener, shared> l) : SocketAddr\u{1f}The address the listener is bound to, with the p"
    "ort the system chose when `bind` asked for port 0.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn TcpListener::local_addr(ref<TcpListene"
    "r, shared> l) : SocketAddr\n    in `std::net`\n\n    The address the listener is bound to, with the por"
    "t the system chose when `bind` asked for port 0.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::net\u{1f}TcpListener::set_accept_timeout_ms\u{1f}fn\u{1f}ex"
    "port fn TcpListener::set_accept_timeout_ms(ref<TcpListener, exclusive> l, u64 ms)\u{1f}Sets how long `acc"
    "ept` waits for a connection, in milliseconds; 0 waits for ever.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn TcpListener::set_accept_t"
    "imeout_ms(ref<TcpListener, exclusive> l, u64 ms)\n    in `std::net`\n\n    Sets how long `accept` waits"
    " for a connection, in milliseconds; 0 waits for ever.\n\n    After the timeout `accept` gives `Err(Tim"
    "edOut)` and the listener is still usable. A server loop that\n    checks `interrupt_requested()` sets"
    " one.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::net\u{1f}TcpListener::accept\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn TcpListener::accept(ref<TcpListener, exclusive> l)"
    " : Result<TcpStream, NetError>\u{1f}Waits for the next connection made to the listener and gives its stre"
    "am.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn TcpListener::accept(ref<TcpListener, exclusive> l) : Result<TcpStream, NetError>\n    "
    "in `std::net`\n\n    Waits for the next connection made to the listener and gives its stream.\n\n    `Er"
    "r(TimedOut)` when the accept timeout (`set_accept_timeout_ms`) passes first.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::net\u{1f}TcpListener:"
    ":drop\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn TcpListener::drop(ref<TcpListener, exclusive> self)\u{1f}Closes the listening socket; "
    "run when a `TcpListener` is dropped.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn TcpListener::drop(ref<TcpListener, exclusive> self)\n"
    "    in `std::net`\n\n    Closes the listening socket; run when a `TcpListener` is dropped.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::net\u{1f}"
