    "<TcpStream, NetError>\n    in `std::net`\n\n    Connects to `a`, waiting as long as the system does.\n\n "
    "   `Err(Refused)` when nothing listens there, `Err(TimedOut)`, `Err(Unreachable)`. `connect_timeout`"
    "\n    bounds the wait.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::net\u{1f}TcpStream::connect_timeout\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn TcpStream::connect_timeout("
    "SocketAddr a, u64 ms) : Result<TcpStream, NetError>\u{1f}Connects to `a`, waiting at most `ms` millisecon"
    "ds.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn TcpStream::connect_timeout(SocketAddr a, u64 ms) : Result<TcpStream, NetError>\n    in"
    " `std::net`\n\n    Connects to `a`, waiting at most `ms` milliseconds.\n\n    `Err(TimedOut)` when the t"
    "ime passes first; an `ms` of 0 is taken as 1. Other errors as `connect`'s.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::net\u{1f}TcpStream::pee"
    "r_addr\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn TcpStream::peer_addr(ref<TcpStream, shared> s) : SocketAddr\u{1f}The address of the o"
    "ther end of the connection.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn TcpStream::peer_addr(ref<TcpStream, shared> s) : SocketAddr\n "
    "   in `std::net`\n\n    The address of the other end of the connection.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::net\u{1f}TcpStream::local_ad"
