    "\u{1f}TcpStream::set_keepalive\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn TcpStream::set_keepalive(ref<TcpStream, exclusive> s, bool on"
    ")\u{1f}Turns TCP keepalive on or off for the connection.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn TcpStream::set_keepalive(ref<TcpStrea"
    "m, exclusive> s, bool on)\n    in `std::net`\n\n    Turns TCP keepalive on or off for the connection.\n\n"
    "    With it on, the system probes an idle connection by its own schedule (after a couple of hours, b"
    "y\n    default), so a peer or a path that has silently gone makes a later read fail rather than wait "
