    "<u8, shared> data) : u32\u{1f}The CRC-32 checksum of `data`, as zlib, PNG, gzip and Ethernet compute it.\u{1f}"
    "\u{1f}export fn crc32(slice<u8, shared> data) : u32\n    in `std::crypto::digest`\n\n    The CRC-32 checksum"
    " of `data`, as zlib, PNG, gzip and Ethernet compute it.\n\n    CRC-32/IEEE: polynomial 0x04C11DB7 (ref"
    "lected 0xEDB88320), initial value and final exclusive or\n    0xFFFFFFFF, input and output reflected;"
    " computed bit by bit.\n\n    It is not cryptographic: it detects accidental corruption, and anyone can"
    " make data with any CRC they\n    choose. To detect tampering, use a hash or a MAC.\n\n    Example, \"cr"
    "c32: the check value\":\n        assert(crc32(b\"123456789\") == 0xCBF43926);\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::crypto::digest\u{1f}dige"
    "st_eq\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn digest_eq(slice<u8, shared> a, slice<u8, shared> b) : bool\u{1f}Whether `a` and `b` ha"
    "ve the same length and the same bytes, in a time that depends on the lengths alone.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn diges"
    "t_eq(slice<u8, shared> a, slice<u8, shared> b) : bool\n    in `std::crypto::digest`\n\n    Whether `a` "
    "and `b` have the same length and the same bytes, in a time that depends on the lengths alone.\n\n    E"
    "very byte is compared, however early they differ, so a sender guessing a MAC learns nothing from how"
