    "d::crypto::pk`\n\n    Whether `signature` is `public_key`'s Ed25519 signature (RFC 8032 §5.1.7) of `m"
    "essage`.\n\n    True exactly when `public_key` and `signature` are 32 and 64 bytes, the key and R (the"
    " signature's first\n    32 bytes) are canonical point encodings, S (the rest, little-endian) is below"
    " L, and S·B = R + k·A with k\n    = SHA-512(R ‖ A ‖ `message`) mod L. Anything else, a wrong le"
    "ngth included, is `false`. Not constant-time,\n    and need not be: it uses public values only.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std"
    "::crypto::pk\u{1f}RsaPrivateKey\u{1f}struct\u{1f}export struct RsaPrivateKey\u{1f}An RSA private key: the modulus `n`, t"
    "he public exponent `e`, the private exponent `d` and the primes `p` and `q`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export struct RsaPriva"
    "teKey\n    in `std::crypto::pk`\n\n    An RSA private key: the modulus `n`, the public exponent `e`, th"
    "e private exponent `d` and the primes `p`\n    and `q`.\n\n    Made by `RsaPrivateKey::new`, `rsa_gener"
    "ate_key` or `PrivateKey::from_der`; it also holds the\n    Chinese-remainder values the private opera"
    "tion uses. Signing computes m^d mod n modulo `p` and `q` with a\n    constant-time exponentiation and"
    " checks the result with `e`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::crypto::pk\u{1f}RsaPrivateKey::new\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn RsaPrivateKey::new(Bi"
    "gUint n, BigUint e, BigUint d, BigUint p, BigUint q) : Option<RsaPrivateKey>\u{1f}The private key with th"
    "ese parts, or `None` when they do not fit together.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn RsaPrivateKey::new(BigUint n, BigUint"
    " e, BigUint d, BigUint p, BigUint q) : Option<RsaPrivateKey>\n    in `std::crypto::pk`\n\n    The priva"
    "te key with these parts, or `None` when they do not fit together.\n\n    They fit when `p` and `q` are"
    " odd and above 2, `p`·`q` = `n`, and `e`·`d` ≡ 1 modulo `p` - 1 and modulo\n    `q` - 1.\n\n    Exa"
    "mple, \"RsaPrivateKey::new: parts that do not fit are refused\":\n        BigUint n = BigUint::from_u64"
    "(3233);\n        BigUint e = BigUint::from_u64(17);\n        BigUint p = BigUint::from_u64(61);\n      "
    "  BigUint q = BigUint::from_u64(53);\n        Option<RsaPrivateKey> good = RsaPrivateKey::new(n, e, B"
    "igUint::from_u64(2753), p, q);\n        assert(Option::is_some(&good));\n        Option<RsaPrivateKey>"
    " bad = RsaPrivateKey::new(\n            BigUint::from_u64(3233),\n            BigUint::from_u64(17),\n "
    "           BigUint::from_u64(2754),\n            BigUint::from_u64(61),\n            BigUint::from_u64"
    "(53),\n        );\n        assert(Option::is_none(&bad));\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::crypto::pk\u{1f}RsaPrivateKey::public_key\u{1f}"
    "fn\u{1f}export fn RsaPrivateKey::public_key(ref<RsaPrivateKey, shared> key) : RsaPublicKey\u{1f}The public hal"
    "f of `key`: its modulus and public exponent.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn RsaPrivateKey::public_key(ref<RsaPrivateKey,"
