    "oo short for two digests and two bytes.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::crypto::pk\u{1f}rsa_generate_key\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn rsa_generate"
    "_key(usize bits) : RsaPrivateKey\u{1f}A new RSA private key of `bits` bits, with the public exponent 6553"
    "7.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn rsa_generate_key(usize bits) : RsaPrivateKey\n    in `std::crypto::pk`\n\n    A new RSA p"
    "rivate key of `bits` bits, with the public exponent 65537.\n\n    n = p·q has exactly `bits` bits; p "
    "and q are distinct primes of `bits`/2 bits from `os_random_bytes`,\n    found by trial division by th"
    "e primes below 1000 and five rounds of Miller–Rabin with random bases (FIPS\n    186-4 B.3.3), with"
    " p - 1 and q - 1 prime to e. Faults (`crypto_length`) when `bits` is below 1024, above\n    8192 or n"
    "ot a multiple of 64. Slow under an interpreter, as every key generation is.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::x509\u{1f}CertError\u{1f}en"
    "um\u{1f}export enum CertError\u{1f}Why a certificate, a chain or a key was refused.\u{1f}\u{1f}export enum CertError\n   "
    " in `std::x509`\n\n    Why a certificate, a chain or a key was refused.\n\n    - `BadEncoding`: the DER "
    "or PEM is malformed, or is not what was asked for.\n    - `Expired`: a certificate's validity ended b"
    "efore the time checked.\n    - `NotYetValid`: a certificate's validity begins after the time checked."
    "\n    - `UnknownAuthority`: no chain from the leaf reaches a trusted root.\n    - `HostMismatch`: the "
