    "ad(slice<u8, shared> buf, usize at) : Option<Der>\u{1f}The DER element at `at` in `buf`, or `None` when i"
    "t is not well-formed.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn der_read(slice<u8, shared> buf, usize at) : Option<Der>\n    in `std"
    "::x509`\n\n    The DER element at `at` in `buf`, or `None` when it is not well-formed.\n\n    Well-forme"
    "d means a single-byte tag, the shortest length form, at most four length bytes, no indefinite\n    le"
    "ngth, and contents inside `buf`. Read an element's first child by calling it again at `start`, and t"
    "he\n    element after it at `next`.\n\n    Example, \"der_read: an element, its child, and a long form r"
    "efused\":\n        array<u8, 5> der = [0x30, 0x03, 0x02, 0x01, 0x05];\n        Der seq = Option::unwrap"
    "(der_read(&der, 0));\n        assert(seq.tag == 0x30 && seq.start == 2 && seq.end == 5 && seq.next =="
    " 5);\n        Der int = Option::unwrap(der_read(&der, seq.start));\n        assert(int.tag == 0x02 && "
    "der[int.start] == 5);\n        array<u8, 4> long_form = [0x04, 0x81, 0x01, 0x00];\n        assert(Opti"
    "on::is_none(&der_read(&long_form, 0)));\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::x509\u{1f}EcPublicKey\u{1f}struct\u{1f}export struct EcPublicKey\u{1f}An "
