    "h`.\n    - `RsaPss(h)`: RSASSA-PSS over `h`, with MGF1 over `h` and a salt as long as its digest.\n   "
    " - `Ecdsa(h)`: ECDSA over `h`.\n    - `Ed25519`: Ed25519, over the message itself.\n    - `Unsupported"
    "Signature`: another algorithm; nothing verifies or signs with it.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::x509\u{1f}Certificate\u{1f}struct\u{1f}exp"
    "ort struct Certificate\u{1f}A parsed X.509 certificate (RFC 5280), v3 or older.\u{1f}\u{1f}export struct Certificat"
    "e\n    in `std::x509`\n\n    A parsed X.509 certificate (RFC 5280), v3 or older.\n\n    - `der`: the whol"
    "e certificate; `tbs`: the signed part; `signature`: the signature over `tbs`, made with\n      `schem"
    "e`.\n    - `issuer`, `subject`: the names' DER, compared whole.\n    - `common_name`: the subject's la"
    "st common name, empty when there is none; host matching does not consult\n      it.\n    - `not_before"
    "`, `not_after`: the validity.\n    - `dns_names`, `ip_addresses`: the subject alternative names' DNS "
    "names and IP addresses.\n    - `is_ca`, `max_path_len`: the basic constraints; `max_path_len` is -1 w"
    "hen there is no limit.\n    - `can_sign_certificates`: key usage's keyCertSign, `true` when there is "
    "no key usage.\n    - `server_auth`: extended key usage allows server authentication or any use, `true"
    "` when there is no\n      extended key usage.\n    - `unhandled_critical`: a critical extension other "
    "than certificate policies or name constraints was not\n      understood, so the certificate is not us"
    "able.\n    - `key`: the subject's public key.\n\n    Not independently audited: `std::x509` is implemen"
    "ted to the standards its documentation names, tested\n    against OpenSSL, and fuzzed continuously, b"
    "ut it has not been independently audited.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::x509\u{1f}Certificate::parse\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Certificate::p"
    "arse(slice<u8, shared> der) : Result<Certificate, CertError>\u{1f}The certificate whose DER is `der` (RFC"
    " 5280 §4.1), or `Err(BadEncoding)`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Certificate::parse(slice<u8, shared> der) : Result<C"
    "ertificate, CertError>\n    in `std::x509`\n\n    The certificate whose DER is `der` (RFC 5280 §4.1), "
    "or `Err(BadEncoding)`.\n\n    `der` must be exactly one certificate, with its inner and outer signatur"
    "e algorithms equal. UTCTime years\n    50 to 99 are read as 19xx. An unknown key or signature algorit"
    "hm still parses, as `UnsupportedKey` or\n    `UnsupportedSignature`; an unknown critical extension se"
    "ts `unhandled_critical`. An Ed25519 key or\n    signature algorithm (OID 1.3.101.112) is `Ed25519Key`"
    " or `Ed25519`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::x509\u{1f}certificates_from_pem\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn certificates_from_pem(StringView text)"
    " : Vec<Certificate>\u{1f}Every certificate in the PEM `text`, in order: its `-----BEGIN CERTIFICATE-----`"
    " blocks (RFC 7468).\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn certificates_from_pem(StringView text) : Vec<Certificate>\n    in `std"
    "::x509`\n\n    Every certificate in the PEM `text`, in order: its `-----BEGIN CERTIFICATE-----` blocks"
    " (RFC 7468).\n\n    Text between blocks is ignored. A block whose base64 does not decode, that holds a"
    " byte that is not ASCII,\n    or that is not a certificate, is skipped.\n\n    Example, \"certificates_f"
    "rom_pem: a malformed block is skipped\":\n        StringView text = \"junk\\n-----BEGIN CERTIFICATE-----"
    "\\nnot base64!\\n-----END CERTIFICATE-----\\n\";\n        Vec<Certificate> certs = certificates_from_pem("
    "text);\n        assert(Vec::len(&certs) == 0);\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::x509\u{1f}TrustStore\u{1f}struct\u{1f}export struct TrustStore"
    "\u{1f}The root certificates a chain may end at, for `verify_chain`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export struct TrustStore\n    in `std"
    "::x509`\n\n    The root certificates a chain may end at, for `verify_chain`.\n\n    `roots` may be read "
    "and changed directly; `TrustStore::system` reads the operating system's.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::x509\u{1f}TrustStore::new"
    "\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn TrustStore::new() : TrustStore\u{1f}A store with no roots.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn TrustStore::new() : T"
    "rustStore\n    in `std::x509`\n\n    A store with no roots.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::x509\u{1f}TrustStore::add\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Tr"
    "ustStore::add(ref<TrustStore, exclusive> t, Certificate root)\u{1f}Adds `root` to the roots of `t`.\u{1f}\u{1f}expo"
    "rt fn TrustStore::add(ref<TrustStore, exclusive> t, Certificate root)\n    in `std::x509`\n\n    Adds `"
    "root` to the roots of `t`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::x509\u{1f}TrustStore::from_pem_file\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn TrustStore::from_pem_f"
    "ile(StringView path) : Result<TrustStore, FileError>\u{1f}The roots in the PEM file at `path`, such as `/"
    "etc/ssl/certs/ca-certificates.crt`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn TrustStore::from_pem_file(StringView path) : Result<T"
    "rustStore, FileError>\n    in `std::x509`\n\n    The roots in the PEM file at `path`, such as `/etc/ssl"
    "/certs/ca-certificates.crt`.\n\n    Its certificates are read as `certificates_from_pem` reads them. `"
    "Err` with the `FileError` when the file\n    cannot be read.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::x509\u{1f}TrustStore::system\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export"
    " fn TrustStore::system() : Result<TrustStore, FileError>\u{1f}The operating system's roots, from the firs"
    "t of the usual bundle files that holds a certificate.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn TrustStore::system() : Result<Trust"
    "Store, FileError>\n    in `std::x509`\n\n    The operating system's roots, from the first of the usual "
    "bundle files that holds a certificate.\n\n    The files tried, in order: `/etc/ssl/certs/ca-certificat"
    "es.crt` (Debian, Ubuntu),\n    `/etc/pki/tls/certs/ca-bundle.crt` (Fedora, RHEL), `/etc/ssl/ca-bundle"
    ".pem`, `/etc/ssl/cert.pem` (Alpine)\n    and `/usr/local/etc/openssl/cert.pem` (macOS with a package "
    "manager's OpenSSL). `Err(NotFound)` where none\n    does, as on Windows: a program there passes a bun"
    "dle to `TrustStore::from_pem_file`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::x509\u{1f}verify_signature\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn verify_signature(ref<C"
    "ertKey, shared> key, ref<SignatureScheme, shared> scheme, slice<u8, shared> message, slice<u8, share"
    "d> signature) : bool\u{1f}Whether `signature` over `message` verifies under `key` with `scheme`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export "
    "fn verify_signature(ref<CertKey, shared> key, ref<SignatureScheme, shared> scheme, slice<u8, shared>"
    " message, slice<u8, shared> signature) : bool\n    in `std::x509`\n\n    Whether `signature` over `mess"
    "age` verifies under `key` with `scheme`.\n\n    The RSA and ECDSA schemes hash `message` with the sche"
    "me's hash first; Ed25519 checks `message` itself. A\n    key of another kind than the scheme, `Unsupp"
    "ortedKey`, `UnsupportedSignature` or a malformed signature\n    gives `false`. Not constant-time, and"
    " need not be: it uses public values only.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::x509\u{1f}Certificate::matches_host\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Certifi"
    "cate::matches_host(ref<Certificate, shared> c, StringView host) : bool\u{1f}Whether `c` is for `host` (RF"
    "C 6125 §6.4).\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Certificate::matches_host(ref<Certificate, shared> c, StringView host) : b"
    "ool\n    in `std::x509`\n\n    Whether `c` is for `host` (RFC 6125 §6.4).\n\n    An IP address literal i"
    "s compared with the certificate's IP addresses. A name is compared with its DNS\n    names, ignoring "
    "ASCII case and one final dot on `host`; a leading `*.` in a DNS name stands for exactly\n    one whol"
    "e label, and only where at least two labels follow it (so `*.com` matches nothing). The common\n    n"
    "ame is not consulted.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::x509\u{1f}verify_chain\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn verify_chain(ref<Certificate, shared> le"
    "af, slice<Certificate, shared> intermediates, ref<TrustStore, shared> roots, StringView host, ref<Da"
    "teTime, shared> now) : Result<void, CertError>\u{1f}Verifies a TLS server's certificate chain from `leaf`"
    " to one of `roots`, for `host` at the time `now`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn verify_chain(ref<Certificate, shared> l"
    "eaf, slice<Certificate, shared> intermediates, ref<TrustStore, shared> roots, StringView host, ref<D"
    "ateTime, shared> now) : Result<void, CertError>\n    in `std::x509`\n\n    Verifies a TLS server's cert"
    "ificate chain from `leaf` to one of `roots`, for `host` at the time `now`.\n\n    `Ok(())` when the le"
    "af matches `host` (`Certificate::matches_host`), may serve TLS, is in date and usable,\n    and a cha"
    "in of at most 10 certificates exists (RFC 5280 §6, as a client needs it) in which:\n\n    - each cert"
    "ificate is signed by the next, found by issuer name and signature among `intermediates`, in any\n    "
    "  order, or among the roots;\n    - every issuer is a CA allowed to sign certificates, in date, and w"
    "ithin its path length;\n    - the last is one of the roots.\n\n    Otherwise `Err` of the first reason "
    "met: `HostMismatch`, then `WrongUsage`, then `NotYetValid`, `Expired`\n    or `UnhandledCritical` for"
    " the leaf, then the chain's (`UnknownAuthority`, `BadSignature`, `NotAuthority`,\n    `NotYetValid`, "
    "`Expired`, `UnhandledCritical` or `ChainTooLong`).\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::x509\u{1f}CertKey::to_der\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn CertKey:"
    ":to_der(ref<CertKey, shared> key) : Option<Vec<u8>>\u{1f}The DER SubjectPublicKeyInfo of `key`, or `None`"
    " for `UnsupportedKey`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn CertKey::to_der(ref<CertKey, shared> key) : Option<Vec<u8>>\n    in"
    " `std::x509`\n\n    The DER SubjectPublicKeyInfo of `key`, or `None` for `UnsupportedKey`.\n\n    `CertK"
    "ey::from_der` reads it back.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::x509\u{1f}CertKey::from_der\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn CertKey::from_der(slice<u8, "
    "shared> der) : Result<CertKey, CertError>\u{1f}The public key of the DER SubjectPublicKeyInfo `der`.\u{1f}\u{1f}exp"
    "ort fn CertKey::from_der(slice<u8, shared> der) : Result<CertKey, CertError>\n    in `std::x509`\n\n   "
    " The public key of the DER SubjectPublicKeyInfo `der`.\n\n    `Err(BadEncoding)` when `der` is not exa"
    "ctly one SubjectPublicKeyInfo; `Err(UnsupportedAlgorithm)` when\n    its algorithm is not RSA, P-256,"
    " P-384 or Ed25519.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::x509\u{1f}CertKey::from_pem\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn CertKey::from_pem(StringView text) : R"
    "esult<CertKey, CertError>\u{1f}The public key of the first `-----BEGIN PUBLIC KEY-----` block in `text` ("
    "RFC 7468).\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn CertKey::from_pem(StringView text) : Result<CertKey, CertError>\n    in `std::x"
    "509`\n\n    The public key of the first `-----BEGIN PUBLIC KEY-----` block in `text` (RFC 7468).\n\n    "
