    "http\u{1f}Url\u{1f}struct\u{1f}export struct Url\u{1f}A parsed absolute URL, `scheme://host[:port]/path?query`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export "
    "struct Url\n    in `std::http`\n\n    A parsed absolute URL, `scheme://host[:port]/path?query`.\n\n    - "
    "`scheme`: lower-cased.\n    - `host`: lower-cased; an IPv6 host keeps its brackets (`[::1]`).\n    - `"
    "port`: the number after the host's `:`, or the scheme's default: 443 for `https`, 80 otherwise.\n    "
    "- `path`: \"/\" when the text has none.\n    - `query`: the text after `?`, without it; empty when ther"
    "e is none.\n\n    The fragment (`#…`), which never reaches a server, is dropped.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::http\u{1f}Url::pa"
    "rse\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Url::parse(StringView text) : Result<Url, HttpError>\u{1f}Parses an absolute URL.\u{1f}\u{1f}expor"
    "t fn Url::parse(StringView text) : Result<Url, HttpError>\n    in `std::http`\n\n    Parses an absolute"
    " URL.\n\n    `Err(BadUrl)` for text without `://`, with an empty host part, with user information (`us"
    "er@`), or with\n    a port that is not a number up to 65535. The scheme is not checked here: `HttpCli"
    "ent::send` gives\n    `Err(UnsupportedScheme)` for one that is neither `http` nor `https`.\n\n    Examp"
    "le, \"Url::parse: defaults and normalisation\":\n        Url u = Result::unwrap(Url::parse(\"HTTPS://Exa"
    "mple.com/a/b?x=1#top\"));\n        assert(u.scheme == \"https\" && u.host == \"example.com\" && u.port == "
    "443);\n        assert(u.path == \"/a/b\" && u.query == \"x=1\");\n        assert(Url::target(&u) == \"/a/b?"
    "x=1\");\n        Url v = Result::unwrap(Url::parse(\"http://[::1]:8080\"));\n        assert(v.host == \"[:"
    ":1]\" && v.path == \"/\");\n        assert(Url::text(&v) == \"http://[::1]:8080/\");\n        assert(Result"
    "::is_err(&Url::parse(\"http://user@example.com/\")));\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::http\u{1f}Url::target\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Url::target"
    "(ref<Url, shared> u) : String\u{1f}The request target: the path, then `?` and the query when the query is"
    " not empty.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Url::target(ref<Url, shared> u) : String\n    in `std::http`\n\n    The request "
    "target: the path, then `?` and the query when the query is not empty.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::http\u{1f}Url::text\u{1f}fn\u{1f}expor"
    "t fn Url::text(ref<Url, shared> u) : String\u{1f}The URL as text again, with the port only when it is not"
    " the scheme's default.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Url::text(ref<Url, shared> u) : String\n    in `std::http`\n\n    The"
    " URL as text again, with the port only when it is not the scheme's default.\n\n    The fragment, dropp"
    "ed by `Url::parse`, does not come back.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::http\u{1f}percent_encode\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn percent_encode(slice"
    "<u8, shared> bytes) : String\u{1f}Percent-encodes `bytes` as RFC 3986 does: unreserved bytes as they are,"
    " every other as `%XX`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn percent_encode(slice<u8, shared> bytes) : String\n    in `std::http"
    "`\n\n    Percent-encodes `bytes` as RFC 3986 does: unreserved bytes as they are, every other as `%XX`."
    "\n\n    The unreserved bytes are ASCII letters and digits, `-`, `.`, `_` and `~`; the hex digits are u"
    "pper\n    case. A space becomes `%20`; `form_encode` writes it as `+`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::http\u{1f}percent_decode\u{1f}fn\u{1f}"
    "export fn percent_decode(StringView text) : Option<Vec<u8>>\u{1f}The bytes `text` percent-encodes, each `"
    "%XX` decoded.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn percent_decode(StringView text) : Option<Vec<u8>>\n    in `std::http`\n\n    T"
    "he bytes `text` percent-encodes, each `%XX` decoded.\n\n    `None` for a `%` not followed by two hex d"
    "igits; hex digits of either case are read. A `+` stays\n    a `+`; `form_decode` reads it as a space."
    "\n\n    Example, \"percent_decode: the reverse of percent_encode\":\n        assert(percent_encode(String"
    "View::as_bytes(\"a b/ü\")) == \"a%20b%2F%C3%BC\");\n        Vec<u8> back = Option::unwrap(percent_decode"
    "(\"a%20b%2f\"));\n        assert(Result::unwrap(String::from_utf8(back)) == \"a b/\");\n        assert(Opt"
    "ion::is_none(&percent_decode(\"100%\")));\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::http\u{1f}Param\u{1f}struct\u{1f}export struct Param\u{1f}One name and va"
    "lue of a query string or an `application/x-www-form-urlencoded` body.\u{1f}\u{1f}export struct Param\n    in `s"
    "td::http`\n\n    One name and value of a query string or an `application/x-www-form-urlencoded` body.\n"
    "\n    Names compare exactly (`find_param`), unlike a header's.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::http\u{1f}Param::new\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Pa"
    "ram::new(StringView name, StringView value) : Param\u{1f}A parameter with a copy of `name` and of `value`"
    ".\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Param::new(StringView name, StringView value) : Param\n    in `std::http`\n\n    A paramet"
    "er with a copy of `name` and of `value`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::http\u{1f}find_param\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn find_param(slice<Param,"
    " shared> params, StringView name) : Option<StringView> from params\u{1f}The value of the first parameter "
    "named exactly `name`, or `None` when there is none.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn find_param(slice<Param, shared> param"
    "s, StringView name) : Option<StringView> from params\n    in `std::http`\n\n    The value of the first "
    "parameter named exactly `name`, or `None` when there is none.\n\n    The comparison is case-sensitive,"
    " unlike `find_header`'s.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::http\u{1f}form_decode\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn form_decode(StringView text) : Vec<Par"
    "am>\u{1f}The parameters of a query string (without its `?`) or of an `application/x-www-form-urlencoded` "
    "body.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn form_decode(StringView text) : Vec<Param>\n    in `std::http`\n\n    The parameters of"
    " a query string (without its `?`) or of an `application/x-www-form-urlencoded` body.\n\n    The text i"
    "s split into `name=value` pairs at `&` and `;`, and empty pairs are skipped. A pair without\n    `=` "
    "has an empty value. Each name and value is read with `+` as a space and then percent-decoded; one\n  "
    "  that is not UTF-8 after decoding, or holds a bad escape, is kept as given, so nothing is lost.\n\n  "
    "  Example, \"form_decode: pairs, bare names and bad escapes\":\n        Vec<Param> ps = form_decode(\"q="
    "red+fish&flag&&n=%41;x=%zz\");\n        assert(Vec::len(&ps) == 4);\n        assert(Option::unwrap(find"
    "_param(&ps, \"q\")) == \"red fish\");\n        assert(Option::unwrap(find_param(&ps, \"flag\")) == \"\");\n   "
    "     assert(Option::unwrap(find_param(&ps, \"n\")) == \"A\");\n        assert(Option::unwrap(find_param(&"
    "ps, \"x\")) == \"%zz\");\n        assert(Option::is_none(&find_param(&ps, \"Q\")));\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::http\u{1f}form_encode"
    "\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn form_encode(slice<Param, shared> params) : String\u{1f}Encodes `params` as a query string o"
    "r form body that `form_decode` reads back.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn form_encode(slice<Param, shared> params) : Str"
    "ing\n    in `std::http`\n\n    Encodes `params` as a query string or form body that `form_decode` reads"
    " back.\n\n    The pairs are `name=value`, joined by `&`, each name and value percent-encoded with a sp"
    "ace as `+`.\n    There is no leading `?`.\n\n    Example, \"form_encode: spaces and reserved bytes\":\n   "
    "     Vec<Param> ps = Vec::new();\n        Vec::push(&mut ps, Param::new(\"q\", \"a b&c\"));\n        Vec::"
    "push(&mut ps, Param::new(\"lang\", \"en\"));\n        String body = form_encode(&ps);\n        assert(body"
    " == \"q=a+b%26c&lang=en\");\n        Vec<Param> back = form_decode(&body);\n        assert(back[0].value"
    " == \"a b&c\");\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::http\u{1f}Url::query_pairs\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Url::query_pairs(ref<Url, shared> u) : Vec<P"
    "aram>\u{1f}The parameters of the URL's query, as `form_decode` reads them.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Url::query_pairs(re"
    "f<Url, shared> u) : Vec<Param>\n    in `std::http`\n\n    The parameters of the URL's query, as `form_d"
    "ecode` reads them.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::http\u{1f}Header\u{1f}struct\u{1f}export struct Header\u{1f}One header field: a name and a val"
    "ue.\u{1f}\u{1f}export struct Header\n    in `std::http`\n\n    One header field: a name and a value.\n\n    Names c"
    "ompare without regard to ASCII case (`find_header`).\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::http\u{1f}Header::new\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Header::ne"
    "w(StringView name, StringView value) : Header\u{1f}A header with a copy of `name` and of `value`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export"
    " fn Header::new(StringView name, StringView value) : Header\n    in `std::http`\n\n    A header with a "
    "copy of `name` and of `value`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::http\u{1f}find_header\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn find_header(slice<Header, shared"
    "> headers, StringView name) : Option<StringView> from headers\u{1f}The value of the first header named `n"
    "ame`, ignoring ASCII case, or `None` when there is none.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn find_header(slice<Header, shared"
    "> headers, StringView name) : Option<StringView> from headers\n    in `std::http`\n\n    The value of t"
    "he first header named `name`, ignoring ASCII case, or `None` when there is none.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::http\u{1f}Request"
    "\u{1f}struct\u{1f}export struct Request\u{1f}An HTTP request: the method, the URL, the headers and the body.\u{1f}\u{1f}expor"
    "t struct Request\n    in `std::http`\n\n    An HTTP request: the method, the URL, the headers and the b"
    "ody.\n\n    For the client, `url` is absolute (`https://…`); for a request a server received, it is "
    "the target as\n    sent (`/path?query`). A server's request has the body decoded if it came chunked.\n"
    "\u{1f}\u{1e}std::http\u{1f}Request::new\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Request::new(StringView method, StringView url) : Request\u{1f}A re"
    "quest with `method` and `url`, no headers and an empty body.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Request::new(StringView meth"
    "od, StringView url) : Request\n    in `std::http`\n\n    A request with `method` and `url`, no headers "
    "and an empty body.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::http\u{1f}Request::header\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Request::header(ref<Request, shared> r, "
    "StringView name) : Option<StringView> from r\u{1f}The value of the request's first header named `name`, i"
    "gnoring ASCII case.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Request::header(ref<Request, shared> r, StringView name) : Option<Str"
    "ingView> from r\n    in `std::http`\n\n    The value of the request's first header named `name`, ignori"
    "ng ASCII case.\n\n    Example, \"Request::header: names ignore case\":\n        Request r = Request::new("
    "\"POST\", \"https://example.com/upload\");\n        Vec::push(&mut r.headers, Header::new(\"Content-Type\","
    " \"text/plain\"));\n        assert(Option::unwrap(Request::header(&r, \"content-type\")) == \"text/plain\")"
    ";\n        assert(Option::is_none(&Request::header(&r, \"accept\")));\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::http\u{1f}Response\u{1f}struct\u{1f}expor"
    "t struct Response\u{1f}An HTTP response: the status, its reason phrase, the headers and the whole body.\u{1f}\u{1f}"
    "export struct Response\n    in `std::http`\n\n    An HTTP response: the status, its reason phrase, the "
    "headers and the whole body.\n\n    The client gives the body decoded if it came chunked, and decompres"
    "sed if it came with\n    `Content-Encoding: gzip` or `deflate` (that header and `Content-Length` are "
    "then dropped).\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::http\u{1f}Response::header\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Response::header(ref<Response, shared> r, S"
    "tringView name) : Option<StringView> from r\u{1f}The value of the response's first header named `name`, i"
    "gnoring ASCII case.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Response::header(ref<Response, shared> r, StringView name) : Option<S"
    "tringView> from r\n    in `std::http`\n\n    The value of the response's first header named `name`, ign"
    "oring ASCII case.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::http\u{1f}Response::text\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Response::text(ref<Response, shared> r) : "
    "Result<String, Utf8Error>\u{1f}The body as text: a copy of its bytes, which must be UTF-8.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Res"
    "ponse::text(ref<Response, shared> r) : Result<String, Utf8Error>\n    in `std::http`\n\n    The body as"
    " text: a copy of its bytes, which must be UTF-8.\n\n    `Err(e)` when they are not.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::http\u{1f}reason"
    "_phrase\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn reason_phrase(u16 status) : str\u{1f}The reason phrase RFC 9110 gives a status code,"
    " such as \"Not Found\" for 404.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn reason_phrase(u16 status) : str\n    in `std::http`\n\n    The"
    " reason phrase RFC 9110 gives a status code, such as \"Not Found\" for 404.\n\n    \"\" for a status it do"
    "es not list here.\n\n    Example, \"reason_phrase: unlisted codes\":\n        assert(reason_phrase(404) ="
    "= \"Not Found\");\n        assert(reason_phrase(299) == \"\");\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::http::client\u{1f}HttpClient\u{1f}struct\u{1f}expo"
    "rt struct HttpClient\u{1f}An HTTP/1.1 client: the settings and the state it carries from request to reque"
    "st.\u{1f}\u{1f}export struct HttpClient\n    in `std::http::client`\n\n    An HTTP/1.1 client: the settings and t"
    "he state it carries from request to request.\n\n    - `roots`: the trusted roots https verifies server"
    "s against; `None` until the first https request\n      loads the system's (`TrustStore::system`), or "
    "a store the program puts there.\n    - `timeout_ms`: the timeout for connecting and for each read and"
    " write, in milliseconds.\n    - `max_redirects`: how many redirects `send` follows.\n    - `max_body`:"
    " the most bytes a response body may have, after decompression too (`TooLarge` beyond).\n    - `header"
    "s`: sent with every request; a request's own header of the same name replaces one.\n    - `keep_alive"
    "`: when set, the last connection is kept open while the server allows, and the next\n      request to"
    " the same origin goes on it; when not (the default), each request has its own connection.\n\n    A pro"
    "gram that makes several https requests keeps one client, so the roots are loaded once.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::http::"
    "client\u{1f}HttpClient::new\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn HttpClient::new() : HttpClient\u{1f}A client with the default setting"
    "s.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn HttpClient::new() : HttpClient\n    in `std::http::client`\n\n    A client with the defau"
    "lt settings.\n\n    No roots loaded yet, a 30 s timeout, up to 10 redirects, a 16 MiB body limit, `kee"
    "p_alive` off, and\n    the headers `User-Agent` and `Accept-Encoding: gzip, deflate`.\n\n    Example, \""
    "HttpClient::new: the defaults\":\n        HttpClient c = HttpClient::new();\n        assert(c.timeout_m"
    "s == 30000 && c.max_redirects == 10 && !c.keep_alive);\n        assert(Option::is_none(&c.roots));\n  "
    "      assert(Option::is_some(&find_header(&c.headers, \"user-agent\")));\n        c.max_body = 1_048_57"
    "6;\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::http::client\u{1f}HttpClient::send\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn HttpClient::send(ref<HttpClient, exclusive> c, "
    "ref<Request, shared> req) : Result<Response, HttpError>\u{1f}Sends `req` and gives the final response, fo"
    "llowing redirects.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn HttpClient::send(ref<HttpClient, exclusive> c, ref<Request, shared> re"
    "q) : Result<Response, HttpError>\n    in `std::http::client`\n\n    Sends `req` and gives the final res"
    "ponse, following redirects.\n\n    - `req.url` is absolute; a scheme other than `http` or `https` is `"
    "Err(UnsupportedScheme)`. The\n      host's addresses are tried in turn.\n    - The request carries `Ho"
    "st`, the client's headers and then the request's own (`Host`,\n      `Content-Length` and `Connection"
    "` of the request are ignored), `Content-Length` when the body is not\n      empty or the method is PO"
    "ST, PUT or PATCH, and `Connection: close` unless `keep_alive` is set.\n    - Interim responses (statu"
    "s 1xx) are read past. A body sent with `Content-Encoding: gzip` or `deflate`\n      arrives decoded.\n"
    "    - A 301, 302 or 303 with a `Location` is followed by GET without the body (HEAD stays HEAD), a 3"
    "07 or\n      308 with the method and body kept; a redirect without `Location` is given as it is. One "
    "redirect\n      more than `max_redirects` is `Err(TooManyRedirects)`. Once a redirect leaves the requ"
    "est's origin\n      (scheme, host and port), `Authorization`, `Proxy-Authorization` and `Cookie`, the"
    " client's and the\n      request's, are not sent again.\n    - On a kept connection that proves closed"
    " before any of the response arrives, an idempotent request\n      (GET, HEAD, PUT, DELETE, OPTIONS, T"
    "RACE) is sent again on a fresh connection; another is\n      `Err(ConnectionClosed)`, since the serve"
    "r may have acted on it.\n    - Network and TLS failures are `Err(HttpNetFailure(e))` and `Err(HttpTls"
    "Failure(e))`; see `HttpError`\n      for the rest.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::http::client\u{1f}http_get\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn http_get"
    "(StringView url) : Result<Response, HttpError>\u{1f}Sends a GET of `url` with a fresh `HttpClient::new()`"
    " and gives the response.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn http_get(StringView url) : Result<Response, HttpError>\n    in `s"
    "td::http::client`\n\n    Sends a GET of `url` with a fresh `HttpClient::new()` and gives the response."
    "\n\n    For https each call loads the system's roots again; a program that makes several requests keep"
    "s an\n    `HttpClient`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::http::client\u{1f}http_post\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn http_post(StringView url, StringVi"
    "ew content_type, slice<u8, shared> body) : Result<Response, HttpError>\u{1f}Sends a POST of `body` to `ur"
    "l`, with `Content-Type: content_type`, from a fresh default client.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn http_post(StringView "
    "url, StringView content_type, slice<u8, shared> body) : Result<Response, HttpError>\n    in `std::htt"
    "p::client`\n\n    Sends a POST of `body` to `url`, with `Content-Type: content_type`, from a fresh def"
    "ault client.\n\n    As `http_get`, a program that makes several requests keeps an `HttpClient`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std:"
    ":http::server\u{1f}HttpServer\u{1f}struct\u{1f}export resource struct HttpServer\u{1f}A listening HTTP/1.1 server: `acce"
    "pt` gives each client's connection.\u{1f}\u{1f}export resource struct HttpServer\n    in `std::http::server`\n\n "
    "   A listening HTTP/1.1 server: `accept` gives each client's connection.\n\n    - `max_body`: the most"
    " bytes a request body may have (`TooLarge` beyond); 16 MiB from `bind`.\n    - `timeout_ms`: the time"
    "out for each read and write on the connections it accepts, in milliseconds;\n      30 s from `bind`.\n"
    "\n    The limits apply to every connection accepted after they are set. A server program handles each"
    "\n    connection in a thread of its own (`spawn`). Dropping the server closes its listening socket.\n\u{1f}"
    "\u{1e}std::http::server\u{1f}HttpServer::bind\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn HttpServer::bind(SocketAddr a) : Result<HttpServer,"
    " NetError>\u{1f}An HTTP server listening at `a`, with a 16 MiB body limit and a 30 s timeout per read and"
    " write.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn HttpServer::bind(SocketAddr a) : Result<HttpServer, NetError>\n    in `std::http::"
    "server`\n\n    An HTTP server listening at `a`, with a 16 MiB body limit and a 30 s timeout per read a"
    "nd write.\n\n    Port 0 asks the system for a free port (`local_addr` names it). Errors as `TcpListene"
    "r::bind`'s.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::http::server\u{1f}HttpServer::bind_tls\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn HttpServer::bind_tls(SocketAddr a,"
    " PrivateKey key, Vec<Certificate> chain) : Result<HttpServer, NetError>\u{1f}An HTTPS server listening at"
    " `a`: each connection it accepts first completes a TLS 1.3 handshake.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn HttpServer::bind_tl"
    "s(SocketAddr a, PrivateKey key, Vec<Certificate> chain) : Result<HttpServer, NetError>\n    in `std::"
    "http::server`\n\n    An HTTPS server listening at `a`: each connection it accepts first completes a TL"
    "S 1.3 handshake.\n\n    `key` is the server's private key and `chain` its certificate first, then its "
    "issuers, as\n    `TlsStream::server` takes them. Otherwise as `bind`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::http::server\u{1f}HttpServer:"
    ":local_addr\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn HttpServer::local_addr(ref<HttpServer, shared> s) : SocketAddr\u{1f}The address "
    "the server listens at, with the port the system chose for port 0.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn HttpServer::local_addr("
    "ref<HttpServer, shared> s) : SocketAddr\n    in `std::http::server`\n\n    The address the server liste"
    "ns at, with the port the system chose for port 0.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::http::server\u{1f}HttpServer::accept\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export f"
    "n HttpServer::accept(ref<HttpServer, exclusive> s) : Result<HttpConnection, HttpError>\u{1f}Waits for the"
    " next client and gives its connection, with the server's limits and timeouts.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn HttpServer:"
    ":accept(ref<HttpServer, exclusive> s) : Result<HttpConnection, HttpError>\n    in `std::http::server`"
    "\n\n    Waits for the next client and gives its connection, with the server's limits and timeouts.\n\n  "
    "  For an https server the TLS handshake comes first: a client that fails it is `Err(HttpTlsFailure(e"
    "))`,\n    and the server is ready for the next. A failure of the listener is `Err(HttpNetFailure(e))`"
    ".\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::http::server\u{1f}HttpConnection\u{1f}struct\u{1f}export resource struct HttpConnection\u{1f}One client's conne"
    "ction to an `HttpServer`: `request`, then `respond`, repeated while it stays open.\u{1f}\u{1f}export resource "
    "struct HttpConnection\n    in `std::http::server`\n\n    One client's connection to an `HttpServer`: `r"
    "equest`, then `respond`, repeated while it stays open.\n\n    The connection stays open for the next r"
    "equest when the request is HTTP/1.1 without\n    `Connection: close`, or HTTP/1.0 with `Connection: k"
    "eep-alive`. Dropping it closes the socket; `close`\n    ends it cleanly first.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::http::server\u{1f}Ht"
    "tpConnection::peer_addr\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn HttpConnection::peer_addr(ref<HttpConnection, shared> c) : Sock"
    "etAddr\u{1f}The client's address.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn HttpConnection::peer_addr(ref<HttpConnection, shared> c) : S"
    "ocketAddr\n    in `std::http::server`\n\n    The client's address.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::http::server\u{1f}HttpConnection::"
    "request\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn HttpConnection::request(ref<HttpConnection, exclusive> c) : Result<Option<Reque"
    "st>, HttpError>\u{1f}Reads the client's next request, or gives `None` when there is none to read.\u{1f}\u{1f}export"
    " fn HttpConnection::request(ref<HttpConnection, exclusive> c) : Result<Option<Request>, HttpError>\n "
    "   in `std::http::server`\n\n    Reads the client's next request, or gives `None` when there is none t"
    "o read.\n\n    - `Ok(Some(r))`: `r.url` is the target as sent (`/path?query`); the body is read by `Co"
    "ntent-Length` or\n      chunked encoding, and there is none without them. When the request expects `1"
    "00-continue`, the\n      `HTTP/1.1 100 Continue` is sent before the body is read.\n    - `Ok(None)`: t"
    "he client closed before a request, or the last response ended the connection.\n    - `Err(BadMessage)"
    "`: a malformed request line, header or body, or an HTTP/1.1 request without `Host`;\n      `Err(TooLa"
    "rge)`: a head over 65536 bytes or a body over `max_body`. The caller answers 400 or 413 if\n      it "
    "wishes, and the connection then closes.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::http::server\u{1f}HttpConnection::respond\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Htt"
    "pConnection::respond(ref<HttpConnection, exclusive> c, u16 status, slice<Header, shared> headers, sl"
    "ice<u8, shared> body) : Result<void, HttpError>\u{1f}Writes a response with `status`, `headers` and `body"
    "`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn HttpConnection::respond(ref<HttpConnection, exclusive> c, u16 status, slice<Header, sh"
    "ared> headers, slice<u8, shared> body) : Result<void, HttpError>\n    in `std::http::server`\n\n    Wri"
    "tes a response with `status`, `headers` and `body`.\n\n    The status line carries `reason_phrase(stat"
    "us)`. `Content-Length` and `Connection` among `headers` are\n    dropped: `Content-Length` is written"
    " from `body` (not for 1xx, 204 or 304), and `Connection` as\n    negotiated. The body is left out aft"
    "er a HEAD request and for a status that has none. After a response\n    that ends the connection, the"
    " connection is closed and `request` gives `None`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::http::server\u{1f}HttpConnection::close\u{1f}fn\u{1f}expor"
    "t fn HttpConnection::close(ref<HttpConnection, exclusive> c)\u{1f}Ends the connection: closes its sending"
    " side, or sends TLS's close_notify on an https connection.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn HttpConnection::close(ref<Http"
    "Connection, exclusive> c)\n    in `std::http::server`\n\n    Ends the connection: closes its sending si"
    "de, or sends TLS's close_notify on an https connection.\n\n    Does nothing on a connection already cl"
    "osed.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::database\u{1f}scram_salted_password\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn scram_salted_password(StringView password, "
    "slice<u8, shared> salt, usize iterations) : Vec<u8>\u{1f}The SCRAM-SHA-256 salted password: PBKDF2 over H"
    "MAC-SHA-256 of `password` and `salt`, 32 bytes.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn scram_salted_password(StringView password"
    ", slice<u8, shared> salt, usize iterations) : Vec<u8>\n    in `std::database`\n\n    The SCRAM-SHA-256 "
    "salted password: PBKDF2 over HMAC-SHA-256 of `password` and `salt`, 32 bytes.\n\n    `iterations` is t"
    "he server's count. The password is used as given, with no SASLprep normalisation.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::database\u{1f}Sc"
    "ram\u{1f}struct\u{1f}export struct Scram\u{1f}The client's side of one SCRAM-SHA-256 exchange (RFC 5802, RFC 7677),"
    " without channel binding.\u{1f}\u{1f}export struct Scram\n    in `std::database`\n\n    The client's side of one "
    "SCRAM-SHA-256 exchange (RFC 5802, RFC 7677), without channel binding.\n\n    The steps in order: `Scra"
    "m::start`, send `Scram::client_first`, answer the server's first message with\n    `Scram::respond`, "
    "then check the server's final message with `Scram::verify`. The PostgreSQL client uses\n    it; it is"
    " exported so a program can speak the exchange to another server.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::database\u{1f}Scram::start\u{1f}fn\u{1f}exp"
    "ort fn Scram::start(StringView user, StringView client_nonce) : Scram\u{1f}A new exchange for `user` with"
    " the client's nonce `client_nonce`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Scram::start(StringView user, StringView client_nonce"
    ") : Scram\n    in `std::database`\n\n    A new exchange for `user` with the client's nonce `client_nonc"
    "e`.\n\n    `,` and `=` in `user` are escaped as `=2C` and `=3D`. The nonce should be fresh random text"
    " for each\n    exchange, such as the base64 of bytes from `os_random_bytes`. PostgreSQL ignores the u"
    "ser, and its client\n    sends `\"\"`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::database\u{1f}Scram::client_first\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Scram::client_f"
    "irst(ref<Scram, shared> s) : String\u{1f}The client's first message, `n,,n=USER,r=NONCE`: no channel bind"
    "ing.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Scram::client_first(ref<Scram, shared> s) : String\n    in `std::database`\n\n    The c"
    "lient's first message, `n,,n=USER,r=NONCE`: no channel binding.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::database\u{1f}Scram::respond\u{1f}fn\u{1f}ex"
    "port fn Scram::respond(ref<Scram, exclusive> s, StringView server_first, StringView password) : Resu"
    "lt<String, PgError>\u{1f}The client's final message, carrying the proof of `password`, for the server's f"
    "irst message.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Scram::respond(ref<Scram, exclusive> s, StringView server_first, StringView"
    " password) : Result<String, PgError>\n    in `std::database`\n\n    The client's final message, carryin"
    "g the proof of `password`, for the server's first message.\n\n    `server_first` is the server's `r=…"
    ",s=…,i=…`. Remembers the signature `Scram::verify` then expects.\n    `Err(AuthFailed)` when the "
    "server's nonce does not begin with the client's and add to it;\n    `Err(ProtocolViolation)` when the"
    " message is malformed, asks for an extension (`m=`), gives an iteration\n    count of 0 or a salt tha"
    "t is not base64.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::database\u{1f}Scram::verify\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Scram::verify(ref<Scram, shared> s, Stri"
    "ngView server_final) : bool\u{1f}Whether the server's final message (`v=…`) carries the signature this "
    "exchange expects.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Scram::verify(ref<Scram, shared> s, StringView server_final) : bool\n   "
    " in `std::database`\n\n    Whether the server's final message (`v=…`) carries the signature this exc"
    "hange expects.\n\n    `false` for anything else, an `e=` error among them, and `false` before `Scram::"
    "respond` has succeeded\n    (there is no signature to expect yet).\n\n    Example, \"Scram: a whole exch"
    "ange\":\n        Scram s = Scram::start(\"user\", \"rOprNGfwEbeRWgbNEkqO\");\n        assert(Scram::client_"
    "first(&s) == \"n,,n=user,r=rOprNGfwEbeRWgbNEkqO\");\n        String first = \"r=rOprNGfwEbeRWgbNEkqO%hvY"
    "DpWUa2RaTCAfuxFIlj)hNlF$k0,\";\n        String::append(&mut first, \"s=W22ZaJ0SNY7soEsUEjb6gQ==,i=4\");\n"
    "        String reply = Result::unwrap(Scram::respond(&mut s, &first, \"pencil\"));\n        assert(Stri"
    "ngView::ends_with(&reply, \",p=0ByS2g6XZEtov8MR140MFRsEfy8/X+bacfpPofVtKjE=\"));\n        assert(Scram:"
    ":verify(&s, \"v=ITrN4zX09+hsD398Qk6ol73eg0shWPnOWwnwS83jitc=\"));\n        assert(!Scram::verify(&s, \"e"
    "=invalid-proof\"));\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::database::postgres\u{1f}PgError\u{1f}enum\u{1f}export enum PgError\u{1f}Why a PostgreSQL conne"
    "ction or statement failed.\u{1f}\u{1f}export enum PgError\n    in `std::database::postgres`\n\n    Why a PostgreS"
    "QL connection or statement failed.\n\n    - `PgNetFailure(e)`: connecting, reading or writing failed; "
    "`e` says how.\n    - `PgTlsFailure(e)`: the TLS handshake or the encrypted stream failed.\n    - `TlsR"
    "efused`: the server does not accept TLS, and the URL asks for `verify-full`.\n    - `NoTrustedRoots`:"
    " the system's trusted roots could not be loaded.\n    - `BadConnectionUrl`: the URL is malformed (`Pg"
    "Url::parse`).\n    - `UnsupportedAuth`: the server asks for a method other than SCRAM-SHA-256 or a pa"
    "ssword over TLS.\n    - `AuthRefused`: the server asks for the password in clear over an unencrypted "
    "connection.\n    - `AuthFailed`: the server refused the credentials, or failed to prove it knows them"
    ".\n    - `Server(e)`: the server reported an error; the connection stays usable.\n    - `ProtocolViola"
    "tion`: a message from the server is malformed or not allowed at that point.\n    - `ResultTooLarge`: "
    "the rows exceed `max_result`, or more than 65 535 parameters were given.\n    - `Disconnected`: the s"
    "tream ended, or the connection was closed or broken by an earlier failure.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::database::postgres"
    "\u{1f}PgServerError\u{1f}struct\u{1f}export struct PgServerError\u{1f}An error or notice the server reported.\u{1f}\u{1f}export st"
    "ruct PgServerError\n    in `std::database::postgres`\n\n    An error or notice the server reported.\n\n  "
    "  `severity` is `ERROR`, `FATAL`, `NOTICE` and so on; `code` the five-character SQLSTATE; `message` "
    "the\n    text; `detail`, `hint` and `position` (a character position from 1 into the statement) when "
    "the server\n    gave them.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::database::postgres\u{1f}PgError::text\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn PgError::text(ref<PgE"
    "rror, shared> e) : String\u{1f}`e` as text for a message; a server error as `severity: message (code)`.\u{1f}\u{1f}"
    "export fn PgError::text(ref<PgError, shared> e) : String\n    in `std::database::postgres`\n\n    `e` a"
    "s text for a message; a server error as `severity: message (code)`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::database::postgres\u{1f}PgSslM"
    "ode\u{1f}enum\u{1f}export enum PgSslMode\u{1f}Whether a connection is encrypted.\u{1f}\u{1f}export enum PgSslMode\n    in `std"
    "::database::postgres`\n\n    Whether a connection is encrypted.\n\n    - `Disable`: not encrypted.\n    -"
    " `VerifyFull`: TLS, with the server's certificate verified for the host name against the trusted roo"
    "ts.\n\n    An unverified TLS connection is not offered.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::database::postgres\u{1f}PgUrl\u{1f}struct\u{1f}export "
    "struct PgUrl\u{1f}A parsed connection URL, `postgres://user[:password]@host[:port]/database[?sslmode=MODE"
    "]`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export struct PgUrl\n    in `std::database::postgres`\n\n    A parsed connection URL, `postgres://"
    "user[:password]@host[:port]/database[?sslmode=MODE]`.\n\n    `user`, `password` and `database` are per"
    "cent-decoded; `host` is a name, an IPv4 literal or an IPv6\n    literal without its brackets.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::"
    "database::postgres\u{1f}PgUrl::parse\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn PgUrl::parse(StringView text) : Result<PgUrl, PgError>\u{1f}"
    "The connection URL `text` taken apart.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn PgUrl::parse(StringView text) : Result<PgUrl, PgEr"
    "ror>\n    in `std::database::postgres`\n\n    The connection URL `text` taken apart.\n\n    The scheme is"
    " `postgres` or `postgresql`. The port defaults to 5432, the database to the user, `sslmode`\n    to `"
    "verify-full`; the only query key is `sslmode`, `disable` or `verify-full`. `Err(BadConnectionUrl)` f"
    "or\n    another scheme, no user, no host, a port that is not a number, another query key or mode, or "
    "a bad\n    percent-encoding.\n\n    Example, \"PgUrl::parse: decoding and defaults\":\n        PgUrl u = R"
    "esult::unwrap(PgUrl::parse(\"postgres://app:p%40ss@[::1]/?sslmode=disable\"));\n        assert(u.host ="
    "= \"::1\" && u.port == 5432);\n        assert(u.database == \"app\");\n        match (&u.password)\n       "
    " {\n            Some(p) : assert(*p == \"p@ss\"),\n            None    : assert(false),\n        }\n      "
    "  Result<PgUrl, PgError> no_user = PgUrl::parse(\"postgres://db.example/shop\");\n        assert(Result"
    "::is_err(&no_user));\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::database::postgres\u{1f}PgValue\u{1f}enum\u{1f}export enum PgValue\u{1f}A statement paramete"
    "r, sent in the text form the server reads for it.\u{1f}\u{1f}export enum PgValue\n    in `std::database::postgr"
    "es`\n\n    A statement parameter, sent in the text form the server reads for it.\n\n    The server infer"
    "s each parameter's type from the statement. `PgValue::text` gives the text each variant\n    is sent "
    "as.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::database::postgres\u{1f}PgValue::text\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn PgValue::text(ref<PgValue, shared> value) :"
    " Option<String>\u{1f}The text `value` is sent as; `None` for `Null`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn PgValue::text(ref<PgValue"
    ", shared> value) : Option<String>\n    in `std::database::postgres`\n\n    The text `value` is sent as;"
    " `None` for `Null`.\n\n    An integer and a float as decimal text (a float that is not finite as `Infi"
    "nity`, `-Infinity` or `NaN`),\n    a bool as `t` or `f`, bytes as bytea's hex form (`\\x` and the hex "
    "digits).\n\n    Example, \"PgValue::text: what is sent\":\n        assert(Option::unwrap(PgValue::text(&B"
    "ool(true))) == \"t\");\n        assert(Option::unwrap(PgValue::text(&Bytes(Vec::filled(2, 0xAB: u8)))) "
    "== \"\\\\xabab\");\n        assert(Option::unwrap(PgValue::text(&Float(1.0 / 0.0))) == \"Infinity\");\n     "
    "   assert(Option::is_none(&PgValue::text(&Null)));\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::database::postgres\u{1f}PgColumn\u{1f}struct\u{1f}export "
    "struct PgColumn\u{1f}One column of a result: its name and the OID of its type (23 for int4, 25 for text, "
    "16 for bool).\u{1f}\u{1f}export struct PgColumn\n    in `std::database::postgres`\n\n    One column of a result: "
    "its name and the OID of its type (23 for int4, 25 for text, 16 for bool).\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::database::postgres\u{1f}"
    "PgRow\u{1f}struct\u{1f}export struct PgRow\u{1f}One row of a result: a cell per column, NULL as `None`, every other"
    " value as the server's text form.\u{1f}\u{1f}export struct PgRow\n    in `std::database::postgres`\n\n    One row"
    " of a result: a cell per column, NULL as `None`, every other value as the server's text form.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std:"
    ":database::postgres\u{1f}PgRow::get\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn PgRow::get(ref<PgRow, shared> r, usize i) : Option<Strin"
    "gView>\u{1f}The text of the cell at column `i` of `r`; `None` for NULL or past the last column.\u{1f}\u{1f}export f"
    "n PgRow::get(ref<PgRow, shared> r, usize i) : Option<StringView>\n    in `std::database::postgres`\n\n "
    "   The text of the cell at column `i` of `r`; `None` for NULL or past the last column.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::databa"
    "se::postgres\u{1f}PgRow::get_i64\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn PgRow::get_i64(ref<PgRow, shared> r, usize i) : Option<i64>"
    "\u{1f}The cell at column `i` of `r` read as an `i64`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn PgRow::get_i64(ref<PgRow, shared> r, usi"
    "ze i) : Option<i64>\n    in `std::database::postgres`\n\n    The cell at column `i` of `r` read as an `"
    "i64`.\n\n    `None` for NULL, past the last column, or for text that is not an integer; `PgRow::get` s"
    "till gives the\n    text.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::database::postgres\u{1f}PgRow::get_f64\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn PgRow::get_f64(ref<Pg"
    "Row, shared> r, usize i) : Option<f64>\u{1f}The cell at column `i` of `r` read as an `f64`, `NaN`, `Infin"
    "ity` and `-Infinity` included.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn PgRow::get_f64(ref<PgRow, shared> r, usize i) : Option<f64"
    ">\n    in `std::database::postgres`\n\n    The cell at column `i` of `r` read as an `f64`, `NaN`, `Infi"
    "nity` and `-Infinity` included.\n\n    `None` for NULL, past the last column, or for text that is not "
    "a number.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::database::postgres\u{1f}PgRow::get_bool\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn PgRow::get_bool(ref<PgRow, shared> "
    "r, usize i) : Option<bool>\u{1f}The cell at column `i` of `r` read as a `bool`: `t` is `true`, `f` is `fa"
    "lse`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn PgRow::get_bool(ref<PgRow, shared> r, usize i) : Option<bool>\n    in `std::database"
    "::postgres`\n\n    The cell at column `i` of `r` read as a `bool`: `t` is `true`, `f` is `false`.\n\n   "
    " `None` for NULL, past the last column, or for any other text.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::database::postgres\u{1f}PgRow::get_"
    "bytes\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn PgRow::get_bytes(ref<PgRow, shared> r, usize i) : Option<Vec<u8>>\u{1f}The cell at col"
    "umn `i` of `r` read as bytes from bytea's hex form (`\\x` and hex digits).\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn PgRow::get_byte"
    "s(ref<PgRow, shared> r, usize i) : Option<Vec<u8>>\n    in `std::database::postgres`\n\n    The cell at"
    " column `i` of `r` read as bytes from bytea's hex form (`\\x` and hex digits).\n\n    `None` for NULL, "
    "past the last column, or for text of another form.\n\n    Example, \"PgRow: typed reads of cells\":\n    "
    "    Vec<Option<String>> cells = Vec::new();\n        Vec::push(&mut cells, Some(\"42\"));\n        Vec::"
    "push(&mut cells, Some(\"t\"));\n        Vec::push(&mut cells, None);\n        PgRow row = PgRow { .cells"
    " = cells };\n        assert(Option::unwrap(PgRow::get_i64(&row, 0)) == 42);\n        assert(Option::un"
    "wrap(PgRow::get_bool(&row, 1)));\n        assert(Option::is_none(&PgRow::get_bool(&row, 0)));\n       "
    " assert(Option::is_none(&PgRow::get(&row, 2)) && Option::is_none(&PgRow::get(&row, 9)));\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::data"
    "base::postgres\u{1f}PgResult\u{1f}struct\u{1f}export struct PgResult\u{1f}What a statement gave: its columns and rows, t"
    "he count of rows affected, and the command tag.\u{1f}\u{1f}export struct PgResult\n    in `std::database::postg"
    "res`\n\n    What a statement gave: its columns and rows, the count of rows affected, and the command t"
    "ag.\n\n    `columns` and `rows` are empty for a statement without a result set. `affected` is the numb"
    "er the tag\n    ends with, 0 when it has none; `tag` is the tag itself (`SELECT 3`, `INSERT 0 1`, `CR"
    "EATE TABLE`).\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::database::postgres\u{1f}PgResult::column\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn PgResult::column(ref<PgResult,"
    " shared> res, StringView name) : Option<usize>\u{1f}The index of the first column named exactly `name`; `"
    "None` when there is none.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn PgResult::column(ref<PgResult, shared> res, StringView name) : "
    "Option<usize>\n    in `std::database::postgres`\n\n    The index of the first column named exactly `nam"
    "e`; `None` when there is none.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::database::postgres\u{1f}PgConnection\u{1f}struct\u{1f}export resource struct "
    "PgConnection\u{1f}An open connection to a PostgreSQL server.\u{1f}\u{1f}export resource struct PgConnection\n    in "
    "`std::database::postgres`\n\n    An open connection to a PostgreSQL server.\n\n    Not independently aud"
    "ited: this client is implemented to PostgreSQL's wire protocol and RFC 5802 and\n    RFC 7677, tested"
    " against their vectors and against a PostgreSQL server on loopback, and fuzzed\n    continuously; it "
    "has not been independently audited.\n\n    One statement runs at a time, its parameters bound (never s"
    "pliced into the SQL text), and rows come back\n    as text. A connection is one thread's: a program t"
    "hat queries from several threads keeps a connection\n    per thread. `notices` holds the notices rece"
    "ived so far, for the program to read and clear;\n    `max_result` is the most a statement's rows may "
    "take in bytes (16 MiB). Dropping a connection without\n    `PgConnection::close` closes the socket wi"
    "thout telling the server. No binary rows, cursors, COPY,\n    LISTEN/NOTIFY, cancellation or channel "
    "binding.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::database::postgres\u{1f}PgConnection::connect\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn PgConnection::connect(StringVi"
    "ew url) : Result<PgConnection, PgError>\u{1f}Connects to the server `url` names, with a 30-second timeout"
    " and the system's trusted roots.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn PgConnection::connect(StringView url) : Result<PgConnect"
    "ion, PgError>\n    in `std::database::postgres`\n\n    Connects to the server `url` names, with a 30-se"
    "cond timeout and the system's trusted roots.\n\n    The roots are loaded only for `verify-full`: `Err("
    "NoTrustedRoots)` when they cannot be. Otherwise as\n    `PgConnection::connect_with`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::database"
    "::postgres\u{1f}PgConnection::connect_with\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn PgConnection::connect_with(StringView url, ref<Tr"
    "ustStore, shared> roots, u64 timeout_ms) : Result<PgConnection, PgError>\u{1f}Connects to the server `url"
    "` names, verifying its certificate against `roots`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn PgConnection::connect_with(StringView"
    " url, ref<TrustStore, shared> roots, u64 timeout_ms) : Result<PgConnection, PgError>\n    in `std::da"
    "tabase::postgres`\n\n    Connects to the server `url` names, verifying its certificate against `roots`"
    ".\n\n    `roots` is unused for `sslmode=disable`. `timeout_ms` bounds connecting to each of the host's"
    " addresses\n    in turn and then every read and write. Authenticates by SCRAM-SHA-256, or by the pass"
    "word over TLS only.\n    Its errors include `BadConnectionUrl`, `PgNetFailure` when no address connec"
    "ts, `TlsRefused`,\n    `PgTlsFailure`, `UnsupportedAuth`, `AuthRefused`, `AuthFailed`, `Server` and `"
    "ProtocolViolation`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::database::postgres\u{1f}PgConnection::parameter\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn PgConnection::par"
    "ameter(ref<PgConnection, shared> c, StringView name) : Option<StringView> from c\u{1f}The value the serve"
    "r reported for the run-time parameter `name` at startup; `None` when it gave none.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn PgConn"
    "ection::parameter(ref<PgConnection, shared> c, StringView name) : Option<StringView> from c\n    in `"
    "std::database::postgres`\n\n    The value the server reported for the run-time parameter `name` at sta"
    "rtup; `None` when it gave none.\n\n    Such as `server_version`, `server_encoding` or `TimeZone`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}st"
    "d::database::postgres\u{1f}PgConnection::query\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn PgConnection::query(ref<PgConnection, exclusi"
    "ve> c, StringView sql, slice<PgValue, shared> params) : Result<PgResult, PgError>\u{1f}Runs one statement"
    " with `$1`, `$2`, ...\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn PgConnection::query(ref<PgConnection, exclusive> c, StringView sql,"
    " slice<PgValue, shared> params) : Result<PgResult, PgError>\n    in `std::database::postgres`\n\n    Ru"
    "ns one statement with `$1`, `$2`, ... bound to `params`, and gives its result.\n\n    A server error i"
    "s `Err(Server(e))` once the server is ready again, and the connection stays usable;\n    `Err(ResultT"
    "ooLarge)` when the rows exceed `max_result`, also leaving it usable. A network or protocol\n    failu"
    "re closes the connection, and every later call gives `Err(Disconnected)`. Transactions are\n    state"
    "ments: `BEGIN`, `COMMIT`, `ROLLBACK`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::database::postgres\u{1f}PgConnection::execute\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn P"
