    "shared> j) : String\u{1f}The value `j` as JSON text for people: one element or member per line, two space"
    "s per level.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Json::pretty(ref<Json, shared> j) : String\n    in `std::encoding::json`\n\n   "
    " The value `j` as JSON text for people: one element or member per line, two spaces per level.\n\n    A"
    " key is followed by `: `, an empty array or object stays `[]` or `{}`, and there is no newline at th"
    "e\n    end. Numbers and strings are written as `Json::text` writes them.\n\n    Example, \"Json::pretty:"
    " the layout\":\n        Json a = JsonArray(Vec::new());\n        Json::push(&mut a, JsonNull);\n        "
