    "export fn base64_encode(slice<u8, shared> bytes) : String\n    in `std::encoding::base64`\n\n    The by"
    "tes in base64 (RFC 4648 §4), padded with `=` to a multiple of four characters.\n\n    The alphabet is"
    " the standard one: `A`-`Z`, `a`-`z`, `0`-`9`, `+` and `/`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::encoding::base64\u{1f}base64_decode\u{1f}fn\u{1f}"
    "export fn base64_decode(StringView text) : Result<Vec<u8>, ParseError>\u{1f}The bytes the base64 `text` s"
    "pells, read as `base64_encode` writes it.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn base64_decode(StringView text) : Result<Vec<u8>"
    ", ParseError>\n    in `std::encoding::base64`\n\n    The bytes the base64 `text` spells, read as `base6"
    "4_encode` writes it.\n\n    Padding is required. Empty text gives no bytes.\n\n    - `Err(Invalid(len))`"
    " when the length is not a multiple of four.\n    - `Err(Invalid(i))` at the first byte that is not a "
    "base64 character; a `=` before the final one or two is\n      such a byte.\n    - `Err(Invalid(i))` at"
    " the last character before the padding when it leaves bits over that are not\n      zero: `\"QR==\"` is"
    " refused, since `base64_encode` writes `\"A\"` as `\"QQ==\"`. Each byte string has one\n      text.\n\n    "
    "Example, \"base64_decode: padding\":\n        StringView text = \"hi!?\";\n        String e = base64_encod"
