    "    {\n            Err(Invalid(i)) : assert(i == 2),\n            _               : assert(false),\n   "
    "     }\n        match (base64_decode(\"QR==\"))\n        {\n            Err(Invalid(i)) : assert(i == 1),"
    "\n            _               : assert(false),\n        }\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::encoding::toml\u{1f}Toml\u{1f}enum\u{1f}export enum "
    "Toml\u{1f}A TOML value: a string, an integer, a float, a boolean, a date-time, an array or a table.\u{1f}\u{1f}expo"
    "rt enum Toml\n    in `std::encoding::toml`\n\n    A TOML value: a string, an integer, a float, a boolea"
    "n, a date-time, an array or a table.\n\n    - `TomlString(s)`: a string, its escapes decoded.\n    - `T"
    "omlInteger(i)`: an integer, exact in `i64`.\n    - `TomlFloat(x)`: a float, `inf` and `nan` included."
    "\n    - `TomlBool(b)`: `true` or `false`.\n    - `TomlDateTime(d)`: one of the four date-time forms (s"
    "ee `TomlDateTime`).\n    - `TomlArray(items)`: the elements, in order; elements may be of different k"
    "inds.\n    - `TomlTable(members)`: the members in the order read or added; a key occurs once.\n\n    Th"
    "e variant names carry `Toml` so that none clashes with another `std` enum's. Dropping a `Toml` frees"
    " the\n    whole tree.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::encoding::toml\u{1f}TomlMember\u{1f}struct\u{1f}export struct TomlMember\u{1f}One member of "
    "a TOML table: its key and its value.\u{1f}\u{1f}export struct TomlMember\n    in `std::encoding::toml`\n\n    One"
    " member of a TOML table: its key and its value.\n\n    - `key`: the member's name, one key part (a dot"
    "ted key `a.b` is a member `a` holding a table with a member `b`).\n    - `value`: its value.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::e"
    "ncoding::toml\u{1f}TomlDateKind\u{1f}enum\u{1f}export enum TomlDateKind\u{1f}Which of the four date-time forms a `TomlDa"
    "teTime` is.\u{1f}\u{1f}export enum TomlDateKind\n    in `std::encoding::toml`\n\n    Which of the four date-time "
    "forms a `TomlDateTime` is.\n\n    - `TomlOffsetDateTime`: a date, a time and an offset from UTC: `1979"
    "-05-27T07:32:00Z`, `…-08:00`.\n    - `TomlLocalDateTime`: a date and a time with no offset: `1979-0"
    "5-27T07:32:00`.\n    - `TomlLocalDate`: a date alone: `1979-05-27`.\n    - `TomlLocalTime`: a time alo"
    "ne: `07:32:00`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::encoding::toml\u{1f}TomlDateTime\u{1f}struct\u{1f}export struct TomlDateTime\u{1f}A TOML date-tim"
    "e: the fields of RFC 3339's form, and `kind`, which of the four forms it is.\u{1f}\u{1f}export struct TomlDate"
    "Time\n    in `std::encoding::toml`\n\n    A TOML date-time: the fields of RFC 3339's form, and `kind`, "
    "which of the four forms it is.\n\n    - `kind`: the form; the fields a form does not have are 0.\n    -"
    " `year`, `month`, `day`: the date (`month` 1 to 12, `day` 1 to the month's length).\n    - `hour`, `m"
    "inute`, `second`: the time (`second` up to 60 for a leap second).\n    - `nanoseconds`: the fraction "
    "of the second, 0 to 999 999 999; digits beyond nine are dropped when read.\n    - `offset_minutes`: t"
    "he offset from UTC in minutes, `-1439` to `1439`; 0 for every other form.\n\n    A plain struct, assig"
    "ned by copying. `TomlDateTime::text` writes it as the format does.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::encoding::toml\u{1f}Toml::parse"
    "\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Toml::parse(StringView text) : Result<Toml, ParseError>\u{1f}The TOML document `text` holds"
    ", as a table.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Toml::parse(StringView text) : Result<Toml, ParseError>\n    in `std::encodi"
    "ng::toml`\n\n    The TOML document `text` holds, as a table.\n\n    The whole of TOML 1.0: tables and ar"
    "rays of tables under headers, dotted keys, inline tables, the four\n    string forms with every escap"
    "e, integers in decimal, hexadecimal, octal and binary with underscores,\n    floats with `inf` and `n"
    "an`, and the four date-time forms. An empty document is an empty table.\n\n    - `Err(Invalid(i))` at "
    "the first byte that does not fit, or at a key that is defined twice or would\n      add to a table th"
    "e format has closed (one defined by an earlier header, or an inline table).\n    - `Err(OutOfRange)` "
    "for an integer beyond `i64`, a float beyond `f64`, or arrays and inline tables\n      nested deeper t"
    "han 512.\n\n    `Err(Empty)` never occurs: a document with no key is an empty table.\n\n    Example, \"To"
    "ml::parse: a configuration file\":\n        Toml doc = Result::unwrap(Toml::parse(\"title = \\\"Example\\\""
    "\\n[owner]\\nname = \\\"Tom\\\"\\ndob = 1979-05-27T07:32:00-08:00\\n[database]\\nports = [ 8001, 8001, 8002 ]"
    "\\nenabled = true\\ntemp_targets = { cpu = 79.5, case = 72.0 }\\n[[servers]]\\nip = \\\"10.0.0.1\\\"\\n[[serv"
    "ers]]\\nip = \\\"10.0.0.2\\\"\\n\"));\n        assert(Option::unwrap(Toml::as_text(Option::unwrap(Toml::look"
    "up(&doc, \"owner.name\")))) == \"Tom\");\n        assert(Toml::as_i64(Option::unwrap(Toml::lookup(&doc, \""
    "database.ports.2\"))) == Some(8002: i64));\n        assert(Toml::as_f64(Option::unwrap(Toml::lookup(&d"
    "oc, \"database.temp_targets.cpu\"))) == Some(79.5));\n        assert(Option::unwrap(Toml::as_text(Optio"
    "n::unwrap(Toml::lookup(&doc, \"servers.1.ip\")))) == \"10.0.0.2\");\n        TomlDateTime dob = Option::u"
    "nwrap(Toml::as_datetime(Option::unwrap(Toml::lookup(&doc, \"owner.dob\"))));\n        assert(dob.year ="
    "= 1979 && dob.hour == 7 && dob.offset_minutes == -480);\n\n    Example, \"Toml::parse: where the error "
    "is\":\n        match (Toml::parse(\"a = 1\\nb = \\n\"))\n        {\n            Err(Invalid(i)) : assert(i ="
    "= 10),\n            _               : assert(false),\n        }\n        match (Toml::parse(\"a = 1\\na ="
    " 2\\n\"))\n        {\n            Err(Invalid(i)) : assert(i == 6),\n            _               : assert"
    "(false),\n        }\n        match (Toml::parse(\"n = 9223372036854775808\"))\n        {\n            Err("
    "OutOfRange) : {},\n            _               : assert(false),\n        }\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::encoding::toml\u{1f}TomlD"
    "ateTime::text\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn TomlDateTime::text(ref<TomlDateTime, shared> d) : String\u{1f}The date-time as"
    " TOML (and RFC 3339) writes it: the date, `T`, the time, its fraction when there is one, and the off"
    "set as `Z` or `±HH:MM`; a local form leaves out what it does not have.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn TomlDateTime::tex"
    "t(ref<TomlDateTime, shared> d) : String\n    in `std::encoding::toml`\n\n    The date-time as TOML (and"
    " RFC 3339) writes it: the date, `T`, the time, its fraction when there is one,\n    and the offset as"
    " `Z` or `±HH:MM`; a local form leaves out what it does not have.\n\n    Example, \"TomlDateTime::text:"
    " the four forms\":\n        String text = \"a = 1979-05-27T07:32:00.999999Z\\nb = 1979-05-27T00:32:00.5-"
    "07:00\\nc = 1979-05-27T07:32:00\\nd = 1979-05-27\\ne = 07:32:00\\n\";\n        Toml doc = Result::unwrap(T"
    "oml::parse(&text));\n        assert(Toml::text(&doc) == text);\n        TomlDateTime b = Option::unwra"
    "p(Toml::as_datetime(Option::unwrap(Toml::get(&doc, \"b\"))));\n        assert(b.nanoseconds == 50000000"
    "0 && b.offset_minutes == -420 && TomlDateTime::text(&b) == \"1979-05-27T00:32:00.5-07:00\");\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::en"
    "coding::toml\u{1f}Toml::text\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Toml::text(ref<Toml, shared> t) : String\u{1f}The value `t` as TOML "
    "text.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Toml::text(ref<Toml, shared> t) : String\n    in `std::encoding::toml`\n\n    The valu"
    "e `t` as TOML text.\n\n    A table is written as a document: its plain members as `key = value` lines,"
    " then each member that is a\n    table under a `[header]`, and each non-empty array of tables under `"
    "[[headers]]`, in order, recursively; a\n    key is bare when it can be and quoted otherwise. Strings "
    "are basic strings with `\"`, `\\` and the control\n    characters escaped; a float is written in the sh"
    "ortest digits that read back as it, with `inf` and `nan`;\n    a date-time as `TomlDateTime::text` wr"
    "ites it. A value that is not a table is written in the form it takes\n    after `=`: arrays as `[a, b"
    "]`, inline tables as `{ k = v }`. Comments are not kept. `Toml::parse` of the text\n    gives `t` bac"
    "k, the plain members of each table before its sub-tables.\n\n    Example, \"Toml::text: the layout\":\n  "
    "      Toml doc = Result::unwrap(Toml::parse(\"[server]\\nhost = \\\"example.org\\\"\\nports = [80, 443]\\n[s"
    "erver.tls]\\ncert = 'a b'\\n[[users]]\\nname = \\\"ann\\\"\\n[[users]]\\nname = \\\"bob\\\"\\n\"));\n        String "
    "t = Toml::text(&doc);\n        assert(t == \"[server]\\nhost = \\\"example.org\\\"\\nports = [80, 443]\\n\\n[s"
    "erver.tls]\\ncert = \\\"a b\\\"\\n\\n[[users]]\\nname = \\\"ann\\\"\\n\\n[[users]]\\nname = \\\"bob\\\"\\n\");\n        as"
    "sert(Toml::text(&Result::unwrap(Toml::parse(&t))) == t);\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::encoding::toml\u{1f}Toml::get\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export f"
    "n Toml::get(ref<Toml, shared> t, StringView key) : Option<ref<Toml, shared>> from t\u{1f}The value of the"
    " member named `key` when `t` is a table, else `None`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Toml::get(ref<Toml, shared> t, Stri"
    "ngView key) : Option<ref<Toml, shared>> from t\n    in `std::encoding::toml`\n\n    The value of the me"
    "mber named `key` when `t` is a table, else `None`.\n\n    `None` also when there is no such member.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}"
    "std::encoding::toml\u{1f}Toml::at\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Toml::at(ref<Toml, shared> t, usize i) : Option<ref<Toml, "
