    "port fn Toml::set(ref<Toml, exclusive> t, StringView key, Toml v)\u{1f}Sets member `key` of the table `t`"
    " to `v`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Toml::set(ref<Toml, exclusive> t, StringView key, Toml v)\n    in `std::encoding:"
    ":toml`\n\n    Sets member `key` of the table `t` to `v`.\n\n    The member of that name is replaced, or "
    "else a new member appended. Faults (`diag.assert-failed`) when\n    `t` is not a table.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::encodi"
    "ng::toml\u{1f}Toml::push\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Toml::push(ref<Toml, exclusive> t, Toml v)\u{1f}Appends `v` to the array"
    " `t`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Toml::push(ref<Toml, exclusive> t, Toml v)\n    in `std::encoding::toml`\n\n    Append"
    "s `v` to the array `t`.\n\n    Faults (`diag.assert-failed`) when `t` is not an array.\n\n    Example, \""
    "Toml::set: building a document\":\n        Toml doc = TomlTable(Vec::new());\n        Toml::set(&mut do"
    "c, \"name\", TomlString(\"demo\"));\n        Toml ports = TomlArray(Vec::new());\n        Toml::push(&mut "
    "ports, TomlInteger(8080));\n        Toml::push(&mut ports, TomlInteger(8081));\n        Toml server = "
    "TomlTable(Vec::new());\n        Toml::set(&mut server, \"ports\", ports);\n        Toml::set(&mut server"
    ", \"debug\", TomlBool(false));\n        Toml::set(&mut doc, \"server\", server);\n        Toml::set(&mut d"
    "oc, \"name\", TomlString(\"demo 2\"));\n        assert(Toml::text(&doc) == \"name = \\\"demo 2\\\"\\n\\n[server]"
    "\\nports = [8080, 8081]\\ndebug = false\\n\");\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::compress\u{1f}CompressError\u{1f}enum\u{1f}export enum CompressEr"
    "ror\u{1f}Why a stream could not be decompressed.\u{1f}\u{1f}export enum CompressError\n    in `std::compress`\n\n    W"
    "hy a stream could not be decompressed.\n\n    - `Corrupt(i)`: the stream is not DEFLATE (or not the wr"
    "apper asked for), or its checksum does not match,\n      first seen at byte `i`.\n    - `Truncated`: t"
    "he stream ends before its last block or its trailer.\n    - `Oversize`: the output would exceed the `"
    "max` given.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::compress\u{1f}CompressError::text\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn CompressError::text(ref<CompressError, "
    "shared> e) : str\u{1f}A short description of `e` for a message, such as `corrupt compressed data`.\u{1f}\u{1f}expor"
    "t fn CompressError::text(ref<CompressError, shared> e) : str\n    in `std::compress`\n\n    A short des"
    "cription of `e` for a message, such as `corrupt compressed data`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::compress\u{1f}inflate\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export "
    "fn inflate(slice<u8, shared> data, usize max) : Result<Vec<u8>, CompressError>\u{1f}The bytes a raw DEFLA"
    "TE stream (RFC 1951, no header or checksum) encodes, at most `max` of them.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn inflate(slice"
    "<u8, shared> data, usize max) : Result<Vec<u8>, CompressError>\n    in `std::compress`\n\n    The bytes"
    " a raw DEFLATE stream (RFC 1951, no header or checksum) encodes, at most `max` of them.\n\n    `Err(Ov"
    "ersize)` as soon as the output would exceed `max`: a limit against a small stream that expands\n    w"
    "ithout bound. `Err(Truncated)` when `data` ends inside a block; `Err(Corrupt(i))` at byte `i` for a\n"
    "    malformed block. Bytes after the final block are ignored. Reads stored, fixed and dynamic Huffma"
    "n blocks.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::compress\u{1f}deflate\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn deflate(slice<u8, shared> data) : Vec<u8>\u{1f}`data` comp"
    "ressed as a raw DEFLATE stream (RFC 1951, no header or checksum).\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn deflate(slice<u8, share"
    "d> data) : Vec<u8>\n    in `std::compress`\n\n    `data` compressed as a raw DEFLATE stream (RFC 1951, "
    "no header or checksum).\n\n    One fixed strategy, so every implementation writes the same bytes: LZ77"
    " over a 32 KiB window, each block\n    stored, fixed or dynamic Huffman, whichever is shortest. Empty"
    " data is one empty block (`03 00`).\n\n    Example, \"deflate: empty data, and adler32\":\n        Vec<u8"
    "> nothing = Vec::new();\n        Vec<u8> empty = deflate(&nothing);\n        assert(Vec::len(&empty) ="
    "= 2 && empty[0] == 0x03 && empty[1] == 0x00);\n        assert(Vec::len(&Result::unwrap(inflate(&empty"
    ", 0))) == 0);\n        assert(adler32(b\"Wikipedia\") == 300286872);\n        assert(adler32(&nothing) ="
    "= 1);\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::compress\u{1f}adler32\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn adler32(slice<u8, shared> data) : u32\u{1f}The Adler-32 checks"
    "um of `data` (RFC 1950), zlib's checksum; 1 for no bytes.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn adler32(slice<u8, shared> data)"
    " : u32\n    in `std::compress`\n\n    The Adler-32 checksum of `data` (RFC 1950), zlib's checksum; 1 fo"
    "r no bytes.\n\n    For CRC-32, gzip's checksum, use `crc32` in `std::crypto`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::compress\u{1f}zlib_def"
    "late\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn zlib_deflate(slice<u8, shared> data) : Vec<u8>\u{1f}`data` compressed as a zlib stream "
    "(RFC 1950): a two-byte header, the DEFLATE stream, the Adler-32.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn zlib_deflate(slice<u8, s"
    "hared> data) : Vec<u8>\n    in `std::compress`\n\n    `data` compressed as a zlib stream (RFC 1950): a "
    "two-byte header, the DEFLATE stream, the Adler-32.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::compress\u{1f}zlib_inflate\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn zlib_in"
    "flate(slice<u8, shared> data, usize max) : Result<Vec<u8>, CompressError>\u{1f}The bytes a zlib stream en"
    "codes, at most `max` of them, its header checked and its checksum verified.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn zlib_inflate("
    "slice<u8, shared> data, usize max) : Result<Vec<u8>, CompressError>\n    in `std::compress`\n\n    The "
    "bytes a zlib stream encodes, at most `max` of them, its header checked and its checksum verified.\n\n "
    "   `Err(Corrupt(0))` for a header that is not DEFLATE without a preset dictionary; `Err(Corrupt(i))`"
