    "gView s) : Result<CString, NulError>\u{1f}`s` with a NUL byte after it, or `Err` with the position of the"
    " first NUL already in `s`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn CString::new(StringView s) : Result<CString, NulError>\n    in "
    "`std::ffi`\n\n    `s` with a NUL byte after it, or `Err` with the position of the first NUL already in"
    " `s`.\n\n    A literal where a `StringView` is expected is made into one: `CString::new(\"HOME\")`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}st"
    "d::ffi\u{1f}CString::ptr\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn CString::ptr(ref<CString, shared> c) : rawptr<u8>\u{1f}The address of th"
    "e first byte, to pass to C as a `const char *`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn CString::ptr(ref<CString, shared> c) : ra"
    "wptr<u8>\n    in `std::ffi`\n\n    The address of the first byte, to pass to C as a `const char *`.\n\n  "
    "  Taking the address is safe; the call that uses it is inside `unsafe`. The address is valid until t"
    "he\n    `CString` is dropped.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::ffi\u{1f}CString::len\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn CString::len(ref<CString, shared> "
    "c) : usize\u{1f}The length of the text, without the NUL.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn CString::len(ref<CString, shared> c) "
    ": usize\n    in `std::ffi`\n\n    The length of the text, without the NUL.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::ffi\u{1f}CString::as_bytes"
    "\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn CString::as_bytes(ref<CString, shared> c) : slice<u8, shared>\u{1f}The text without the NUL"
    ", as bytes.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn CString::as_bytes(ref<CString, shared> c) : slice<u8, shared>\n    in `std::ff"
    "i`\n\n    The text without the NUL, as bytes.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::ffi\u{1f}copy_to_raw\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn copy_to_raw<T: plain"
    ">(slice<T, shared> s, rawptr<T> p)\u{1f}The elements of `s`, plain data, copied to C memory at `p`: an ou"
    "tput buffer a C caller owns (D-0257).\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn copy_to_raw<T: plain>(slice<T, shared> s, rawptr<T>"
    " p)\n    in `std::ffi`\n\n    The elements of `s`, plain data, copied to C memory at `p`: an output\n   "
    " buffer a C caller owns (D-0257). Called inside `unsafe { }`\n    (`[Trusted-Call]`): the caller vouc"
    "hes that `p` has room for them and\n    that nothing else uses that memory for the call.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::ffi\u{1f}i"
    "s_null\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn is_null<T>(rawptr<T> p) : bool\u{1f}Whether `p` is C's `NULL`, the address `null_rawp"
    "tr<T>()`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn is_null<T>(rawptr<T> p) : bool\n    in `std::ffi`\n\n    Whether `p` is C's `NULL`"
    ", the address `null_rawptr<T>()`.\n\n    C functions return `NULL` for \"none\": `getenv` of a name that"
    " is not set, `fopen` of a file that cannot be\n    opened. Testing for it is safe; reading through `p"
    "` is not.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::core\u{1f}Result::map_err\u{1f}built in fn\u{1f}fn Result::map_err<T, E1, E2>(Result<T, E1> r, fn("
    "E1) : E2 f) : Result<T, E2>\u{1f}Keeps an `Ok` as it is and maps an `Err` through `f`: `match (r) { Ok(v)"
    " : Ok(v), Err(e) : Err(f(e)) }`.\u{1f}\u{1f}fn Result::map_err<T, E1, E2>(Result<T, E1> r, fn(E1) : E2 f) : Re"
    "sult<T, E2>\n    in `std::core`\n\n    Keeps an `Ok` as it is and maps an `Err` through `f`: `match (r)"
    " { Ok(v) : Ok(v), Err(e) : Err(f(e)) }`.\n    It is the step that turns a library's error into a prog"
    "ram's own before `?` passes it on. `r` is\n    consumed; `f` runs only for an `Err`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::io\u{1f}printf"
    "\u{1f}built in fn\u{1f}fn printf(str f, a1, …, an)\u{1f}Writes the arguments to standard output as the format `f`"
    " says (`spec/21` §2f, `rule.stdlib.format`).\u{1f}\u{1f}fn printf(str f, a1, …, an)\n    in `std::io`\n\n    W"
    "rites the arguments to standard output as the format `f` says (`spec/21` §2f, `rule.stdlib.format`)"
    ".\n    `f` is a string literal, so the format and the arguments are checked when the program is compi"
    "led and\n    nothing about it can fail at run time. The conversions are C's: `%d` for any integer typ"
    "e (there is no\n    `%ld`), `%u`, `%x`, `%X`, `%o`, `%b` (binary) for an integer's bits in its own wi"
    "dth, `%f`, `%e`, `%g` for\n    `f32` and `f64`, `%s` for a `str`, a `ref<String, shared>` or a `bool`"
    ", and `%v` for any printable value\n    or enum \"as CobaltC writes it\" (an enum's variant name; a flo"
    "at that reads back as the same value). Width\n    and precision may be `*`, taking the next argument "
    "(a `usize`). A reference to a number, a `bool` or a\n    `str` prints as what it refers to, so `forea"
    "ch (x in &v) { printf(\"%d\\n\", x); }` prints the elements.\n    Output is buffered (D-0178) and writte"
    "n out when the buffer fills, at `flush_stdout()`, and when the\n    program ends.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::io\u{1f}eprintf\u{1f}b"
    "uilt in fn\u{1f}fn eprintf(str f, a1, …, an)\u{1f}Writes the arguments to standard error as the format `f` s"
    "ays, with `printf`'s conversions.\u{1f}\u{1f}fn eprintf(str f, a1, …, an)\n    in `std::io`\n\n    Writes the a"
    "rguments to standard error as the format `f` says, with `printf`'s conversions. For\n    messages tha"
    "t are not the program's output: errors, warnings, progress. Standard error is written at\n    once, w"
    "ith nothing held back, so its text and standard output's interleave in the order the calls ran\n    ("
    "after a `flush_stdout()`, exactly).\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::text\u{1f}sprintf\u{1f}built in fn\u{1f}fn sprintf(str f, a1, …, an) :"
    " String\u{1f}The text `printf` would write for the same arguments, as a new `String` instead of output.\u{1f}\u{1f}"
    "fn sprintf(str f, a1, …, an) : String\n    in `std::text`\n\n    The text `printf` would write for th"
    "e same arguments, as a new `String` instead of output. The format is\n    checked when the program is"
    " compiled, as `printf`'s is.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::text\u{1f}String::appendf\u{1f}built in fn\u{1f}fn String::appendf(ref<String, "
    "exclusive> s, str f, a1, …, an)\u{1f}Appends to `*s` the text `printf` would write for the same argumen"
    "ts; `String::append` of `sprintf`'s result, without the intermediate `String`.\u{1f}\u{1f}fn String::appendf(r"
    "ef<String, exclusive> s, str f, a1, …, an)\n    in `std::text`\n\n    Appends to `*s` the text `print"
    "f` would write for the same arguments; `String::append` of `sprintf`'s\n    result, without the inter"
    "mediate `String`. The common way to build a line piece by piece before printing\n    or keeping it on"
    "ce.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::io\u{1f}File::printf\u{1f}built in fn\u{1f}fn File::printf(ref<File, exclusive> f, str format, a1, …, "
    "an) : Result<void, FileError>\u{1f}Writes the formatted text to the open file `*f`, as `printf` would to "
    "standard output (D-0059); the format is checked when the program is compiled.\u{1f}\u{1f}fn File::printf(ref<F"
    "ile, exclusive> f, str format, a1, …, an) : Result<void, FileError>\n    in `std::io`\n\n    Writes t"
    "he formatted text to the open file `*f`, as `printf` would to standard output (D-0059); the\n    form"
    "at is checked when the program is compiled. A write that fails is the `Err`, as for `File::write`.\n "
    "   `File` itself is `std::fs`'s type; this function is registered with the `printf` family in `std::"
    "io`,\n    and `import std;` brings in both.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::net\u{1f}TcpStream::printf\u{1f}built in fn\u{1f}fn TcpStream::pr"
    "intf(ref<TcpStream, exclusive> s, str format, a1, …, an) : Result<void, NetError>\u{1f}Writes the forma"
    "tted text to the connected stream `*s`, as `File::printf` does to a file; the whole text is written "
    "or the `Err` says why (`[Stream-Write]`).\u{1f}\u{1f}fn TcpStream::printf(ref<TcpStream, exclusive> s, str for"
    "mat, a1, …, an) : Result<void, NetError>\n    in `std::net`\n\n    Writes the formatted text to the c"
    "onnected stream `*s`, as `File::printf` does to a file; the whole text\n    is written or the `Err` s"
    "ays why (`[Stream-Write]`). A line protocol's reply in one call:\n    `TcpStream::printf(&mut c, \"%d "
    "%s\\r\\n\", code, text)?`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::core\u{1f}assert\u{1f}built in fn\u{1f}fn assert(bool c), fn assert(bool c, str f, a"
    "1, …, an)\u{1f}Checks `c` and, if it is false, faults with `diag.assert-failed`, reporting the formatte"
    "d message if one is given (`spec/18` §1a, `rule.fail.assert`, D-0065).\u{1f}\u{1f}fn assert(bool c), fn asser"
    "t(bool c, str f, a1, …, an)\n    in `std::core`\n\n    Checks `c` and, if it is false, faults with `d"
    "iag.assert-failed`, reporting the formatted message if one\n    is given (`spec/18` §1a, `rule.fail."
    "assert`, D-0065). The message's arguments are evaluated only when the\n    assertion fails. An assert"
    "ion is part of the program's meaning: there is no build in which it is left\n    out, and `--check` s"
    "ees its format as it sees `printf`'s. The fault unwinds like any other, so\n    destructors run and a"
    " supervised task reports it to its parent.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::process\u{1f}exit\u{1f}built in fn\u{1f}fn exit(u8 status) : neve"
    "r\u{1f}Ends the program with exit status `status` (`[Exit]`, `spec/21` §2k, D-0150).\u{1f}\u{1f}fn exit(u8 status)"
    " : never\n    in `std::process`\n\n    Ends the program with exit status `status` (`[Exit]`, `spec/21` "
    "§2k, D-0150). The calling thread unwinds\n    first, so its destructors run and standard output is w"
    "ritten out; other threads are not waited for. The\n    result type is `never`, so a branch that calls"
    " `exit` needs no value of its own. `fn main() : u8`'s return\n    value is the ordinary way to set th"
    "e status; `exit` is for deep inside a program.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::math\u{1f}sqrt\u{1f}built in fn\u{1f}fn sqrt(T x) : T\u{1f}The squ"
    "are root of `x`, correctly rounded (`[Float-Fn]`, `spec/21` §3d, D-0091): every conforming implemen"
    "tation gives the same bits.\u{1f}\u{1f}fn sqrt(T x) : T\n    in `std::math`\n\n    The square root of `x`, correc"
    "tly rounded (`[Float-Fn]`, `spec/21` §3d, D-0091): every conforming\n    implementation gives the sa"
    "me bits. A NaN for a negative `x`; `-0.0` for `-0.0`; a NaN in gives a NaN out.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::math\u{1f}floor\u{1f}bu"
    "ilt in fn\u{1f}fn floor(T x) : T\u{1f}`x` rounded to an integral value toward negative infinity, exactly (`[Fl"
    "oat-Fn]`).\u{1f}\u{1f}fn floor(T x) : T\n    in `std::math`\n\n    `x` rounded to an integral value toward negati"
    "ve infinity, exactly (`[Float-Fn]`). A NaN or an infinity is\n    returned as it is.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::math\u{1f}ceil"
    "\u{1f}built in fn\u{1f}fn ceil(T x) : T\u{1f}`x` rounded to an integral value toward positive infinity, exactly (`["
    "Float-Fn]`).\u{1f}\u{1f}fn ceil(T x) : T\n    in `std::math`\n\n    `x` rounded to an integral value toward posit"
    "ive infinity, exactly (`[Float-Fn]`).\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::math\u{1f}round\u{1f}built in fn\u{1f}fn round(T x) : T\u{1f}`x` rounded to"
    " the nearest integral value, halfway cases away from zero (`2.5` to `3.0`, `-2.5` to `-3.0`), exactl"
    "y (`[Float-Fn]`).\u{1f}\u{1f}fn round(T x) : T\n    in `std::math`\n\n    `x` rounded to the nearest integral val"
    "ue, halfway cases away from zero (`2.5` to `3.0`, `-2.5` to\n    `-3.0`), exactly (`[Float-Fn]`). Con"
    "vert the result with `rule.arith.convert` when an integer is wanted.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::math\u{1f}trunc\u{1f}built in fn\u{1f}f"
    "n trunc(T x) : T\u{1f}`x` rounded to an integral value toward zero, exactly (`[Float-Fn]`): the fractiona"
    "l part dropped.\u{1f}\u{1f}fn trunc(T x) : T\n    in `std::math`\n\n    `x` rounded to an integral value toward z"
    "ero, exactly (`[Float-Fn]`): the fractional part dropped.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::math\u{1f}ln\u{1f}built in fn\u{1f}fn ln(T x) : T\u{1f}"
    "The natural logarithm of `x`, within one unit in the last place of the mathematical value (`[Float-T"
    "ranscendental]`, D-0101): the platform's C library computes it, so `coby` and `cobc` agree on one pl"
    "atform and may differ in the last bit between platforms.\u{1f}\u{1f}fn ln(T x) : T\n    in `std::math`\n\n    The"
    " natural logarithm of `x`, within one unit in the last place of the mathematical value\n    (`[Float-"
    "Transcendental]`, D-0101): the platform's C library computes it, so `coby` and `cobc` agree on one\n "
    "   platform and may differ in the last bit between platforms. A NaN for a negative `x`; negative inf"
    "inity for\n    `±0`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::math\u{1f}exp\u{1f}built in fn\u{1f}fn exp(T x) : T\u{1f}`e` to the power `x`, within one un"
    "it in the last place (`[Float-Transcendental]`).\u{1f}\u{1f}fn exp(T x) : T\n    in `std::math`\n\n    `e` to the"
    " power `x`, within one unit in the last place (`[Float-Transcendental]`). Overflows to infinity\n    "
    "as IEEE-754 says.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::math\u{1f}log2\u{1f}built in fn\u{1f}fn log2(T x) : T\u{1f}The base-2 logarithm of `x`, within "
    "one unit in the last place (`[Float-Transcendental]`); a NaN for a negative `x`, negative infinity f"
    "or `±0`.\u{1f}\u{1f}fn log2(T x) : T\n    in `std::math`\n\n    The base-2 logarithm of `x`, within one unit in "
    "the last place (`[Float-Transcendental]`); a NaN for a\n    negative `x`, negative infinity for `±0`"
    ". For an integer's bit length, `integer` arithmetic is exact and\n    cheaper.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::math\u{1f}log10\u{1f}buil"
    "t in fn\u{1f}fn log10(T x) : T\u{1f}The base-10 logarithm of `x`, within one unit in the last place (`[Float-T"
    "ranscendental]`); a NaN for a negative `x`, negative infinity for `±0`.\u{1f}\u{1f}fn log10(T x) : T\n    in `"
    "std::math`\n\n    The base-10 logarithm of `x`, within one unit in the last place (`[Float-Transcenden"
    "tal]`); a NaN for a\n    negative `x`, negative infinity for `±0`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::math\u{1f}sin\u{1f}built in fn\u{1f}fn si"
    "n(T x) : T\u{1f}The sine of `x`, an angle in radians, within one unit in the last place (`[Float-Transcen"
    "dental]`).\u{1f}\u{1f}fn sin(T x) : T\n    in `std::math`\n\n    The sine of `x`, an angle in radians, within one"
    " unit in the last place (`[Float-Transcendental]`).\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::math\u{1f}cos\u{1f}built in fn\u{1f}fn cos(T x) : T\u{1f}The "
    "cosine of `x`, an angle in radians, within one unit in the last place (`[Float-Transcendental]`).\u{1f}\u{1f}f"
    "n cos(T x) : T\n    in `std::math`\n\n    The cosine of `x`, an angle in radians, within one unit in th"
    "e last place (`[Float-Transcendental]`).\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::math\u{1f}tan\u{1f}built in fn\u{1f}fn tan(T x) : T\u{1f}The tangent of "
    "`x`, an angle in radians, within one unit in the last place (`[Float-Transcendental]`).\u{1f}\u{1f}fn tan(T x)"
    " : T\n    in `std::math`\n\n    The tangent of `x`, an angle in radians, within one unit in the last pl"
    "ace (`[Float-Transcendental]`).\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::math\u{1f}asin\u{1f}built in fn\u{1f}fn asin(T x) : T\u{1f}The arc sine of `x`, i"
    "n radians in `[-π/2, π/2]`, within one unit in the last place (`[Float-Transcendental]`, D-0181); "
    "a NaN for `x` outside `[-1, 1]`.\u{1f}\u{1f}fn asin(T x) : T\n    in `std::math`\n\n    The arc sine of `x`, in r"
    "adians in `[-π/2, π/2]`, within one unit in the last place\n    (`[Float-Transcendental]`, D-0181);"
    " a NaN for `x` outside `[-1, 1]`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::math\u{1f}acos\u{1f}built in fn\u{1f}fn acos(T x) : T\u{1f}The arc cosine of `x"
    "`, in radians in `[0, π]`, within one unit in the last place (`[Float-Transcendental]`, D-0181); a "
    "NaN for `x` outside `[-1, 1]`.\u{1f}\u{1f}fn acos(T x) : T\n    in `std::math`\n\n    The arc cosine of `x`, in r"
    "adians in `[0, π]`, within one unit in the last place\n    (`[Float-Transcendental]`, D-0181); a NaN"
    " for `x` outside `[-1, 1]`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::math\u{1f}atan\u{1f}built in fn\u{1f}fn atan(T x) : T\u{1f}The arc tangent of `x`, in"
    " radians in `(-π/2, π/2)`, within one unit in the last place (`[Float-Transcendental]`, D-0181).\u{1f}\u{1f}"
    "fn atan(T x) : T\n    in `std::math`\n\n    The arc tangent of `x`, in radians in `(-π/2, π/2)`, with"
    "in one unit in the last place\n    (`[Float-Transcendental]`, D-0181). For an angle from two coordina"
    "tes use `atan2`, which knows the quadrant.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::math\u{1f}atan2\u{1f}built in fn\u{1f}fn atan2(T y, T x) : T\u{1f}The "
    "angle of the point `(x, y)` from the positive x axis, in radians in `(-π, π]`, within one unit in "
    "the last place (`[Float-Transcendental-2]`); C's `atan2`.\u{1f}\u{1f}fn atan2(T y, T x) : T\n    in `std::math`"
    "\n\n    The angle of the point `(x, y)` from the positive x axis, in radians in `(-π, π]`, within on"
    "e unit in the\n    last place (`[Float-Transcendental-2]`); C's `atan2`. Both operands have the same "
    "type.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::math\u{1f}powf\u{1f}built in fn\u{1f}fn powf(T x, T y) : T\u{1f}`x` to the power `y` for floating-point ope"
    "rands, within one unit in the last place (`[Float-Transcendental-2]`); C's `pow`.\u{1f}\u{1f}fn powf(T x, T y)"
    " : T\n    in `std::math`\n\n    `x` to the power `y` for floating-point operands, within one unit in th"
    "e last place\n    (`[Float-Transcendental-2]`); C's `pow`. For an integer exponent, `pow` (an ordinar"
    "y `std::math` function)\n    is exact and checked for overflow.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}";
